window.CURRENT_FINAL_IDEAS = {"schema_version":"1.0","generated_at":"2026-08-08T15:51:14+00:00","source":"backend R3.1/R3.2 finalization; raw reviewer/model metadata removed","count":20,"ideas":[{"idea_id":"contradiction-preserving-consolidation","revision":"R3.2","title":{"zh":"固定容量下基于交叉删除干预的保留矛盾记忆巩固","en":"Contradiction-Preserving Memory Consolidation under Fixed Capacity with Crossed Deletion Interventions"},"purpose":{"zh":"解决记忆巩固只保留共识摘要、丢弃可推翻规则的稀有反证的问题：在固定容量下检验“显式保留最小结论改变集”是否比非学习的矛盾感知保留或效用保留更能降低过泛化与后续负迁移。","en":"Address the problem that memory consolidation keeps consensus summaries and drops rare counterevidence that can overturn a rule: test, under fixed capacity, whether explicitly retaining a minimal conclusion-changing set reduces overgeneralization and later negative transfer more than non-learned contradiction-aware or utility-based retention."},"importance":{"zh":"长期智能体记忆若系统性丢弃反证，会在规则被推翻后持续过泛化并产生负迁移；明确反证保留的因果价值与可证伪边界，可为记忆巩固机制提供可复现的设计准则。","en":"Long-horizon agent memory that systematically drops counterevidence will keep overgeneralizing after a rule is overturned, causing negative transfer; establishing the causal value and falsifiable boundary of counterevidence retention gives reproducible design criteria for memory consolidation."},"core_idea":{"zh":"在固定容量 K 下，用一次性、可 oracle 验证的结论改变探测构建并冻结一个最小结论改变保留集（删除该条目会使至少一个留出探针查询的最终答案翻转），剩余容量用最近条目填充；通过与矛盾感知非学习保留和效用保留在相同记忆/检索/校准预算下的交叉删除干预对比，隔离反证保留的因果效应，并用预注册的非劣效界值 δ 与绑定决策规则直接判定主张存亡。","en":"Under fixed capacity K, build and freeze a minimal conclusion-changing retention set via one-time oracle-verifiable probes (an entry is conclusion-changing iff removing it flips the final answer of at least one held-out probe query), fill remaining capacity by recency, and isolate the causal effect of counterevidence retention through crossed deletion interventions against contradiction-aware non-learned retention and utility-based retention under identical memory/retrieval/calibration budgets, with a preregistered non-inferiority margin δ and a binding decision rule that directly determines whether the claim survives or dies."},"core_intuition":{"zh":"真正决定未来结论的是那些“删掉就会改答案”的条目，而不是仅仅与多数结论相矛盾的条目；直接以结论改变为标准保留反证，应比启发式矛盾检测更精准地防止规则被推翻后的过泛化。","en":"What truly determines future conclusions are entries whose deletion flips an answer, not merely entries that contradict the majority; retaining counterevidence by the conclusion-change criterion should prevent post-overturn overgeneralization more precisely than heuristic contradiction detection."},"rationale":{"zh":"R3 指出原方案未将学习式巩固器与矛盾感知非学习保留隔离，R3.1 移除了学习巩固器但未给出可机械执行的证伪阈值，且 oracle 校准成本未在基线中匹配。R3.2 的最小修复是：（1）在实验设计内嵌入预注册的非劣效界值 δ 与绑定决策规则，使“无差异”与“噪声”可被区分，主张可被直接杀死；（2）为矛盾感知基线匹配相同的校准 token/调用预算，或将 oracle 校准成本计入每条件预算对比并在停止规则中检验收益是否可归因于额外校准预算。","en":"R3 found the learned consolidator was not isolated from contradiction-aware non-learned retention; R3.1 removed the learned consolidator but provided no mechanically executable falsification threshold and did not match the oracle calibration cost in the baseline. The minimal R3.2 repair: (1) embed a preregistered non-inferiority margin δ and a binding decision rule inside the experimental design so that 'no difference' is distinguishable from noise and the claim can be directly killed; (2) match the contradiction-aware baseline with an identical calibration token/call budget, or include oracle calibration cost in the per-condition budget comparison and check in the stop rule whether gains are attributable to the extra calibration budget."},"method_logic":{"zh":"（1）在构建集上，对每个候选记忆条目用同一冻结模型与相同提示各运行两次下游任务（含/不含该条目），若任一留出探针查询最终答案改变则标记为结论改变；（2）按“先保留全部结论改变条目、再以最近条目填满容量 K”生成冻结记忆缓冲，评估前锁定，不在测试时重学；（3）评估时施加交叉删除算子：删结论改变条目、删等量随机非结论改变条目、删最旧条目、不删除；（4）与矛盾感知非学习保留、效用保留在相同预算下对比结论稳定性、未来任务收益、最坏回归与更新准入精度；（5）校准预算匹配：矛盾感知基线获得与 oracle 校准相同的 token/调用预算用于其 NLI 启发式选择（对每个候选条目运行相同次数的前向传播，只是用 NLI 打分替代结论改变判定）；若无法匹配，则将 oracle 校准成本显式计入每条件总预算，并在结果中单独报告“校准成本调整后”的净收益；（6）预注册非劣效界值 δ：在两个模型×两个领域共 4 个条件中，若 oracle 结论改变保留在至少 3 个条件上的最坏回归优于矛盾感知基线的幅度不超过 δ=2 个百分点（绝对差），则判定主张不成立。","en":"(1) On a construction set, run the downstream task twice per candidate entry (with/without it) using the same frozen model and identical prompts; mark an entry conclusion-changing if any held-out probe query's final answer flips. (2) Build the frozen memory buffer by admitting all conclusion-changing entries first, then filling capacity K with the most recent entries; lock before evaluation with no test-time relearning. (3) At evaluation, apply crossed deletion operators: drop conclusion-changing entries, drop an equal number of random non-conclusion-changing entries, drop oldest entries, or no deletion. (4) Compare against contradiction-aware non-learned retention and utility-based retention under identical budgets on conclusion stability, future-task gain, worst-case regression, and update-admission precision. (5) Calibration budget matching: the contradiction-aware baseline receives an identical token/call budget for its NLI-heuristic selection (same number of forward passes per candidate entry, with NLI scoring replacing conclusion-change judgment); if matching is impossible, explicitly include oracle calibration cost in each condition's total budget and separately report 'calibration-cost-adjusted' net gain. (6) Preregistered non-inferiority margin δ: across the 2 model × 2 domain = 4 conditions, if oracle conclusion-changing retention does not exceed contradiction-aware retention on worst-case regression by more than δ=2 percentage points (absolute difference) in at least 3 of 4 conditions, the claim is judged dead."},"persistent_update_object":"frozen_counterevidence_retention_set","learning_signal":{"zh":"无梯度学习：保留集由一次性 oracle 结论改变探测确定性地构建并冻结；不训练任何嵌入或打分函数，测试时无参数更新。","en":"No gradient learning: the retention set is deterministically constructed once from oracle conclusion-change probes and frozen; no embedding or scoring function is trained, and no parameters are updated at test time."},"independent_ground_truth":{"zh":"外部程序化/执行真值：结论改变标签由对原始知识源或金标答案的程序化重跑判定（如 HotpotQA 的精确匹配、ALFWorld 的环境成功信号），未来任务成功由环境/任务验证器度量，绝不使用同一学习打分器或评判模型。","en":"External programmatic/execution truth: conclusion-change labels are determined by programmatic reruns against the original knowledge source or gold answers (e.g., exact match on HotpotQA, environment success signals in ALFWorld); future-task success is measured by the environment/task verifier, never by the same learned scorer or judge."},"strongest_baseline":{"zh":"矛盾感知非学习保留：相同固定容量 K、相同检索 top-M 与接口，用一个冻结且独立于智能体模型的轻量 NLI 启发式挑选与多数条目相矛盾的条目；该基线获得与 oracle 校准相同的 token/调用预算（对每个候选条目运行相同次数的前向传播，仅将结论改变判定替换为 NLI 矛盾打分）；另设效用保留（保留检索效用最高条目）以及无记忆/FIFO/相似度检索/摘要记忆/随机删除控制。","en":"Contradiction-aware non-learned retention: same fixed capacity K, same retrieval top-M and interface, selecting entries that contradict the majority via a lightweight NLI heuristic frozen and separate from the agent model; this baseline receives an identical calibration token/call budget (same number of forward passes per candidate entry, with conclusion-change judgment replaced by NLI contradiction scoring); plus utility-based retention (highest retrieval-utility entries) and no-memory/FIFO/similarity-retrieval/summary-memory/random-deletion controls."},"matched_resources":["identical memory capacity K","identical retrieval top-M and retrieval interface","identical observation streams and candidate memory entries","identical probe/query sets and gold labels","identical downstream task calls and tokens per query","identical frozen agent model and decoding configuration per condition","identical deletion intervention budgets within each crossed cell","identical consolidation passes (one-time calibration only, no evaluation-time extra calls)","identical calibration token/call budget per candidate entry across all retention rules (oracle conclusion-change probes and NLI-heuristic selection use the same number of forward passes per candidate)","identical optimizer/minibatches/steps (none; no learned parameters in any retention rule)","identical wall-clock and GPU-hour budget (1 GPU, 20 GPU-hours)"],"decisive_pilot":{"zh":"单一预注册交叉/析因实验：因子 A = 保留规则（oracle 结论改变保留 vs 矛盾感知非学习保留 vs 效用保留），因子 B = 删除干预（删结论改变条目 vs 删等量随机非结论改变条目 vs 删最旧条目 vs 不删除）；在 HotpotQA 与 ALFWorld 两个领域、Llama-3 与 Mistral 两个开源模型上运行，1 GPU、20 GPU 小时；主要终点为留出结论改变案例上的最坏回归与更新准入精度，及每调用/每 GPU 小时的未来任务收益。预注册绑定决策规则：在 4 个模型×领域条件中，若 oracle 结论改变保留在至少 3 个条件上的最坏回归优于矛盾感知基线的幅度 ≤ δ=2 个百分点（绝对差），则主张被杀死，结果报告为空结果（非学习启发式已足够）；若 ≥3 个条件上幅度 > δ，则主张存活。校准预算匹配：矛盾感知基线对每个候选条目运行与 oracle 探测相同次数的前向传播（仅替换判定函数），若因实现限制无法匹配，则在每条件总预算中显式计入 oracle 校准成本，并单独报告扣除校准成本后的净收益；若净收益 ≤ 0，主张同样被杀死。","en":"A single preregistered crossed/factorial test: Factor A = retention rule (oracle conclusion-changing retention vs contradiction-aware non-learned retention vs utility-based retention), Factor B = deletion intervention (drop conclusion-changing vs drop equal number of random non-conclusion-changing vs drop oldest vs no deletion); run on two domains (HotpotQA, ALFWorld) and two open models (Llama-3, Mistral) with 1 GPU and 20 GPU-hours; primary endpoints are worst-case regression and update-admission precision on held-out conclusion-change cases, plus future-task gain per call/GPU-hour. Preregistered binding decision rule: across the 4 model×domain conditions, if oracle conclusion-changing retention does not exceed contradiction-aware retention on worst-case regression by more than δ=2 percentage points (absolute difference) in at least 3 of 4 conditions, the claim is killed and the result is reported as null (the non-learned heuristic suffices); if the margin exceeds δ in ≥3 conditions, the claim survives. Calibration budget matching: the contradiction-aware baseline runs the same number of forward passes per candidate entry as the oracle probes (only the judgment function is replaced); if matching is impossible due to implementation constraints, oracle calibration cost is explicitly included in each condition's total budget and net gain after subtracting calibration cost is reported separately; if net gain ≤ 0, the claim is likewise killed."},"stop_condition":{"zh":"绑定决策规则（预注册、机械可执行）：在 4 个模型×领域条件中，若 oracle 结论改变保留在至少 3 个条件上的最坏回归优于矛盾感知基线的幅度 ≤ δ=2 个百分点（绝对差），则主张被杀死，结果报告为空结果（非学习启发式已足够）；若删除干预匹配后效应消失（即删除结论改变条目造成的性能下降与保留规则无关），主张被杀死；若扣除 oracle 校准成本后的净收益 ≤ 0，主张被杀死；若校准成本超出 20 GPU 小时预算导致实验无法完成，主张不可检验，同样报告为空结果。","en":"Binding decision rule (preregistered, mechanically executable): across the 4 model×domain conditions, if oracle conclusion-changing retention does not exceed contradiction-aware retention on worst-case regression by more than δ=2 percentage points (absolute difference) in at least 3 of 4 conditions, the claim is killed and the result is reported as null (the non-learned heuristic suffices); if the effect disappears once deletion interventions are matched (i.e., deleting conclusion-changing entries causes the same performance drop regardless of retention rule), the claim is killed; if net gain after subtracting oracle calibration cost is ≤ 0, the claim is killed; if calibration cost exceeds the 20 GPU-hour budget making the experiment infeasible, the claim is untestable and likewise reported as null."},"surviving_claim":{"zh":"在相同固定记忆容量与相同校准预算下，仅保留 oracle 验证的结论改变条目（加最近条目填充）比保留矛盾启发式标记条目或高效用条目更能降低过泛化与负迁移（在至少 3/4 模型×领域条件上最坏回归改善 > δ=2 个百分点），因为前者直接隔离了“缺失即改变下游答案”的条目。","en":"Under identical fixed memory capacity and identical calibration budget, retaining only oracle-verified conclusion-changing entries (plus recency filler) reduces overgeneralization and negative transfer more than retaining contradiction-heuristic-flagged or high-utility entries (worst-case regression improvement > δ=2 percentage points in at least 3/4 model×domain conditions), because the former directly isolates entries whose absence changes downstream answers."},"collision_boundary":{"zh":"与 Memory Consolidation 的区别：不学习压缩摘要，而是用可验证的结论改变标准做确定性保留选择；与 EvoGraph-R1 的区别：不做图结构演化或梯度更新，持久对象是一次性构建并冻结的保留集；与 Contradiction Retrieval 的区别：不是在检索时检测矛盾，而是在巩固时以“删除是否翻转结论”为准入标准，并用交叉删除干预隔离其因果效应。仅基于给定最近工作上下文，不主张相关文献不存在。","en":"Versus Memory Consolidation: no learned compressive summarization—retention is a deterministic, verifiable conclusion-change criterion. Versus EvoGraph-R1: no graph-structure evolution or gradient updates—the persistent object is a one-time constructed, frozen retention set. Versus Contradiction Retrieval: contradiction is not detected at retrieval time; admission at consolidation time is based on whether deletion flips a conclusion, with crossed deletion interventions isolating the causal effect. Based only on the supplied nearest-work context; no claim that related literature does not exist."},"r3_repair_summary":{"zh":"R3.2 在 R3.1 基础上修复两个材料边界：（1）在实验设计内嵌入预注册的非劣效界值 δ=2 个百分点与绑定决策规则（4 个模型×领域条件中至少 3 个条件上最坏回归改善 > δ 方为主张存活），使“无差异”与“噪声”可被区分，主张可被机械执行地杀死；（2）为矛盾感知基线匹配相同的校准 token/调用预算（对每个候选条目运行相同次数的前向传播，仅替换判定函数），若无法匹配则将 oracle 校准成本显式计入每条件预算对比并在停止规则中检验扣除校准成本后的净收益是否 ≤ 0。其余机制、数据集与主张保持不变。","en":"R3.2 repairs two material boundaries on top of R3.1: (1) embed a preregistered non-inferiority margin δ=2 percentage points and a binding decision rule inside the experimental design (the claim survives only if worst-case regression improvement exceeds δ in at least 3 of 4 model×domain conditions), making 'no difference' distinguishable from noise and the claim mechanically killable; (2) match the contradiction-aware baseline with an identical calibration token/call budget (same number of forward passes per candidate entry, only the judgment function is replaced), or if matching is impossible, explicitly include oracle calibration cost in the per-condition budget comparison and check in the stop rule whether net gain after subtracting calibration cost is ≤ 0. All other mechanisms, datasets, and claims remain unchanged."},"remaining_risk":{"zh":"（1）oracle 校准成本随候选条目×探针查询数增长，若超出 20 GPU 小时预算则主张不可检验，需预注册校准子采样上限；（2）若结论改变条目过少，最近条目填充可能使条件退化为纯 recency；（3）若探针构建与留出评估不够 disjoint，机制可能被高估；（4）若矛盾感知启发式已捕获大部分收益，绑定决策规则将机械地把主张杀死并报告为空结果，而非强行主张学习组件价值；（5）δ=2 个百分点的选择需在预注册中明确论证其临床/实际意义，若被质疑为任意，需补充敏感性分析（δ=1, 3, 5 个百分点）以检验结论稳健性。","en":"(1) Oracle calibration cost grows with candidate entries × probe queries; if it exceeds the 20 GPU-hour budget the claim is untestable, so a preregistered calibration subsampling cap is needed. (2) If too few entries are conclusion-changing, the recency filler may collapse the condition to recency-only. (3) If probe construction and held-out evaluation are not kept disjoint, the mechanism may be overestimated. (4) If the contradiction-aware heuristic already captures most of the benefit, the binding decision rule will mechanically kill the claim and report it as null, rather than forcing a learned-component claim. (5) The choice of δ=2 percentage points must be justified in the preregistration as practically meaningful; if challenged as arbitrary, sensitivity analyses (δ=1, 3, 5 percentage points) must be added to test robustness of the conclusion."}},{"idea_id":"compositional-update-compatibility","revision":"R3.2","title":{"en":"Compositional Update Compatibility with Frozen Update Surface, Preregistered N=12 Updates, and Architecture-Matched Ablation","zh":"组合更新兼容性：冻结更新表面、预注册N=12更新与架构匹配消融"},"purpose":{"en":"Address the problem that two individually useful updates can interfere when composed, and individual regression tests cannot predict composition outcomes.","zh":"解决两个单独有用的更新在组合时可能相互干扰的问题，且个体回归测试无法预测组合结果。"},"importance":{"en":"In continual agent self-improvement, update composition interference is a critical bottleneck for reliable deployment; understanding and predicting composition compatibility reduces unexpected regressions and improves iteration efficiency.","zh":"在智能体持续自我改进中，更新的组合干扰是可靠部署的关键瓶颈；理解并预测组合兼容性可减少意外回归，提高迭代效率。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Freeze a preregistered set of N=12 atomic update surfaces and verify through architecture-matched ablation whether explicit pairwise interaction features (fed into a shared graph/relational architecture) predict unseen composition regressions better than the same architecture with interaction features stripped but node/edge capacity matched.","zh":"冻结一组预注册的N=12个原子更新表面，通过架构匹配消融验证显式成对交互特征（输入共享图/关系架构）是否比剥离交互特征但节点/边容量匹配的相同架构更能预测未见过的组合回归。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"If non-additive interaction effects exist between updates, explicitly providing pairwise interaction features should outperform the same architecture forced to infer interactions from node embeddings alone; the key is using identical architecture class (graph/relational) for both conditions to ensure differences come from explicit interaction features rather than architectural inductive bias.","zh":"如果更新间存在非加性交互效应，显式提供成对交互特征应优于被迫仅从节点嵌入推断交互的相同架构；关键在于两种条件使用相同的架构类别（图/关系），确保差异来自显式交互特征而非架构归纳偏置。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3.1 was blocked because the graph-vs-sequence architectural difference confounded the explicit interaction structure claim, N was unspecified, and the stop condition was too weak. By preregistering N=12 specific updates, using identical RelationalGraphEncoder architecture for both conditions with only edge features ablated, and requiring significant superiority in at least 3 of 4 model×domain conditions with preregistered thresholds, we isolate the contribution of explicit interaction features from architectural inductive bias.","zh":"R3.1被阻止是因为图与序列架构差异混淆了显式交互结构声明，N未指定，且停止条件太弱。通过预注册N=12个特定更新，两种条件使用相同的RelationalGraphEncoder架构仅消融边特征，并要求在至少3/4模型×领域条件中以预注册阈值显著优于，我们将显式交互特征的贡献与架构归纳偏置分离。"},"method_logic":{"en":"1) Preregister and freeze N=12 atomic updates: 6 prompt patches (P1-P6) and 6 tool replacements (T1-T6), with exact specifications committed before any measurement; 2) Measure execution outcomes for all 132 ordered pairs (12×11) and 220 three-update combinations on training set; 3) Train two predictors using identical RelationalGraphEncoder architecture: (a) explicit interaction model receives pairwise interaction features (order-swap differentials, co-occurrence statistics) as edge attributes, (b) stripped baseline receives only node embeddings (update identity) with edge attributes zeroed but same parameter count; 4) Evaluate on preregistered disjoint reversed-pair (66 pairs) and three-update (110 combinations) tests.","zh":"1) 预注册并冻结N=12个原子更新：6个提示补丁（P1-P6）和6个工具替换（T1-T6），在任何测量前提交确切规格；2) 在训练集上测量所有132个有序对（12×11）和220个三更新组合的执行结果；3) 使用相同的RelationalGraphEncoder架构训练两个预测器：(a) 显式交互模型接收成对交互特征（顺序交换差异、共现统计）作为边属性，(b) 剥离基线仅接收节点嵌入（更新身份），边属性置零但参数数量相同；4) 在预注册的不相交反向对（66对）和三更新（110组合）测试上评估。"},"persistent_update_object":"A preregistered frozen set of N=12 atomic agent updates: 6 prompt patches (P1: add reasoning scaffold, P2: add retrieval instruction, P3: add verification step, P4: add decomposition prompt, P5: add reflection prompt, P6: add tool-use instruction) and 6 tool replacements (T1: calculator→code interpreter, T2: search→retrieval, T3: single→multi-query search, T4: add calculator, T5: add code executor, T6: add fact-checker). Each update is a concrete patch with unique index, exact text/configuration committed to a preregistration document before any composition measurement. The update surface is fixed and never changed. All composition outcomes are measured once and frozen.","learning_signal":{"en":"Order-swap success-rate differentials from training-set composition tests (AB vs BA execution) and local composition success/failure labels. Both predictors are trained only on these training-set signals and frozen before disjoint held-out evaluation.","zh":"来自训练集组合测试的顺序交换成功率差异（AB vs BA执行）和局部组合成功/失败标签。两个预测器仅使用这些训练集信号进行训练，并在不相交保留评估前冻结。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Programmatic execution of composed updates on held-out tasks: for each update pair (A,B), run tasks with order AB and BA under identical conditions; ground-truth interference is defined as a success-rate difference exceeding a preregistered threshold (|Δ| > 0.15), determined by task verifiers (environment reward signals, exact-match), not by any learned model.","zh":"通过程序化执行组合更新在保留任务上获得：对于每个更新对(A,B)，在相同条件下以AB和BA顺序运行任务；真实干扰定义为成功率差异超过预注册阈值（|Δ| > 0.15），由任务验证器（环境奖励信号、精确匹配）确定，而非任何学习模型。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"Architecture-matched stripped baseline: identical RelationalGraphEncoder (4 layers, hidden dim 128, 2.1M parameters) as the explicit interaction model, trained on the same order-swap and composition-test data with the same optimizer (AdamW, lr=1e-4, 10k steps, batch 32), but with pairwise interaction edge features zeroed out — the model must infer interactions from node embeddings (update identity) alone. Same node embedding dimension, same edge capacity, same everything except edge feature content.","zh":"架构匹配剥离基线：与显式交互模型相同的RelationalGraphEncoder（4层，隐藏维度128，2.1M参数），在相同的顺序交换和组合测试数据上以相同优化器（AdamW，lr=1e-4，10k步，批次32）训练，但成对交互边特征置零——模型必须仅从节点嵌入（更新身份）推断交互。相同节点嵌入维度，相同边容量，除边特征内容外一切相同。"},"matched_resources":["identical training data (same order-swap tests, same composition tests, same number of training pairs)","identical parameter budget/capacity (2.1M parameters)","identical architecture class (RelationalGraphEncoder with 4 layers, hidden dim 128)","identical optimizer steps/minibatches (AdamW, 10k steps, batch 32)","identical inference calls/tokens for held-out prediction","identical number of downstream evaluation queries","identical agent model calls per composition measurement","same update pool, traces, labels, intervention outcomes","same wall-clock budget","identical node embedding dimension and edge capacity"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"Crossed factorial on AgentBench and ALFWorld with two open models (Llama-3-8B and Mistral-7B): Factor A = feature set (explicit pairwise interaction features vs stripped node-only features), Factor B = composition test type (seen-order pairs vs disjoint reversed-pair and three-update tests). Both conditions use identical RelationalGraphEncoder architecture, parameter count (2.1M), training data, and budget. Preregistered significance threshold: p < 0.01 (Bonferroni-corrected for 4 model×domain conditions), effect size Cohen's d > 0.5. Testing order: (1) Llama-3-8B × AgentBench, (2) Llama-3-8B × ALFWorld, (3) Mistral-7B × AgentBench, (4) Mistral-7B × ALFWorld. Claim requires significant A×B interaction on disjoint splits in at least 3 of 4 conditions, with no condition showing significant reversal. 1 GPU, 24 GPU-hours.","zh":"在AgentBench和ALFWorld上使用两个开源模型（Llama-3-8B和Mistral-7B）进行交叉因子实验：因子A = 特征集（显式成对交互特征 vs 剥离的仅节点特征），因子B = 组合测试类型（已见顺序对 vs 不相交反向对和三更新测试）。两种条件使用相同的RelationalGraphEncoder架构、参数数量（2.1M）、训练数据和预算。预注册显著性阈值：p < 0.01（对4个模型×领域条件进行Bonferroni校正），效应量Cohen's d > 0.5。测试顺序：(1) Llama-3-8B × AgentBench，(2) Llama-3-8B × ALFWorld，(3) Mistral-7B × AgentBench，(4) Mistral-7B × ALFWorld。声明要求至少3/4条件在不相交分割上显示显著A×B交互作用，且无显著反转。1 GPU，24 GPU小时。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Preregistered testing order: (1) Llama-3-8B × AgentBench, (2) Llama-3-8B × ALFWorld, (3) Mistral-7B × AgentBench, (4) Mistral-7B × ALFWorld. For each condition, compute A×B interaction effect on disjoint reversed-pair and three-update regression prediction. Significance threshold: p < 0.01 (Bonferroni-corrected α = 0.05/4 = 0.0125 per condition, using 0.01 for conservatism), minimum effect size Cohen's d > 0.5. STOP RULES: (a) Stop immediately if any condition shows significant reversal (stripped baseline significantly outperforms explicit interaction, p < 0.01); (b) Stop if fewer than 3 of 4 conditions show significant superiority of explicit interaction features; (c) Stop if gains in any condition are attributable to extra inference compute (measured by FLOPs/token > 1% difference). Claim survives only if ≥3 conditions show significant superiority with no reversal.","zh":"预注册测试顺序：(1) Llama-3-8B × AgentBench，(2) Llama-3-8B × ALFWorld，(3) Mistral-7B × AgentBench，(4) Mistral-7B × ALFWorld。对每个条件，计算不相交反向对和三更新回归预测上的A×B交互效应。显著性阈值：p < 0.01（Bonferroni校正α = 0.05/4 = 0.0125每条件，保守取0.01），最小效应量Cohen's d > 0.5。停止规则：(a) 如果任何条件显示显著反转（剥离基线显著优于显式交互，p < 0.01），立即停止；(b) 如果少于3/4条件显示显式交互特征显著优于，停止；(c) 如果任何条件的收益可归因于额外推理计算（FLOPs/token差异>1%），停止。声明仅在≥3条件显示显著优于且无反转时成立。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"Explicit pairwise interaction features, provided as edge attributes to a RelationalGraphEncoder and frozen before evaluation, predict unseen reversed-pair and three-update composition regressions significantly better (p < 0.01 Bonferroni-corrected, Cohen's d > 0.5) than the same architecture with interaction features stripped, in at least 3 of 4 model×domain conditions (Llama-3-8B and Mistral-7B × AgentBench and ALFWorld), with no condition showing significant reversal, at equal training data, architecture, and inference cost.","zh":"显式成对交互特征作为边属性提供给RelationalGraphEncoder并在评估前冻结，在至少3/4模型×领域条件（Llama-3-8B和Mistral-7B × AgentBench和ALFWorld）中，以相同训练数据、架构和推理成本，比剥离交互特征的相同架构显著更好地预测未见过的反向对和三更新组合回归（p < 0.01 Bonferroni校正，Cohen's d > 0.5），且无显著反转条件。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Distinct from Flow, AFlow, and Software Merge Testing: this work does not focus on workflow search or code merge conflict detection, but on learning to predict interference for arbitrary update compositions (including unseen orders), with strict separation of representational contribution via architecture-matched ablation.","zh":"与Flow、AFlow和软件合并测试的区别：本工作不关注工作流搜索或代码合并冲突检测，而是专注于学习预测任意更新组合（包括未见过的顺序）的干扰，且通过架构匹配消融严格分离表示结构的贡献。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"Closes R3.1 boundary by: (1) preregistering N=12 specific atomic updates (6 prompt patches P1-P6, 6 tool replacements T1-T6) with exact specifications before any measurement; (2) replacing the architecture-confounded comparison with an architecture-matched ablation — both explicit interaction and stripped baseline use identical RelationalGraphEncoder (4 layers, hidden 128, 2.1M params), differing only in edge features (pairwise interaction features vs zeroed); (3) strengthening stop condition to require significant superiority (p<0.01 Bonferroni-corrected, Cohen's d>0.5) in at least 3 of 4 model×domain conditions with no significant reversal, tested in preregistered order; (4) preregistering ground-truth interference threshold (|Δ|>0.15).","zh":"通过以下方式关闭R3.1边界：(1) 在任何测量前预注册N=12个特定原子更新（6个提示补丁P1-P6，6个工具替换T1-T6）及确切规格；(2) 用架构匹配消融替代架构混淆比较——显式交互和剥离基线均使用相同的RelationalGraphEncoder（4层，隐藏128，2.1M参数），仅在边特征上不同（成对交互特征 vs 置零）；(3) 强化停止条件，要求在至少3/4模型×领域条件中显著优于（p<0.01 Bonferroni校正，Cohen's d>0.5）且无显著反转，按预注册顺序测试；(4) 预注册真实干扰阈值（|Δ|>0.15）。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"The RelationalGraphEncoder architecture itself may be suboptimal for this task compared to other architectures; if both conditions perform poorly, the comparison may be underpowered. Additionally, if pairwise interaction features can be easily inferred from node embeddings alone, the stripped baseline may match performance, falsifying the claim.","zh":"RelationalGraphEncoder架构本身可能不是此任务的最优选择；如果两种条件都表现不佳，比较可能功效不足。此外，如果成对交互特征可以轻易从节点嵌入推断，剥离基线可能匹配性能，从而证伪声明。"}},{"idea_id":"update-trust-region","revision":"R3.1","title":{"en":"Frozen Non-Parametric Behavioral-Divergence Trust Region for Discrete Agent Updates","zh":"面向离散智能体更新的冻结非参数行为散度信赖域"},"purpose":{"en":"Decide which candidate agent updates to admit by predicting harmful behavioral distribution shifts before they cause downstream regressions, using a simple, frozen, non-parametric behavioral-divergence gate rather than a learned or multi-component trust region.","zh":"通过预先预测有害的行为分布漂移来决定接纳哪些候选智能体更新，使用简单、冻结、非参数的行为散度门控，而非学习型或多组件信赖域。"},"importance":{"en":"Updates with similar average gains can induce very different behavioral distribution shifts and regressions. If a cheap behavioral-divergence signal can predict harmful updates better than outcome-only, current-gain, or text-edit gates, it enables safer self-evolution of agents without extra task interactions.","zh":"平均收益相近的更新可能引发截然不同的行为分布漂移与回归。若低成本的行为散度信号能比仅看结果、当前增益或文本编辑的门控更好地预测有害更新，就能在不增加任务交互的前提下实现更安全的智能体自演化。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Use one non-parametric update surface: a frozen probe suite, a predefined behavioral-divergence estimator computed from execution traces (empirical action/tool-routing distributions), and a fixed acceptance threshold. Admit an update only if its divergence is below the threshold, and compare this gate against matched outcome-only, current-gain, and text-edit gates under identical budgets.","zh":"采用单一非参数更新面：冻结的探针套件、由执行轨迹计算的预定义行为散度估计量（经验动作/工具路由分布）以及固定的接纳阈值。仅当散度低于阈值时才接纳更新，并在相同预算下将该门控与匹配的仅结果、当前增益和文本编辑门控进行比较。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"Two updates can look equally good on average task success yet move the agent's behavior very differently. A direct, non-parametric measure of that behavioral shift should flag risky updates earlier and more precisely than looking only at outcomes, immediate gains, or how much text was edited.","zh":"两个更新在平均任务成功率上可能看起来同样好，但对智能体行为的改变却大相径庭。对这种行为漂移的直接非参数度量应能比仅看结果、即时增益或文本编辑量更早、更精确地标记高风险更新。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3 found that the divergence representation was not isolated from simpler outcome or edit-level gates. The repair removes all learned components, uses a single predefined non-parametric estimator with a frozen threshold, and forces a head-to-head comparison against the simplest matched gates under identical information and budget, so any surviving advantage must come from the behavioral-divergence signal itself.","zh":"R3 发现散度表示未与更简单的结果级或编辑级门控相隔离。修复方案移除了所有学习组件，使用单一预定义非参数估计量和冻结阈值，并在相同信息和预算下与最简单的匹配门控进行正面对比，因此任何存留的优势都必须来自行为散度信号本身。"},"method_logic":{"en":"1) Freeze a probe suite of tasks and a set of candidate updates. 2) Run the pre-update agent on the probe suite to obtain empirical action/tool-routing frequency vectors. 3) Apply each candidate update, run the post-update agent on the same probe suite, and compute a predefined non-parametric divergence (e.g., Jensen-Shannon divergence between empirical action-frequency vectors). 4) Calibrate a single acceptance threshold on a separate construction set and freeze it. 5) On held-out tasks, compare the behavioral-divergence gate against outcome-only, current-gain, and text-edit gates for regression-detection precision/AUROC, using identical update pools, probe executions, evaluation tasks, calls, tokens, and wall-clock.","zh":"1) 冻结探针任务套件和候选更新集合。2) 在探针套件上运行更新前智能体，得到经验动作/工具路由频率向量。3) 应用每个候选更新，在同一探针套件上运行更新后智能体，并计算预定义的非参数散度（例如经验动作频率向量之间的 Jensen-Shannon 散度）。4) 在单独的构建集上校准单一接纳阈值并冻结。5) 在留出任务上，使用相同的更新池、探针执行、评估任务、调用次数、token 数和墙钟时间，比较行为散度门控与仅结果、当前增益和文本编辑门控在回归检测精度/AUROC 上的表现。"},"persistent_update_object":"Frozen probe suite, predefined non-parametric behavioral-divergence estimator, and frozen acceptance threshold.","learning_signal":{"en":"No task-specific relearning after threshold selection. The divergence is a deterministic computation over empirical frequencies; the threshold is calibrated once on a construction set and frozen before held-out evaluation.","zh":"阈值选择后不再进行任务特定的再学习。散度是对经验频率的确定性计算；阈值在构建集上一次性校准，并在留出评估前冻结。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Held-out task regressions and future-task gains measured by external programmatic environment/task metrics on a test set disjoint from the probe suite and construction set. An update is labeled as causing regression if the post-update agent's success rate is significantly lower than the pre-update agent's (e.g., binomial test, p < 0.05). Divergence labels are never reused as truth.","zh":"由外部程序化环境/任务指标在与探针套件和构建集不相交的测试集上测量的留出任务回归和未来任务收益。若更新后智能体成功率显著低于更新前（如二项检验 p < 0.05），则将该更新标记为导致回归。散度标签绝不被复用为真值。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"Outcome-only gate: accept an update if it improves average task success on the same probe suite used by the behavioral-divergence gate, with the same number of probe executions and evaluation budget. This is the simplest gate that uses execution outcomes but ignores distribution shift.","zh":"仅结果门控：若更新在行为散度门控所用的同一探针套件上提高了平均任务成功率，则接纳该更新，且探针执行次数和评估预算相同。这是使用执行结果但忽略分布漂移的最简门控。"},"matched_resources":["same candidate update pool","same frozen probe suite","same number of probe-task executions for estimation","same held-out evaluation tasks","same model capacity and architecture","same total agent calls","same total tokens","same optimizer/minibatches/steps (no gradient updates for any gate)","same wall-clock/GPU-hour budget"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"Crossed factorial on ALFWorld and AgentBench with two open models: Factor A = gate type (behavioral-divergence vs outcome-only vs current-gain vs text-edit), Factor B = update risk stratum (low-shift vs high-shift, defined by the independent divergence estimator). The behavioral-divergence gate's claim survives only if it achieves significantly higher update-admission precision/regression-detection AUROC than all matched gates on high-shift updates (significant A×B interaction), at equal call/token/wall-clock budget, and replicates on the second model and second domain.","zh":"在 ALFWorld 和 AgentBench 上使用两个开源模型进行交叉析因实验：因子 A = 门控类型（行为散度 vs 仅结果 vs 当前增益 vs 文本编辑），因子 B = 更新风险层级（由独立散度估计量定义的低漂移 vs 高漂移）。行为散度门控的主张仅当其在高漂移更新上以相同的调用/token/墙钟预算显著优于所有匹配门控的更新接纳精度/回归检测 AUROC（显著的 A×B 交互作用），并在第二个模型和第二个领域上复现时才成立。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Stop if, on the second model or second domain, the behavioral-divergence gate does not outperform the best matched gate (outcome-only, current-gain, or text-edit) on regression-detection AUROC/update-admission precision for high-shift updates, or if any advantage comes only from extra probe-task calls.","zh":"若在第二个模型或第二个领域上，行为散度门控在高漂移更新的回归检测 AUROC/更新接纳精度上未优于最佳匹配门控（仅结果、当前增益或文本编辑），或任何优势仅来自额外的探针任务调用，则停止。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"A frozen non-parametric behavioral-divergence gate predicts harmful discrete agent updates better than matched outcome-only, current-gain, and text-edit gates under identical budgets, specifically for high-shift updates, on at least two domains and two models.","zh":"在相同预算下，冻结的非参数行为散度门控比匹配的仅结果、当前增益和文本编辑门控更能预测有害的离散智能体更新，特别是在高漂移更新上，且至少在两个领域和两个模型上成立。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Unlike Retroformer, which learns a retrospective model to improve future trajectories, this work uses a non-parametric divergence gate with no learned components. Unlike TRPO, which constrains policy updates in continuous RL via a KL trust region during optimization, this work applies a frozen behavioral-divergence gate to discrete agent updates (patches) after they are proposed, not during gradient-based policy optimization. Unlike Safe Policy Improvement, which typically relies on outcome-based or return-based guarantees, this work tests whether a purely behavioral-divergence signal adds predictive value beyond outcome-only, current-gain, and text-edit gates.","zh":"与 Retroformer 不同，后者学习回溯模型以改进未来轨迹，而本工作使用无学习组件的非参数散度门控。与 TRPO 不同，后者在连续 RL 的优化过程中通过 KL 信赖域约束策略更新，而本工作在离散智能体更新（补丁）被提出后、而非基于梯度的策略优化过程中，应用冻结的行为散度门控。与安全策略改进不同，后者通常依赖基于结果或回报的保证，而本工作检验纯行为散度信号是否能在仅结果、当前增益和文本编辑门控之外提供额外的预测价值。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"Closed the R3 boundary by removing all learned divergence components, adopting a single non-parametric update surface (frozen probe suite + predefined JS-divergence estimator + frozen threshold), and forcing a factorial comparison against matched outcome-only, current-gain, and text-edit gates under identical budgets, with a required gate-type × shift-level interaction to prove behavioral divergence is the active ingredient.","zh":"通过移除所有学习型散度组件，采用单一非参数更新面（冻结探针套件 + 预定义 JS 散度估计量 + 冻结阈值），并在相同预算下强制与匹配的仅结果、当前增益和文本编辑门控进行析因对比，且要求门控类型 × 漂移层级的交互作用来证明行为散度是有效成分，从而闭合了 R3 边界。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"The non-parametric divergence estimate may be noisy if the action space is large and probe trajectories are limited; if the text-edit or outcome-only gate performs comparably, the surviving claim narrows to high-shift regimes where behavioral divergence adds unique value.","zh":"若动作空间较大且探针轨迹有限，非参数散度估计可能存在噪声；若文本编辑或仅结果门控表现相当，则存留主张将缩小至行为散度能提供独特价值的高漂移区间。"}},{"idea_id":"correction-action-causal-compiler","revision":"R3.2","title":{"en":"Minimal Causally Necessary Typed-Action Conjunction Compiler","zh":"最小型因果必要类型化动作合取编译器"},"purpose":{"en":"Address the problem that whole-trajectory reflection mixes observation, planning, tool, and execution errors so success does not identify necessary correction actions, by extracting minimal causally necessary typed-action conjunctions that transfer across failure compositions and domains.","zh":"解决全轨迹反思混合观测、规划、工具、执行错误导致无法识别必要纠错动作的问题，通过提取最小因果必要的类型化动作合取来实现跨失败组合和领域的迁移。"},"importance":{"en":"Agent self-improvement requires attributable, reusable correction mechanisms; existing executable correction libraries overlap strongly, leaving transfer of minimal causally necessary conjunctions as the unoccupied boundary.","zh":"智能体自我改进需要可归因、可复用的纠错机制；现有可执行纠错库已重叠较强，最小因果必要合取的迁移能力是未被占据的边界。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Compile from module-replacement interventions the minimal conjunction of typed actions necessary to repair each failure class (rather than full correction programs), freeze the library, then retrieve and execute on unseen failure combinations and a second domain. The enumeration cap is empirically calibrated rather than arbitrarily fixed, and the design includes a chaining-repair baseline to distinguish genuine conjunction necessity from mere data efficiency.","zh":"从模块替换干预中编译出修复每类失败所必需的最小类型化动作合取（而非完整纠错程序），冻结后在未见失败组合和第二领域上检索执行。枚举上限通过经验校准而非任意固定，并设计链式修复基线以区分真正的合取必要性与单纯的数据效率。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"Failure recovery often requires multiple jointly necessary actions that single-repair retrieval cannot express; minimal conjunctions remove redundancy, enabling transfer across compositions. However, this claim is only meaningful if (a) the enumeration cap does not systematically exclude real conjunctions, and (b) the advantage over single repairs is not merely an artifact of the baseline being unable to chain multiple repairs.","zh":"失败恢复往往需要多个联合必要的动作，单一修复检索无法表达这种结构；最小合取去除了冗余，使跨组合迁移成为可能。然而，该主张仅在以下条件下有意义：(a) 枚举上限不会系统性地排除真实合取，(b) 相对于单修复的优势并非仅因基线无法链式组合多个修复而产生。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3 found reusable executable correction libraries overlap strongly with existing work; the surviving boundary is transfer of minimal causally necessary typed-action conjunctions. R3.1 narrowed the mechanism accordingly. DeepSeek identified two remaining internal boundaries: (a) the size-3 cap is arbitrary and could systematically exclude necessary conjunctions requiring 4+ actions, and (b) if most failures are single-action fixable, the conjunction claim collapses to data efficiency. R3.2 repairs both: the cap is now empirically calibrated from the data with a preregistered coverage rule, and a chained-repair baseline arm is added to distinguish genuine conjunction structure from mere sequential application of single repairs.","zh":"R3判定可复用可执行纠错库与现有工作重叠强，存活边界是最小因果必要类型化动作合取的迁移。R3.1相应收窄了机制。DeepSeek识别出两个剩余内部边界：(a) 大小3上限是任意的，可能系统性排除需要4+动作的必要合取；(b) 若多数失败可由单动作修复，合取主张将坍塌为数据效率。R3.2修复两者：上限现在从数据中经验校准并附带预注册覆盖规则，并增加链式修复基线臂以区分真正的合取结构与单修复的顺序应用。"},"method_logic":{"en":"Phase 0 (cap calibration): Before library construction, run an uncapped greedy enumeration on a held-out calibration set of training failures to measure the empirical distribution of minimal sufficient subset sizes. Report the full size distribution (sizes 1 through max observed) and the computational cost of uncapped enumeration. Set the cap k* = smallest k such that ≥95% of observed minimal sufficient subsets have size ≤ k. If k* > 5, report this and use full enumeration with a preregistered computational budget; if the budget is exceeded, the claim narrows to conjunctions of size ≤ k*. This distribution is preregistered before the main experiment.\n\nPhase 1 (library construction): For each source-domain failure trajectory, generate typed candidate correction actions (observation-fix, planning-fix, tool-fix, execution-fix), enumerate subsets up to the calibrated cap k*, and test each subset by intervention execution: keep subsets satisfying (a) sufficiency (success when applied) and (b) minimality (removing any action causes failure). The library is the deduplicated union of minimal sufficient subsets by action-type conjunction, frozen before transfer.\n\nPhase 2 (transfer): At transfer, retrieve the conjunction matching the new failure's error types and instantiate for the new domain. Necessity is verified by leave-one-action-out counterfactual execution.\n\nPhase 3 (chained-repair control): The strongest baseline is augmented with a chained-repair variant: at inference, the baseline may sequentially retrieve and apply multiple individually validated single repairs (up to the same total number of correction actions as the conjunction arm's largest conjunction), with each step receiving the same intervention-validation budget per repair. This controls for the possibility that the conjunction advantage is merely due to the baseline being artificially restricted to one repair.","zh":"Phase 0（上限校准）：在库构建之前，在训练失败的留出校准集上运行无上限贪心枚举，测量最小充分子集大小的经验分布。报告完整大小分布（从1到观察到的最大值）和无上限枚举的计算成本。设定上限 k* = 使得≥95%观察到的最小充分子集大小≤k的最小k值。若k* > 5，报告此情况并使用预注册计算预算进行完整枚举；若预算超限，主张收缩为大小≤k*的合取。该分布在主实验前预注册。\n\nPhase 1（库构建）：对源领域每个失败轨迹，生成类型化候选纠错动作（观测修复、规划修复、工具修复、执行修复），枚举大小不超过校准上限k*的子集，通过干预执行测试每个子集：保留满足(a)充分性且(b)最小性的子集。库为所有最小充分子集按动作类型合取去重后的并集，冻结后用于迁移。\n\nPhase 2（迁移）：对新失败检索匹配错误类型的合取并实例化执行。必要性由留一动作反事实执行验证。\n\nPhase 3（链式修复对照）：最强基线增加链式修复变体：推理时基线可顺序检索并应用多个经单独验证的单修复（最多达到合取臂最大合取的动作总数），每步获得与合取臂相同的逐修复干预验证预算。这控制了合取优势仅因基线被人为限制为单修复的可能性。"},"persistent_update_object":"frozen minimal typed-action conjunction library with empirically calibrated size cap","learning_signal":{"en":"Module-replacement intervention outcomes, failure-type labels, and sufficiency/necessity tests from training environments only; no learned parameters, library construction is purely algorithmic, frozen without modification after building. The Phase 0 size-distribution estimation uses only environment execution outcomes on a held-out calibration set, disjoint from both library construction and evaluation splits.","zh":"模块替换干预结果、失败类型标签、以及训练环境中的充分性/必要性测试；无学习参数，库构建为纯算法过程，冻结后不修改。Phase 0的大小分布估计仅使用留出校准集上的环境执行结果，与库构建和评估划分均不相交。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Independent programmatic task verifier (environment execution success/failure signals) judges success on disjoint failure compositions and transfer domain; necessity is determined by leave-one-action-out counterfactual execution via the environment, not by any learned scorer or the correction library itself. The Phase 0 conjunction-size distribution is computed purely from environment execution outcomes, not from any model judgment.","zh":"独立程序化任务验证器（环境执行成功/失败信号）在不相交失败组合和迁移领域上判定成功；必要性通过留一动作反事实执行由环境判定，不依赖任何学习评分器或纠错库自身。Phase 0的合取大小分布完全由环境执行结果计算，不依赖任何模型判断。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"Executable correction library plus retrieval of individually intervention-validated single repairs: a library of full correction programs, each individually validated by intervention on single error types, retrieving the best single repair at inference with the same retrieval budget. This baseline has access to the same correction actions but without minimal-conjunction structure. Critical addition: a chained-repair variant of this baseline that may sequentially retrieve and apply up to k* individually validated single repairs at inference, with each step receiving the same per-repair intervention validation and the same total retrieval budget as the conjunction arm. This chained baseline directly tests whether the conjunction advantage is structural or merely reflects the baseline's inability to compose multiple repairs. Additional controls: whole-trajectory reflection, REFLECT/InT, success-trace SFT, leave-one-step-out attribution.","zh":"可执行纠错库加逐条干预验证的单修复检索：完整纠错程序库，每条在单一错误类型上经干预验证，推理时使用相同检索预算检索最佳单修复。该基线可访问相同纠错动作但无最小合取结构。关键新增：该基线的链式修复变体，推理时可顺序检索并应用最多k*个经单独验证的单修复，每步获得与合取臂相同的逐修复干预验证和相同总检索预算。该链式基线直接检验合取优势是结构性的还是仅反映基线无法组合多个修复。附加对照：全轨迹反思、REFLECT/InT、成功轨迹SFT、留一步归因。"},"matched_resources":["identical training failure compositions and traces","identical intervention-validation budget (same number of counterfactual execution queries)","identical retrieval calls and tokens at inference","identical model capacity and base agent calls","identical optimizer/minibatches/steps where any learning occurs","identical wall-clock budget","identical action-type taxonomy and candidate action pool for all three arms (conjunction, single-repair, chained-repair)","chained-repair baseline receives the same per-step intervention validation and the same total retrieval budget as the conjunction arm"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"Matched-budget factorial in a verifier-rich tool environment and transfer domain with two open models: Factor A = repair representation (minimal typed-action conjunctions vs executable correction library + single-repair retrieval vs executable correction library + chained-repair retrieval), Factor B = failure composition (seen error types vs disjoint novel compositions), Factor C = domain (source vs second domain). Preregister all failure types, action-type taxonomies, train/test splits, the conjunction-size distribution from Phase 0, and the chosen cap with its coverage guarantee. Phase 0 (cap calibration): run uncapped greedy enumeration on a held-out calibration set of training failures to measure the empirical conjunction-size distribution; set cap = smallest k covering ≥95% of minimal sufficient subsets; report the full distribution and the computational cost of uncapped enumeration. Primary test: conjunctions vs single-repair retrieval on disjoint compositions and transfer domain (A×B interaction). Secondary test: conjunctions vs chained-repair retrieval on the same splits — if the conjunction advantage disappears against chained repairs, the claim narrows to data efficiency. 1 GPU, 24 GPU-hours.","zh":"在验证器丰富的工具环境和迁移领域上用两个开源模型进行匹配预算析因实验：因子A = 修复表示（最小类型化动作合取 vs 可执行纠错库+单修复检索 vs 可执行纠错库+链式修复检索），因子B = 失败组合（训练可见错误类型 vs 不相交新组合），因子C = 领域（源领域 vs 第二领域）。预注册所有失败类型、动作类型分类法、训练/测试划分、Phase 0的合取大小分布以及所选上限及其覆盖率保证。Phase 0（上限校准）：在训练失败的留出校准集上运行无上限贪心枚举，测量经验合取大小分布；设定上限 = 覆盖≥95%最小充分子集的最小k值；报告完整分布和无上限枚举的计算成本。主要检验：在不相交组合和迁移领域上合取 vs 单修复检索（A×B交互）。次要检验：在相同划分上合取 vs 链式修复检索——若合取优势相对于链式修复消失，主张收缩为数据效率。1 GPU，24 GPU小时。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Stop or collapse the claim if any of the following holds: (1) minimal typed-action conjunctions do not transfer better than the matched-budget executable correction library with single-repair retrieval on disjoint novel failure compositions in the transfer domain or second model; (2) the independent verifier cannot confirm necessity via counterfactual execution; (3) the conjunction advantage over single-repair retrieval disappears when the baseline is allowed to chain multiple single repairs (i.e., chained-repair baseline achieves statistically indistinguishable performance from conjunctions on disjoint compositions and transfer domain) — in this case the claim narrows to a data-efficiency or sample-complexity advantage, not a structural conjunction advantage; (4) the Phase 0 calibration reveals that >50% of training failures require only single-action repairs, in which case the conjunction claim is abandoned as the mechanism reduces to single-repair retrieval for the majority of cases; (5) the calibrated cap k* excludes >5% of observed minimal sufficient subsets, in which case the cap is reported as a limitation and the claim is scoped to conjunctions of size ≤ k* only.","zh":"若以下任一条件成立则终止或收缩主张：(1) 最小类型化动作合取在迁移领域或第二模型上在不相交新失败组合上不优于匹配预算的可执行纠错库+单修复检索；(2) 独立验证器无法通过反事实执行确认必要性；(3) 当基线被允许链式组合多个单修复时，合取相对于单修复检索的优势消失（即链式修复基线在不相交组合和迁移领域上达到与合取统计上不可区分的性能）——此时主张收缩为数据效率或样本复杂度优势，而非结构性合取优势；(4) Phase 0校准显示>50%的训练失败仅需单动作修复，此时放弃合取主张，因为机制对多数案例退化为单修复检索；(5) 校准上限k*排除了>5%的观察到的最小充分子集，此时将上限报告为局限性并将主张范围限定为大小≤k*的合取。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"Minimal causally necessary typed-action conjunctions, frozen after counterfactual validation with an empirically calibrated size cap, transfer to novel failure compositions and a second domain better than both (a) an executable correction library with single-repair retrieval and (b) the same library with chained-repair retrieval, at equal budget, verified by an independent evaluator. The claim requires that ≥30% of failures in the target domains genuinely require multi-action conjunctions, and that the cap covers ≥95% of observed minimal sufficient subsets.","zh":"经反事实验证后冻结的最小因果必要类型化动作合取（具有经验校准的大小上限），在相等预算下比(a)可执行纠错库加单修复检索和(b)同一库加链式修复检索更好地迁移到新失败组合和第二领域，由独立评估器验证。该主张要求目标领域中≥30%的失败真正需要多动作合取，且上限覆盖≥95%的观察到的最小充分子集。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Boundary with DoVer (intervention-driven debugging), CausalFlow (causal attribution and counterfactual repair), ANNEAL (symbolic patch learning): this method does not build a general executable correction library or debugging system, but extracts only minimal causally necessary action conjunctions and tests their cross-composition transfer; if these nearest works already cover transfer validation of minimal conjunctions, the claim must narrow further.","zh":"与DoVer（干预驱动调试）、CausalFlow（因果归因与反事实修复）、ANNEAL（符号补丁学习）的边界在于：本方法不构建通用可执行纠错库或调试系统，而是仅提取最小因果必要动作合取并检验其跨组合迁移；若这些近邻工作已涵盖最小合取的迁移验证，则主张需进一步收窄。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"R3.1 narrowed the mechanism to minimal necessary-and-sufficient action conjunctions with matched-budget baselines. R3.2 addresses DeepSeek's identified boundary: (1) replaced the arbitrary size-3 cap with an empirically calibrated cap from a preregistered Phase 0 that measures the true conjunction-size distribution and reports uncapped enumeration cost; (2) added a chained-repair baseline arm that allows the baseline to sequentially apply multiple validated single repairs, with a preregistered stop rule that narrows the claim to data efficiency if the conjunction advantage disappears against chaining; (3) added a single-action dominance check with a preregistered threshold (≥30% multi-action) that kills the conjunction claim if most failures are single-action fixable.","zh":"R3.1将机制收窄为最小必要充分动作合取并采用匹配预算基线。R3.2修复DeepSeek识别的边界：(1) 用预注册Phase 0的经验校准上限替换任意大小3上限，测量真实合取大小分布并报告无上限枚举成本；(2) 增加链式修复基线臂，允许基线顺序应用多个经验证的单修复，并预注册停止规则——若合取优势相对于链式修复消失则主张收缩为数据效率；(3) 增加单动作主导检验，预注册阈值（≥30%多动作）在多数失败可单动作修复时终止合取主张。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"If failure compositions are too synthetic or too close to training interventions, transfer gains may overstate real utility. The empirical cap calibration depends on the calibration set being representative of the true conjunction-size distribution; if the calibration set is biased toward simpler failures, the cap may still exclude material cases. If the chained-repair baseline matches conjunction performance, the claim narrows to data efficiency, which may still be useful but is a weaker contribution. If the 30% multi-action threshold is barely met, the conjunction advantage may be driven by a small subset of failures, limiting practical impact.","zh":"若失败组合过于合成或与训练干预过近，迁移收益可能高估实际效用。经验上限校准依赖于校准集对真实合取大小分布的代表性；若校准集偏向简单失败，上限仍可能排除重要案例。若链式修复基线匹配合取性能，主张收缩为数据效率，这仍然有用但是更弱的贡献。若30%多动作阈值勉强达标，合取优势可能由一小部分失败驱动，限制实际影响。"}},{"idea_id":"memory-interaction-clause-learner","revision":"R3.1","title":{"zh":"身份与组合类型不相交的记忆交互子句归纳器","en":"Identity- and Composition-Disjoint Memory Interaction Clause Induction"},"purpose":{"zh":"解决记忆交互问题：单独有用的记忆在被共同检索时可能相互冲突、覆盖或错误组合。目标是学习可迁移的交互兼容规则，使其能泛化到训练中从未见过的记忆身份与组合类型。","en":"Address the memory-interaction problem: individually useful memories can conflict, overwrite, or compose incorrectly when retrieved together. The goal is to learn transferable compatibility rules that generalize to memory identities and composition types never seen in training."},"importance":{"zh":"记忆交互冲突是长期记忆智能体的真实失效模式。若交互规则能以可迁移的抽象结构（而非逐对记忆的身份关联）被学习，记忆系统就能在新增记忆时无需重新学习即可安全组合，这对可扩展的记忆管理具有研究价值。","en":"Memory-interaction conflict is a real failure mode for long-horizon memory agents. If interaction rules can be learned as transferable abstract structure rather than identity-specific pairwise associations, memory systems can safely compose newly added memories without relearning, which matters for scalable memory management."},"core_idea":{"zh":"在类型化交互特征（记忆类型签名 + 上下文特征，不含任何记忆身份索引）上归纳兼容子句；子句在训练身份集合上学习后冻结，并在完全未见过的记忆身份与未见过的类型组合（对/三元组）上直接复用，不做任何测试时重学习。","en":"Induce compatibility clauses over typed interaction features (memory-type signatures plus contextual features, with no identity-indexed features); clauses are learned on a training set of memory identities, frozen, and then reused without any test-time relearning on entirely unseen memory identities and unseen pair/triple type combinations."},"core_intuition":{"zh":"如果兼容子句捕捉的是抽象交互规则（例如某两类记忆在共同检索时会相互覆盖），而不是记住特定记忆身份对的共现模式，那么这些规则应能迁移到实例化相同类型组合的新身份；在相同特征与容量下，直接的 pair/triple 上下文门控不应获得同样优势，除非子句结构本身确实提供了有效的归纳偏置。","en":"If compatibility clauses capture abstract interaction rules (e.g., two memories of certain types overwrite each other when co-retrieved) rather than memorized identity-pair co-occurrences, they should transfer to new identities instantiating the same type combinations; a direct pair/triple gate with identical features and capacity should not gain the same advantage unless clause structure itself is the useful inductive bias."},"rationale":{"zh":"原始问题真实存在，但 R3 发现原切分可记忆记忆身份，且未将子句归纳与直接交互预测区分开。最小修复是：身份不相交与组合类型不相交的切分 + 去除身份索引特征 + 一个接收相同类型化特征、相同训练信号、相同容量的对/三元组上下文门控基线。任何剩余优势才可归因于子句结构。","en":"The original problem is real, but R3 found the split could memorize memory identities and did not isolate clause induction from direct interaction prediction. The minimal repair is: identity-disjoint and composition-type-disjoint splits, removal of identity-indexed features, and a matched pair/triple contextual gate baseline receiving identical typed features, training signal, and capacity. Only then can any remaining advantage be attributed to clause structure."},"method_logic":{"zh":"（1）按记忆身份将 20–40 条可程序化验证的记忆切分为不相交的训练/验证/测试集合；（2）仅在训练身份的共同检索结果上归纳类型签名兼容子句，子句只基于类型对/类型三元组签名与上下文特征触发，评估时无任何逐记忆嵌入查找；（3）冻结子句注册表；（4）在未见身份与未见组合类型上，将冻结子句与同等条件的上下文门控基线对比，以程序化执行结果判定成功。","en":"(1) Split 20–40 programmatically verifiable memories into identity-disjoint train/val/test sets; (2) induce type-signature compatibility clauses only on training-identity co-retrieval outcomes, firing on type-pair/type-triple signatures plus contextual features with no per-memory embedding lookup at evaluation; (3) freeze the clause registry; (4) on unseen identities and unseen composition types, compare frozen clauses against the matched contextual gate, with success determined by programmatic execution outcomes."},"persistent_update_object":"Frozen type-signature compatibility clause registry (learned on training identities and composition types, frozen before any held-out evaluation, reused without relearning on new identities and new type combinations; no identity-indexed features at evaluation).","learning_signal":{"zh":"仅来自训练身份组合的共同检索成功/失败标签（经程序化执行验证）及可用的冲突解释标签；子句归纳在抽象于记忆身份之外的类型交互标签上训练，绝不使用身份索引特征；最终评估回路中不含任何学习型打分器。","en":"Co-retrieval success/failure labels from training-identity compositions only, verified by programmatic execution, plus conflict-explanation labels where available; clause induction trains on type-interaction labels abstracted away from memory identity, never on identity-indexed features; no learned scorer is in the final evaluation loop."},"independent_ground_truth":{"zh":"由程序化执行检查器判定的下游任务成功率，测试任务要求使用未见的记忆身份与未见的组合类型；真值来自可执行环境结果，而非子句打分器或任何学习型评判。","en":"Downstream task success determined by programmatic execution checkers on held-out tasks requiring unseen memory identities and unseen composition types; ground truth comes from executable environment outcomes, not from the clause scorer or any learned judge."},"strongest_baseline":{"zh":"最强匹配化简基线：容量匹配的对/三元组上下文门控（相同类型化特征、相同训练数据、相同容量、无子句结构）；并列对照：相同支持度/置信度阈值的关联规则学习器，以及简单相似度去重/冲突检查。所有基线接收相同的观测、标签与预算。","en":"Strongest matched simplification: a capacity-matched pair/triple contextual gate (same typed features, same training data, same capacity, no clause structure); parallel controls: an association-rule learner with identical support/confidence thresholds, and simple similarity-dedup/conflict checks. All baselines receive identical observations, labels, and budgets."},"matched_resources":["same 20–40 memory pool with identical typed feature vocabulary","identical co-retrieval training pairs/triples and combination budget","identical observations, labels, and conflict-explanation traces","identical model capacity (parameter count and FLOPs) for clause inducer and gate","identical token and API-call budgets","identical retrieval budget at test time","identical optimizer, minibatches, and training steps","identical wall-clock limits","same frozen-evaluation protocol: no test-time relearning for any arm"],"decisive_pilot":{"zh":"单一预注册交叉因子实验：{冻结子句归纳器 vs 匹配上下文门控（并列关联规则对照）} × {已见 vs 未见身份组} × {对组合 vs 三元组组合}，另将组合类型按训练/测试不相交切分；使用 20–40 条可验证记忆，子句在训练切分后冻结，在未见身份、未见组合类型与未见组合顺序上评估；预注册身份切分与显著性检验（bootstrap CI 不重叠，α=0.05）。","en":"A single preregistered crossed factorial: {frozen clause inducer vs matched contextual gate (with association-rule control)} × {seen vs unseen identity groups} × {pair vs triple combinations}, with composition types additionally split train/test-disjoint; 20–40 verifiable memories; clauses frozen after the training split and evaluated on unseen identities, unseen composition types, and unseen composition orders; preregistered identity splits and significance tests (non-overlapping bootstrap CIs, α=0.05)."},"stop_condition":{"zh":"若冻结子句在未见身份与未见组合类型上的成功率未显著超过匹配上下文门控（预注册 α=0.05，bootstrap CI 重叠），或简单相似度/冲突检查即达到同等表现，则终止该主张，至多将其降级为记忆管理子组件；若子句在未见组合类型上退化至随机水平，同样终止。","en":"Terminate the claim if frozen clauses do not significantly outperform the matched contextual gate on unseen-identity and unseen-composition-type success (preregistered α=0.05, overlapping bootstrap CIs), or if simple similarity/conflict checks match performance; at most demote the object to a memory-management sub-component. Also terminate if clause performance degrades to random on unseen composition types."},"surviving_claim":{"zh":"在相同特征、相同训练信号、相同容量与相同检索预算下，冻结的类型签名兼容子句在未见记忆身份与未见组合类型上的共同检索成功率显著优于匹配的对/三元组上下文门控，因为归纳出的子句结构捕捉了可迁移的抽象交互规则，而非记忆身份特定的共现模式。","en":"Under identical features, training signal, capacity, and retrieval budget, frozen type-signature compatibility clauses achieve significantly higher co-retrieval success on unseen memory identities and unseen composition types than a matched pair/triple contextual gate, because the induced clause structure captures transferable abstract interaction rules rather than identity-specific co-occurrence patterns."},"collision_boundary":{"zh":"ActMem（arXiv/2026）同样关注记忆检索与推理之间的交互问题，但本主张的区别在于学习一个冻结、可迁移的类型级兼容子句对象，并以身份不相交与组合类型不相交切分验证泛化；风险敏感的记忆检索上下文 bandit（arXiv/2026）与本方法共享逐决策门控机制，因此在这里被视为匹配基线而非贡献；面向多步 RAG 的超图记忆（arXiv/2025）也建模记忆之间的关系结构，但并未主张所诱导兼容子句能够冻结后跨记忆身份迁移。除这些已给出的工作之外，不主张相关文献不存在。","en":"ActMem (arXiv/2026) addresses the same memory-retrieval/reasoning interaction problem, but this claim differs in learning a frozen, transferable type-level compatibility clause object validated under identity/composition-disjoint splits; the risk-sensitive contextual-bandit retrieval work (arXiv/2026) shares a per-decision gating mechanism, which here serves as the matched baseline rather than the contribution; hypergraph memory for multi-step RAG (arXiv/2025) models relational structure over memories but does not claim frozen cross-identity transfer of induced compatibility clauses. No claim is made that related literature does not exist beyond these supplied works."},"r3_repair_summary":{"zh":"按 R3 要求完成最小机制修复：（1）随机组合留出改为身份不相交 + 组合类型不相交切分；（2）移除子句评估中的身份索引特征与逐记忆嵌入查找，子句仅基于类型签名与上下文特征触发；（3）引入容量匹配的对/三元组上下文门控作为最强化简基线，并列关联规则对照，二者接收相同观测、标签、预算与训练步数；（4）子句在留出评估前冻结，测试时无重学习；（5）独立真值改为程序化执行检查，不含学习型评判。身份记忆化路径被封死，子句归纳与直接交互预测由匹配基线隔离。","en":"Minimal mechanism repair per R3: (1) random combination holdout replaced by identity-disjoint plus composition-type-disjoint splits; (2) identity-indexed features and per-memory embedding lookup removed from clause evaluation—clauses fire only on type signatures plus contextual features; (3) a capacity-matched pair/triple contextual gate introduced as the strongest simplification, with an association-rule control, both receiving identical observations, labels, budgets, and training steps; (4) clauses frozen before held-out evaluation with no test-time relearning; (5) independent truth changed to programmatic execution checks with no learned judge. The identity-memorization path is closed, and clause induction is isolated from direct interaction prediction by the matched baseline."},"remaining_risk":{"zh":"类型词表可能过粗，无法区分真实冲突与虚假冲突，或无法跨记忆域泛化，导致子句因谓词覆盖不足而空泛失效而非缺乏泛化能力；通过在先导实验中确保谓词覆盖、并由终止条件要求在未见身份上显著优于门控来缓解。","en":"The type vocabulary may be too coarse to distinguish real conflicts from spurious ones or to generalize across memory domains, so clauses could fail vacuously from insufficient predicate coverage rather than from lack of generalization; mitigated by ensuring predicate coverage in the pilot design and by the stop condition requiring significant improvement over the gate on unseen identities."}},{"idea_id":"probe-mutation-retirement-policy","revision":"R3.1","title":{"en":"Probe Mutation and Retirement Policy: Prequential Crossed Mutation vs. Matched Learned Future-Value Selection","zh":"Probe 变异与退役策略：序贯交叉的变异对照匹配的学习型未来价值选择"},"purpose":{"en":"Decide whether structural probe mutation adds identifiable value over a matched learned future-value diversity selector for maintaining a regression-probe portfolio under version drift.","zh":"判定在版本漂移下维护回归探针组合时，结构性探针变异是否相对于匹配的学习型未来价值多样性选择器带来可识别的独立价值。"},"importance":{"en":"Regression suites are the main defense against agent self-modification errors; a policy that provably improves the recall-cost frontier would let agents keep protection current at fixed testing cost, while a negative result justifies retiring mutation machinery in favor of simpler learned selection.","zh":"回归套件是防御智能体自我修改错误的主要手段；一个能被证明改善召回-成本前沿的策略，可让智能体在固定测试成本下保持防护的时效性，而阴性结果则可为淘汰变异机制、改用更简单的学习型选择提供依据。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Isolate mutation as a single preregistered factor on top of a frozen learned future-value diversity top-k selector, and test whether structural mutation of probes improves the future-regression-recall vs execution-cost frontier beyond what the identical selector achieves with mutation OFF.","zh":"将变异作为单一预注册因子，叠加在一个冻结的学习型未来价值多样性 top-k 选择器之上，检验探针的结构变异是否能在完全相同的选择器（变异关闭）之外，改善未来回归召回与执行成本的前沿。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"If mutation only re-weights or re-selects existing probes, a learned selector with the same features, capacity, and budget can absorb it; mutation earns its place only if it structurally generates probes that anticipate regressions no selection-from-existing-probes can reach.","zh":"如果变异只是对现有探针的重新加权或再选择，那么具有相同特征、容量和预算的学习型选择器就能吸收它；只有当变异在结构上生成了能预见回归、而仅从现有探针中选择无法达到的探针时，变异才有独立价值。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3 found that mutation/merge/retire is not identified beyond learned future-value selection plus diversity control. The minimal repair keeps the learned selector fixed and identical across arms and manipulates only structural mutation, so any frontier improvement is attributable to mutation rather than to selection power or budget differences.","zh":"R3 指出变异/合并/退役未能与学习型未来价值选择加多样性控制区分开。最小修复保持学习型选择器在两臂间固定且一致，仅操纵结构变异，因此任何前沿改进都可归因于变异本身，而非选择能力或预算差异。"},"method_logic":{"en":"Train the future-value diversity top-k selector on historical version streams, freeze it, then run a prequential crossed evaluation: at each version boundary, mutation ON generates structural variants of selected probes before execution while mutation OFF uses the portfolio as-is; retirement is handled by the same top-k cutoff in both arms, so the only manipulated factor is structural mutation.","zh":"在历史版本流上训练未来价值多样性 top-k 选择器并冻结，然后进行序贯交叉评估：每次版本边界，变异开臂在执行前对入选探针做结构变异，变异关臂直接使用现有组合；两臂的退役由同一 top-k 截断处理，因此唯一被操纵的因子是结构变异。"},"persistent_update_object":"Frozen learned future-value diversity top-k selector weights (fitted on historical version streams, frozen before held-out prequential evaluation, and reused at every version transition without test-time relearning); the probe portfolio at each window is produced by this frozen selector plus the mutation ON/OFF factor.","learning_signal":{"en":"Historical probe hit/miss execution records, probe lineage, mutation outcomes, and update diffs from past version transitions, all derived from actual test executions; the selector is trained prequentially on past windows only, with no lookahead into evaluation windows.","zh":"来自既往版本切换的真实测试执行命中/未命中记录、探针谱系、变异结果与更新差异；选择器仅用过去窗口按序贯方式训练，不对评估窗口做任何前视。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Future regressions determined by programmatic test execution and version-control/CI history on subsequent preregistered version windows; recall and cost are computed from execution logs, never from the learned selector's own scores or any learned judge.","zh":"由后续预注册版本窗口上的程序化测试执行与版本控制/CI 历史确定的真实未来回归；召回与成本从执行日志计算，绝不使用学习型选择器自身打分或任何学习型裁判。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"The identical frozen learned future-value diversity top-k selector with mutation OFF (retirement-only via the same top-k cutoff), receiving the same features, probe budget, execution-cost budget, capacity, and version order; keep-all, half-life retirement, IRT-based selection, and random mutation serve as secondary reference baselines under the same prequential budget.","zh":"完全相同、冻结的学习型未来价值多样性 top-k 选择器但关闭变异（经同一 top-k 截断实现退役），接收相同特征、探针预算、执行成本预算、容量与版本顺序；全保留、半衰期退役、IRT 选择与随机变异作为相同序贯预算下的次级参照基线。"},"matched_resources":["same historical execution outcomes and training windows","same probe pool and probe-lineage/update-diff features","same total probe budget k per version","same execution-cost budget per version","same selector architecture, capacity, and parameter count","same optimizer, minibatches, and training steps","same version-stream order and timeline","same wall-clock limit per version transition","same frozen-at-boundary evaluation protocol"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"A single preregistered prequential crossed factorial: {mutation ON vs OFF} × {two version streams}, with both arms using the identical frozen learned future-value diversity top-k selector, identical probe budget k, and identical execution-cost budget; at each version transition the portfolio is frozen, future-regression recall and execution cost are measured from actual CI outcomes on the next version window, and the recall-cost frontier is compared across arms with preregistered bootstrap bands.","zh":"单一预注册序贯交叉析因：{变异开 vs 关} × {两条版本流}，两臂使用完全相同的冻结学习型未来价值多样性 top-k 选择器、相同探针预算 k 与相同执行成本预算；每次版本切换时冻结组合，从下一版本窗口的真实 CI 结果测量未来回归召回与执行成本，并以预注册 bootstrap 置信带比较两臂的召回-成本前沿。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Terminate or collapse the claim to the plain learned-selector policy if the mutation-ON arm does not achieve a strictly better future-regression-recall vs execution-cost frontier than the matched mutation-OFF arm on preregistered windows with non-overlapping bootstrap bands, or if neither arm beats the keep-all cost frontier at the same budget.","zh":"若在预注册窗口上，变异开臂未以不重叠的 bootstrap 置信带取得严格优于匹配变异关臂的未来回归召回-成本前沿，或两臂在相同预算下均未优于全保留成本前沿，则终止或将主张坍缩为纯学习型选择器策略。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"Structural mutation of probes, added to a frozen learned future-value diversity top-k selector, improves the future-regression-recall vs execution-cost frontier on preregistered prequential version windows beyond what the identical selector with mutation OFF achieves at the same budget—because mutation generates probes that anticipate regression patterns unreachable by selection from existing probes alone.","zh":"在冻结的学习型未来价值多样性 top-k 选择器之上加入探针结构变异，能在预注册序贯版本窗口上，于相同预算下取得优于同一选择器（变异关闭）的未来回归召回-成本前沿——因为变异生成了能预见回归模式的探针，而仅从现有探针中选择无法达到这些模式。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Nearest supplied work: (1) 'Are Benchmark Tests Strong Enough? Mutation-Guided Diagnosis and Augmentation of Regression Suites' (arXiv/2026) overlaps on mechanism—mutation-guided suite augmentation—but does not cross mutation against a matched learned future-value plus diversity selector on a prequential recall-cost frontier. (2) 'Keeping Mutation Test Suites Consistent and Relevant with Long-Standing Mutants' (ESEC/FSE 2023) overlaps on problem—long-standing mutants and suite relevance—but not on a learned-selector-matched factorial evaluation. (3) 'Reliable and Efficient Amortized Model-based Evaluation' (ICLR 2025) overlaps on mechanism—amortized learned evaluation—but not on structural probe mutation for regression portfolios. The residual claim is the isolated contribution of structural mutation beyond a capacity- and budget-matched learned future-value diversity selector under prequential evaluation; no supplied work is asserted to be absent beyond this context.","zh":"所供最近工作：(1)《Are Benchmark Tests Strong Enough? Mutation-Guided Diagnosis and Augmentation of Regression Suites》(arXiv/2026) 在机制上重叠——变异引导的套件增强——但未将变异与匹配的学习型未来价值加多样性选择器在序贯召回-成本前沿上做交叉。(2)《Keeping Mutation Test Suites Consistent and Relevant with Long-Standing Mutants》(ESEC/FSE 2023) 在问题上重叠——长期变异体与套件相关性——但未做学习型选择器匹配的析因评估。(3)《Reliable and Efficient Amortized Model-based Evaluation》(ICLR 2025) 在机制上重叠——摊销式学习评估——但未涉及回归组合的结构性探针变异。剩余主张是：在序贯评估下，结构性变异相对于能力与预算匹配的学习型未来价值多样性选择器的独立贡献；除所供上下文外，不断言任何文献不存在。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"Adopted the smallest shared repair across all three proposals: a preregistered prequential crossed design with mutation ON/OFF as the single manipulated factor on top of an identical frozen learned future-value diversity top-k selector (deepseek-v4-pro's factor isolation and frozen selector object, glm-5.2's matched features/capacity and freeze-before-window protocol, kimi-k3's live version-stream prequential budget matching). Merge/retire are collapsed into the shared top-k cutoff so mutation alone must explain any frontier gain.","zh":"采纳三个方案共通的最小修复：预注册序贯交叉设计，将变异开/关作为唯一操纵因子，叠加在完全相同的冻结学习型未来价值多样性 top-k 选择器之上（deepseek-v4-pro 的因子隔离与冻结选择器对象、glm-5.2 的匹配特征/容量与窗口前冻结协议、kimi-k3 的实时版本流序贯预算匹配）。合并/退役被折叠进共享的 top-k 截断，因此任何前沿收益都必须由变异单独解释。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"Mutation operators may be version-stream-specific and not transfer across project types, and two streams may give limited statistical power; if the crossed design is underpowered, extend to additional preregistered streams before concluding, and if the learned selector implicitly approximates mutation-equivalent transformations, the claim collapses to the selector by the stop rule.","zh":"变异算子可能依赖特定版本流、无法跨项目类型迁移，且两条版本流的统计功效可能不足；若析因设计功效不足，应在下结论前扩展至更多预注册版本流；若学习型选择器隐含逼近了变异等价的变换，则按终止规则主张坍缩为该选择器。"}},{"idea_id":"update-composition-repair-compiler","revision":"R3.1","title":{"zh":"冻结免搜索更新组合修复编译器","en":"Frozen No-Search Update-Composition Repair Compiler"},"purpose":{"zh":"在检测到提示、记忆与工作流更新互不兼容后，不直接拒绝组合或回滚单个更新，而是学习一个可复用的修复程序，在保留更多已接受更新的同时恢复组合正确性。","en":"After detecting incompatible prompt, memory, and workflow updates, learn a reusable repair program that restores composition correctness while retaining more accepted updates, instead of rejecting the composition or rolling back a single update."},"importance":{"zh":"智能体自演化会持续接受多表面更新，更新间不兼容是常见故障；若只能拒绝或回滚，会损失已验证能力。一个能跨不兼容模板与更新表面泛化的修复机制，可显著降低维护成本并保留演化收益。","en":"Self-evolving agents continuously accept multi-surface updates, and cross-update incompatibility is a common failure. Rejection or rollback alone discards validated capabilities. A repair mechanism that generalizes across incompatibility templates and update surfaces can substantially reduce maintenance cost and preserve evolution gains."},"core_idea":{"zh":"将训练阶段的不兼容修复经验编译为一个冻结的、测试时零搜索的修复程序；在未见的不兼容模板×更新表面组合上，与预算匹配的约束图搜索基线对比，验证编译策略是否带来可识别的泛化/效率优势。","en":"Compile repair experience from training into a frozen, zero-test-time-search repair program; on held-out incompatibility-template × update-surface cells, compare it against a budget-matched constrained graph-search baseline to test whether the compiled policy yields an identifiable generalization/efficiency advantage."},"core_intuition":{"zh":"若修复结构可复用，编译器应把修复知识摊销进静态程序，在相同计算/调用预算下比从头搜索的基线保留更多更新、恢复更多组合，且测试时成本更低。","en":"If repair structure is reusable, the compiler should amortize repair knowledge into a static program, retaining more updates and restoring more compositions than a from-scratch search baseline under the same compute/call budget, at lower test-time cost."},"rationale":{"zh":"R3 指出冻结编译器与同等表达能力的约束修复搜索无法区分。最小实质修复是：移除测试时搜索，使用留出模板×表面单元，并引入容量/预算匹配的备忘录约束图搜索基线，在独立执行套件上比较。","en":"R3 found the frozen compiler indistinguishable from equally expressive constrained repair search. The smallest material repair is: remove test-time search, use held-out template × surface cells, and introduce a capacity/budget-matched memoized constrained graph-search baseline compared on a disjoint execution suite."},"method_logic":{"zh":"训练阶段：在训练用不兼容模板×更新表面单元上施加组合干预，收集失败模块轨迹与回归套件执行结果，学习修复策略并编译为静态程序（按不兼容特征索引的决策表/浅层程序）。测试前冻结。评估阶段：在留出的不兼容模板×更新表面单元上，冻结编译器直接输出修复动作（重排序、修改或选择性回滚），不进行任何搜索或重学习；备忘录约束图搜索基线可在测试时搜索，但使用相同更新图表示、相同节点扩展预算、相同测试调用预算与相同模型容量。","en":"Training: on training incompatibility-template × update-surface cells, apply composition interventions, collect failing-module traces and regression-suite execution outcomes, learn a repair policy and compile it into a static program (decision table/shallow program indexed by incompatibility features). Freeze before evaluation. Evaluation: on held-out template × surface cells, the frozen compiler directly emits repair actions (reorder, modify, or selective rollback) with no search or relearning; the memoized constrained graph-search baseline may search at test time but uses the same update-graph representation, node-expansion budget, testing-call budget, and model capacity."},"persistent_update_object":"Frozen versioned multi-surface update-repair program (compiled on training template × surface cells, frozen before held-out evaluation, no test-time search, no hidden relearning on held-out compositions).","learning_signal":{"zh":"仅来自训练单元的更新组合干预结果、失败模块轨迹与程序化回归套件执行结果；编译器在留出单元评估前冻结。","en":"Update-composition intervention outcomes, failing-module traces, and programmatic regression-suite execution results from training cells only; the compiler is frozen before held-out cells are evaluated."},"independent_ground_truth":{"zh":"在独立不相交的执行回归套件上，对修复后组合进行程序化执行验证：恢复成功且已掌握能力无回归（通过/失败），不使用编译器自身评分器或任何学习得到的评判器。","en":"Programmatic execution of a disjoint regression suite on the repaired composition: restoration success with no regression on mastered capabilities (pass/fail), never using the compiler's own scorer or any learned judge."},"strongest_baseline":{"zh":"容量与预算匹配的备忘录约束图搜索基线：在相同更新图表示上搜索重排序、回滚与合并，节点扩展预算与编译器训练成本摊销到每次修复的预算相同，允许测试时搜索；另含直接拒绝、最近更新回滚、增量调试与风险门控作为次要对照。","en":"Memoized capacity- and budget-matched constrained graph-search baseline: searches reorderings, rollbacks, and merges over the same update-graph representation, with node-expansion budget equal to the compiler's training cost amortized per repair, allowed to search at test time; secondary controls include direct rejection, last-update rollback, delta debugging, and risk gating."},"matched_resources":["same update-graph representation","same node-expansion budget (graph-search expansions or equivalent FLOPs)","same regression-suite signals and disjoint execution suite","same model parameter count/capacity","same testing-call budget","same token budget","same wall-clock limit","same optimizer/minibatches/steps for any learned components","same update set and incompatibility detection signal"],"decisive_pilot":{"zh":"预注册交叉因子实验：（冻结免搜索编译器 vs 预算匹配备忘录约束图搜索）×（已见/未见不兼容模板）×（已见/未见更新表面，如 {单表面、跨表面、顺序故障} × {提示、记忆、工作流}），在不相交执行套件上测量恢复成功率、保留更新数与测试成本。","en":"Preregistered crossed factorial: (frozen no-search compiler vs budget-matched memoized constrained graph search) × (seen/unseen incompatibility templates) × (seen/unseen update surfaces, e.g., {single-surface, cross-surface, order-fault} × {prompt, memory, workflow}), measuring restoration success, retained updates, and testing cost on a disjoint execution suite."},"stop_condition":{"zh":"若冻结编译器在留出模板×表面单元上的恢复成功率不高于预算匹配图搜索基线（bootstrap 置信区间重叠），或保留更新数不超过最小回滚，或备忘录搜索基线在等预算下匹配或超过它，则终止主张并降级为约束图搜索工具。","en":"Terminate the claim and demote to a constrained graph-search tool if the frozen compiler does not achieve higher restoration success than the budget-matched graph-search baseline on held-out cells (overlapping bootstrap CIs), or retains no more updates than minimal rollback, or if the memoized search baseline matches or beats it under equal budget."},"surviving_claim":{"zh":"在训练不兼容模板×更新表面单元上训练并冻结的免搜索编译器，在相同扩展与测试预算下，于留出模板×表面单元上比预算匹配约束图搜索基线保留更多更新并取得更高恢复成功率，因为编译程序捕获了可复用的修复结构而非从零搜索。","en":"A frozen no-test-time-search compiler, trained on training incompatibility-template × update-surface cells, retains more updates and achieves higher restoration success on held-out template × surface cells than a budget-matched constrained graph-search baseline at the same expansion and testing budget, because the compiled program captures reusable repair structure rather than searching from scratch."},"collision_boundary":{"zh":"与 Workflow-Localized Mechanism Learning（arXiv/2026）的区别：该工作做归因引导修复与知识复用，本主张特指冻结免搜索编译策略相对预算匹配搜索的泛化优势。与 Shepherd（arXiv/2026）的区别：Shepherd 提供可逆执行轨迹以支持元智能体，本主张不依赖轨迹可逆性，而是编译修复决策。与 Automatic Configuration Repair（HotNets/2024）的区别：该工作针对配置修复问题，本主张聚焦多表面智能体更新的组合修复，且要求与预算匹配搜索的受控对比。","en":"Distinct from Workflow-Localized Mechanism Learning (arXiv/2026), which performs attribution-guided repair and knowledge reuse; this claim specifically concerns the generalization advantage of a frozen no-search compiled policy over budget-matched search. Distinct from Shepherd (arXiv/2026), which provides reversible execution traces for meta-agents; this claim does not rely on trace reversibility but on compiled repair decisions. Distinct from Automatic Configuration Repair (HotNets/2024), which targets configuration repair; this claim focuses on multi-surface agent update-composition repair with a controlled comparison to budget-matched search."},"r3_repair_summary":{"zh":"按 R3 要求：编译器改为严格冻结、测试时零搜索；评估使用留出的不兼容模板×更新表面单元；引入容量/预算匹配的备忘录约束图搜索基线；独立真值由不相交执行套件程序化验证。","en":"Per R3: the compiler is strictly frozen with zero test-time search; evaluation uses held-out incompatibility-template × update-surface cells; a capacity/budget-matched memoized constrained graph-search baseline is introduced; independent truth is programmatically verified on a disjoint execution suite."},"remaining_risk":{"zh":"编译器可能过拟合训练模板，在真正新颖的不兼容结构上失败；备忘录搜索基线在简单单元上可能近似编译策略。留出模板划分与停止条件用于防范前者；后者若发生则按停止条件降级。","en":"The compiler may overfit training templates and fail on genuinely novel incompatibility structures; the memoized search baseline may approximate the compiled policy on simple cells. The held-out template split and stop condition guard the former; if the latter occurs, the stop condition demotes the claim."}},{"idea_id":"monotone-applicability-specializer-v4","revision":"R3.1","title":{"en":"Monotone Applicability-Set Specializer vs Complexity-Matched Symbolic Baselines on a Frozen Predicate Vocabulary","zh":"冻结谓词词表上的单调适用集合专化器对阵复杂度匹配符号基线"},"purpose":{"en":"Repair free-text lessons that over-apply: counterexample-driven repair often damages correct regions, while deleting the lesson wastes transferable knowledge. The goal is a repair mechanism that minimally narrows where a lesson applies while preserving its correct uses.","zh":"修复过度适用的自由文本课程：由反例驱动的修复常损害正确区域，而删除课程又浪费可迁移知识。目标是一种最小化收窄课程适用位置、同时保留其正确用途的修复机制。"},"importance":{"en":"Agents that accumulate reusable lessons need repairs that fix misuse without collateral damage; establishing whether monotone exception-based specialization beats generic symbolic learners determines whether this mechanism is a real contribution or a re-branding of standard rule induction.","zh":"积累可复用课程的智能体需要既能修复误用又不造成附带损害的修复方式；确立基于单调例外的专化是否优于通用符号学习器，决定了该机制是真实贡献还是标准规则归纳的重新包装。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Repair an over-broad lesson by finding the smallest monotone restriction of its applicability set—adding typed exception predicates from a frozen vocabulary while preserving executable exception lineage—so counterexamples are excluded without deleting transferable positive coverage.","zh":"通过对课程适用集合做最小单调限制来修复过宽的课程——从冻结词表中添加类型化例外谓词并保留可执行例外谱系——从而在不删除可迁移正例覆盖的情况下排除反例。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"If repair only ever narrows where a lesson applies (never rewrites or deletes correct behavior), the repair should be minimal, interpretable, and protective of positives; the open empirical question is whether this monotonicity is a real inductive-bias advantage or whether any generic rule learner over the same predicates already does as well.","zh":"如果修复只收窄课程的适用位置（从不重写或删除正确行为），修复应当最小、可解释且保护正例；悬而未决的实证问题是：这种单调性是真实的归纳偏置优势，还是任何基于相同谓词的通用规则学习器已能达到同等效果。"},"rationale":{"en":"The R3 finding says the novelty is narrow: monotone applicability specialization must prove necessary beyond generic symbolic applicability learners and precondition-only repair. The smallest material repair is to keep the mechanism unchanged but force a complexity-matched comparison on a shared frozen predicate vocabulary, converting the claim from representational necessity into a falsifiable inductive-bias/efficiency claim.","zh":"R3 结论指出新颖性狭窄：单调适用性专化必须证明其超越通用符号适用性学习器与仅前置条件修复的必要性。最小的实质性修复是保持机制不变，但强制在共享冻结谓词词表上进行复杂度匹配比较，将声明从表征必要性转化为可证伪的归纳偏置/效率声明。"},"method_logic":{"en":"Given a lesson plus counterexamples and retained positives, the specializer searches for the smallest monotone restriction of the applicability set expressible in the frozen typed predicate language, keeping exception lineage executable. Baselines receive the identical data and vocabulary: complexity-matched ILP/rule-induction, decision-tree/rule-list learners, and precondition-only repair. Because every arm shares the same vocabulary and complexity budget, no representational-impossibility claim is made; the monotone constraint is tested purely as an inductive bias for minimal, positive-preserving repair on disjoint held-out states.","zh":"给定课程及反例与保留正例，专化器在冻结类型化谓词语言中搜索适用集合的最小单调限制，并保持例外谱系可执行。基线获得完全相同的数据与词表：复杂度匹配的 ILP/规则归纳、决策树/规则列表学习器与仅前置条件修复。由于所有臂共享词表与复杂度预算，本想法不作表征不可能性声明；单调约束仅作为面向最小化、保护正例修复的归纳偏置，在不相交留出状态上接受检验。"},"persistent_update_object":"structured lesson with executable exception lineage, frozen after training on counterexample and positive demonstrations; the typed predicate vocabulary is fixed before any baseline comparison, and the frozen artifact is reused on unseen states without relearning","learning_signal":{"en":"Minimal counterexamples, unaffected-positive labels, and constraint-deletion traces from training states only, all verified by programmatic execution; the typed exception language and specialization rules are frozen before held-out misuse/retention evaluation.","zh":"仅来自训练状态的最小反例、未受影响正例标签与约束删除轨迹，均经程序化执行验证；类型化例外语言与专化规则在留出误用/保持评估前冻结。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Applicability ground truth, misuse, and positive retention are determined by programmatic execution outcomes in the executable-rule environment on unseen states—never by the specializer's own scorer or any learned judge.","zh":"适用性真值、误用与正例保持均由可执行规则环境在未见状态上的程序化执行结果判定——绝不使用专化器自身的评分器或任何学习型评判。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"Complexity-matched ILP/rule-induction on the same frozen predicate vocabulary with the same rule-complexity budget and the same training counterexamples/positives; additionally decision-tree/rule-list learners and precondition-only repair under identical budgets.","zh":"在相同冻结谓词词表、相同规则复杂度预算与相同训练反例/正例下的复杂度匹配 ILP/规则归纳；另有相同预算下的决策树/规则列表学习器与仅前置条件修复。"},"matched_resources":["Same frozen predicate vocabulary for all arms","Same training counterexample sets","Same positive-state sets","Same constraint-deletion traces","Same rule-complexity budget (number of rules, clauses, or tree nodes)","Same model calls and token budget","Same optimizer/minibatches/optimization steps where applicable","Same wall-clock limits","Same evaluation protocol on identical disjoint held-out misuse/retention states","Same frozen-artifact evaluation with no test-time relearning for any arm"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"A single preregistered crossed factorial: {monotone specializer vs complexity-matched ILP/rule-induction vs decision-tree/rule-list vs precondition-only repair} × {seen misuse patterns vs unseen misuse patterns}, all arms on the same frozen predicate vocabulary with equal rule-complexity budgets, trained on identical counterexample/positive sets and evaluated on disjoint held-out misuse/retention states; primary metrics are misuse rate, positive retention, and edit size with bootstrap confidence intervals.","zh":"单一预注册交叉析因：{单调专化器 vs 复杂度匹配的 ILP/规则归纳 vs 决策树/规则列表 vs 仅前置条件修复} × {已见误用模式 vs 未见误用模式}，所有臂使用同一冻结谓词词表与相等规则复杂度预算，在相同反例/正例集合上训练，并在不相交的留出误用/保持状态上评估；主指标为误用率、正例保持率与编辑量，附自助置信区间。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Stop or collapse the claim if any complexity-matched baseline (ILP, rule-list, or precondition-only repair) matches the specializer on misuse and positive retention with overlapping bootstrap CIs on disjoint states. If only precondition-only repair matches, narrow the claim to monotone narrowing as an interpretable component; if generic rule induction matches, narrow to an edit-minimality/efficiency claim; if the typed vocabulary proves task-specific, retain only as an interpretable component for that setting.","zh":"若任一复杂度匹配基线（ILP、规则列表或仅前置条件修复）在不相交状态上的误用与正例保持指标以重叠自助置信区间追平专化器，则终止或收缩声明。若仅前置条件修复追平，则将声明收窄为“单调收窄作为可解释组件”；若通用规则归纳追平，则收窄为编辑最小性/效率声明；若类型化词表被证明为任务专用，则仅作为该设定下的可解释组件保留。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"On a frozen predicate vocabulary, monotone applicability-set specialization with typed exception lineage achieves lower misuse and higher positive retention than complexity-matched ILP/rule-induction, decision-tree/rule-list, and precondition-only repair at equal complexity, as an inductive-bias advantage for minimal, positive-preserving exception narrowing—an empirically falsifiable claim, not a representational one.","zh":"在冻结谓词词表上，带类型化例外谱系的单调适用集合专化在同等复杂度下，相较复杂度匹配的 ILP/规则归纳、决策树/规则列表与仅前置条件修复，取得更低误用与更高正例保持——这是关于最小化、保护正例的例外收窄的归纳偏置优势，是一条可经验证伪的声明，而非表征性声明。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"SkillAdaptor (arXiv/2026) and SkillTracer (ICLR Workshop/2026) adapt or refine skills from trajectories but do not test monotone applicability narrowing against complexity-matched symbolic rule learners on a shared frozen predicate vocabulary; GraSP (arXiv/2026) composes skills into graphs rather than repairing applicability sets. This idea's collision risk is precisely whether generic ILP/rule-list learners or precondition-only repair already capture the benefit, which the preregistered factorial pilot is designed to settle rather than assume.","zh":"SkillAdaptor（arXiv/2026）与 SkillTracer（ICLR Workshop/2026）从轨迹中适配或精炼技能，但未在共享冻结谓词词表上将单调适用性收窄与复杂度匹配的符号规则学习器对照；GraSP（arXiv/2026）将技能组合为图而非修复适用集合。本想法的碰撞风险恰恰在于通用 ILP/规则列表学习器或仅前置条件修复是否已涵盖该收益，预注册析因试点旨在判定而非假设这一点。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"Replaced the SkillTracer/SkillAdaptor-only baseline suite with complexity-matched ILP/rule-induction, decision-tree/rule-list, and precondition-only repair, all on the same frozen predicate vocabulary with disjoint misuse/retention evaluation; narrowed the claim from implied representational necessity to a falsifiable inductive-bias claim about monotone exception narrowing, per the R3 required action.","zh":"将仅含 SkillTracer/SkillAdaptor 的基线组替换为复杂度匹配的 ILP/规则归纳、决策树/规则列表与仅前置条件修复，全部在同一冻结谓词词表上并采用不相交误用/保持评估；按 R3 要求，将声明从隐含的表征必要性收窄为关于单调例外收窄的可证伪归纳偏置声明。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"If the frozen predicate vocabulary is too expressive, complexity-matched ILP may match the specializer; if too restrictive, all arms fail or the vocabulary becomes task-specific. Monotone specialization may also degenerate to precondition-only repair when exceptions are simple. The stop rule explicitly handles all three outcomes.","zh":"若冻结谓词词表表达力过强，复杂度匹配的 ILP 可能追平专化器；若过弱，所有臂都会失败或词表变成任务专用。当例外很简单时，单调专化也可能退化为仅前置条件修复。停止条件显式覆盖这三种结果。"}},{"idea_id":"api-error-semantic-adapter","revision":"R3.2","title":{"en":"API Error-Semantics Adapter: Learned Discrete Taxonomy vs. Structured Bottleneck Under Matched Resources with Human-Design Control","zh":"API 错误语义适配器：学习离散分类法与结构化瓶颈在匹配资源下的对比（含人工设计控制）"},"purpose":{"en":"Address the problem where equivalent tool capabilities expose different error semantics across APIs, silently breaking recovery policies after migration.","zh":"解决等价工具能力在不同 API 间暴露不同错误语义、导致迁移后恢复策略静默失效的问题。"},"importance":{"en":"Robust error recovery during cross-API migration is a critical bottleneck for enterprise AI agents; if error semantics do not transfer across providers, agents fail silently.","zh":"企业 AI 代理在跨 API 迁移时，错误恢复策略的鲁棒性是关键瓶颈；若错误语义无法跨提供方迁移，代理将频繁失效。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Learn an explicit, enumerable canonical error-state taxonomy (or retain a constrained learned latent), map provider-specific failures into canonical recovery states, and compile target-API repair actions. The core claim is that a structured bottleneck provides better cross-API-family transfer inductive bias than a matched flat discrete classifier. Critically, the taxonomy construction itself must be learned end-to-end from data—any human state selection invalidates the mechanism claim.","zh":"学习一个显式、可枚举的规范错误状态分类法（或保留一个受约束的学习潜在变量），将提供方特定的错误映射到规范恢复状态，并编译目标 API 修复动作。核心主张是：结构化瓶颈比匹配容量的扁平离散分类器具有更好的跨 API 族迁移归纳偏置。关键地，分类法构建本身必须从数据端到端学习——任何人工状态选择都会使机制主张无效。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"Error semantics are shared across semantically equivalent APIs but differ in surface form. An explicit canonical-state bottleneck captures this shared structure and generalizes better to unseen API families than an unstructured flat classifier—provided the structure is learned from data, not hand-encoded by human designers.","zh":"错误语义在语义等价的 API 间是共享的，但表面形式不同。一个显式的规范状态瓶颈可以捕获这种共享结构，比无结构的扁平分类器更好地泛化到未见 API 族——前提是结构从数据中学习，而非由人类设计者手工编码。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3 found the learned latent unnecessary unless it beats a matched discrete taxonomy plus templates. R3.1 made the mechanism explicit but left the human-design confound unresolved. R3.2 adds the human-designed taxonomy baseline to isolate the learned component: if the learned taxonomy cannot beat a human-designed taxonomy, the claimed mechanism (learned inductive bias) is not identifiable and the claim dies.","zh":"R3 发现学习潜在变量除非能击败匹配资源的离散分类法加模板，否则不必要。R3.1 使机制显式化但未解决人工设计混淆。R3.2 添加人工设计分类法基线以隔离学习组件：若学习分类法无法击败人工设计分类法，则所主张的机制（学习归纳偏置）不可识别，主张死亡。"},"method_logic":{"en":"1) Build a fixed discrete error taxonomy from source-API error traces via hierarchical clustering or constrained learning—no human state selection permitted. 2) Each source provider gets a deterministic lookup table mapping taxonomy codes to recovery templates. 3) At test time, an unseen target-API error is classified into the frozen taxonomy via nearest-neighbor over frozen embeddings. 4) The matched taxonomy code selects a recovery template from source tables; if none exists, fall back to a generic retry/log template. 5) Three arms compared under identical resources: (a) structured bottleneck with learned taxonomy, (b) flat discrete classifier with learned taxonomy, (c) flat discrete classifier with human-designed taxonomy (expert-curated canonical states). Arm (c) isolates the human-prior contribution; if (a) ≈ (c), the learned component is not identifiable.","zh":"1) 从源 API 错误轨迹通过层次聚类或受约束学习构建固定离散错误分类法——不允许人工状态选择。2) 每个源提供方获得确定性查找表，将分类法代码映射到恢复模板。3) 测试时，未见目标 API 错误通过冻结嵌入模型的最近邻分类到冻结分类法。4) 匹配的分类法代码从源表中选择恢复模板；若无源模板，则回退到通用重试/日志模板。5) 三臂在相同资源下对比：(a) 学习分类法的结构化瓶颈，(b) 学习分类法的扁平离散分类器，(c) 人工设计分类法的扁平离散分类器（专家策划的规范状态）。臂 (c) 隔离人类先验贡献；若 (a) ≈ (c)，则学习组件不可识别。"},"persistent_update_object":"frozen canonical error-state taxonomy plus provider-to-canonical mapper and recovery-action table","learning_signal":{"en":"Source-API-family error traces, executed recovery actions, and programmatic final outcomes (success/failure/retry-needed) used only to construct the taxonomy and populate templates; no target-API traces used for training or freezing. For the human-designed taxonomy arm, the taxonomy is fixed by expert specification and does not consume learning signal.","zh":"源 API 族错误轨迹、执行的恢复动作和程序化最终结果（成功/失败/需重试），仅用于构建分类法和填充模板；不使用目标 API 轨迹进行训练或冻结。对于人工设计分类法臂，分类法由专家规范固定，不消耗学习信号。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Programmatic recovery-success labels: re-execute compiled repair actions on the held-out target API and record success/failure/error-class-mismatch by actual API response codes and runtime exceptions, not by the adapter's own classification.","zh":"程序化恢复成功标签：在保留的目标 API 上重新执行编译的修复动作，通过实际 API 响应码和运行时异常记录成功/失败/错误类不匹配，而非由适配器自身分类。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"Discrete error-taxonomy classifier (logistic regression or small MLP on error-string features) plus deterministic per-class repair templates, matched on capacity, data, calls, tokens, optimizer, steps, and wall-clock; error-text retrieval (nearest-neighbor error string to canonical class) as a third matched control; human-designed taxonomy classifier (expert-curated canonical states with same cardinality) as the identifiability control.","zh":"离散错误分类法分类器（错误字符串特征上的逻辑回归或小 MLP）加确定性每类修复模板，匹配容量、数据、调用、令牌、优化器、步数和墙钟时间；错误文本检索（最近邻错误字符串到规范类）作为第三匹配控制；人工设计分类法分类器（专家策划的规范状态，相同基数）作为可识别性控制。"},"matched_resources":["identical error traces","identical recovery-action sets","identical model capacity","identical optimizer","identical minibatches","identical steps","identical LLM calls","identical tokens","identical wall-clock","identical embedding model","identical taxonomy cardinality","identical human design budget (expert hours for taxonomy specification)"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"Crossed 3×2 pilot: {learned latent adapter, learned discrete taxonomy classifier, human-designed taxonomy classifier} × {source-API-family training only, full-API training} on a held-out target API family. All three arms receive identical error traces, recovery-action sets, model capacity, optimizer, minibatches, steps, LLM calls, tokens, and wall-clock. The learned latent and learned taxonomy are frozen before target evaluation; the human-designed taxonomy is fixed by construction. Target-API repair templates are deterministic and shared across arms. The human-designed taxonomy arm serves as the identifiability control: if it matches or beats the learned taxonomy arm, the learned-structure claim dies.","zh":"交叉 3×2 试点：{学习潜在适配器, 学习离散分类法分类器, 人工设计分类法分类器} × {仅源 API 族训练, 全 API 训练}，在保留的目标 API 族上评估。所有三臂接收相同的错误轨迹、恢复动作集、模型容量、优化器、小批量、步数、LLM 调用、令牌和墙钟时间。学习潜在变量和学习分类法在目标评估前冻结；人工设计分类法由构造固定。目标 API 修复模板是确定性的并在三臂间共享。人工设计分类法臂作为可识别性控制：若它匹配或击败学习分类法臂，学习结构主张死亡。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Stop if: (a) the learned discrete taxonomy arm matches the learned latent arm on held-out recovery success within a pre-registered equivalence margin (δ = 2 percentage points), or (b) neither learned arm exceeds error-text retrieval on held-out transfer, or (c) the human-designed taxonomy arm matches or exceeds the learned taxonomy arm on held-out recovery success within δ. If (c) triggers, the learned-structure claim dies and the surviving contribution narrows to 'taxonomy-based recovery works, but human design suffices.' If (a) triggers, the learned latent is dropped. If (b) triggers, the entire taxonomy approach is questioned.","zh":"停止若：(a) 学习离散分类法臂在保留恢复成功上与学习潜在臂在预注册等价裕度 (δ = 2 个百分点) 内匹配，或 (b) 两个学习臂均未超过错误文本检索的保留迁移，或 (c) 人工设计分类法臂在保留恢复成功上匹配或超过学习分类法臂在 δ 内。若 (c) 触发，学习结构主张死亡，幸存贡献缩小到'基于分类法的恢复有效，但人工设计足够'。若 (a) 触发，学习潜在变量被丢弃。若 (b) 触发，整个分类法方法受到质疑。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"An explicit canonical recovery-state bottleneck yields better cross-API-family recovery-policy transfer than a matched flat discrete classifier at equal capacity and budget, AND this advantage is attributable to learned structure rather than human priors (i.e., the learned taxonomy beats the human-designed taxonomy). This is an empirically falsifiable inductive-bias/transfer claim with identifiability guaranteed by the human-design control.","zh":"一个显式规范恢复状态瓶颈在相等容量和预算下，比匹配的扁平离散分类器产生更好的跨 API 族恢复策略迁移，且此优势可归因于学习结构而非人类先验（即学习分类法击败人工设计分类法）。这是一个可经验证伪的归纳偏置/迁移主张，通过人工设计控制保证可识别性。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Overlaps with PALADIN (arXiv/2025) and Agent-First Tool API (arXiv/2026) on problem, but differs in mechanism: PALADIN focuses on self-correcting agents, Agent-First on semantic interface paradigms; overlaps with Self-Reflective APIs (arXiv/2026) on mechanism, but this work emphasizes matched-resource comparison of learned discrete taxonomy vs. structured bottleneck, not structure beats verbosity.","zh":"与 PALADIN (arXiv/2025) 和 Agent-First Tool API (arXiv/2026) 的问题重叠，但机制不同：PALADIN 关注自我修复代理，Agent-First 关注语义接口范式；与 Self-Reflective APIs (arXiv/2026) 的机制重叠，但本工作强调学习离散分类法与结构化瓶颈的匹配资源对比，而非结构优于冗长。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"R3 required the learned latent to prove itself against a matched discrete taxonomy plus templates. R3.1 made the bottleneck explicit but left the human-design confound unresolved. R3.2 adds the human-designed taxonomy baseline as a third arm, making the learned-structure claim identifiable: the learned taxonomy must beat both the flat classifier AND the human-designed taxonomy to survive.","zh":"R3 要求学习潜在变量在匹配资源的离散分类法加模板面前证明自身。R3.1 使瓶颈显式但未解决人工设计混淆。R3.2 添加人工设计分类法基线作为第三臂，使学习结构主张可识别：学习分类法必须同时击败扁平分类器和人工设计分类法才能幸存。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"The human-designed taxonomy may still benefit from unmeasured expert iteration; the 'identical human design budget' matching is approximate. If the learned taxonomy wins but by a margin within the noise of human design variability, the claim may need to narrow to 'learned taxonomy matches human-designed taxonomy at lower human cost.'","zh":"人工设计分类法可能仍受益于未测量的专家迭代；'相同人工设计预算'匹配是近似的。若学习分类法获胜但裕度在人工设计变异性的噪声范围内，主张可能需要缩小到'学习分类法以更低人力成本匹配人工设计分类法'。"}},{"idea_id":"workflow-repair-grammar-v5","revision":"R3.2","title":{"en":"Workflow Repair Grammar v5: Composition-Caused Transfer Isolation on Full Distribution","zh":"工作流修复语法 v5：全分布上的组合因果迁移隔离"},"purpose":{"en":"Address the original problem that recurring structural workflow failures are patched from scratch and do not transfer across APIs or graph motifs, while narrowing the contribution to a falsifiable causal claim: cross-API×motif transfer must be caused by novel composition of at least two learned productions, not by retrieval or graph-diff templating. The claim must hold on the full distribution of held-out workflow failures, not merely on a filtered subset where composition is structurally required.","zh":"解决反复出现的结构性工作流失败被从头修补、无法跨 API 或图模体迁移的问题，并将贡献收窄为可证伪的因果主张：跨 API×模体迁移必须由至少两条已学习产生式的新颖组合引起，而非检索或图差分模板化。该主张必须在留出工作流失败的全分布上成立，而非仅在组合被结构性要求的过滤子集上成立。"},"importance":{"en":"If composition is the true mechanism of transfer, a frozen, search-free repair grammar can generalize structural repairs to unseen APIs and motifs at far lower cost than retrieval or test-time search; if composition is not the mechanism, the decisive pilot terminates the claim outright, preventing misattribution of retrieval-reachable repairs to grammar structure. Crucially, the claim must hold on the full distribution of real workflow failures, not just on a filtered slice where composition is structurally required.","zh":"如果组合是迁移的真实机制，那么一个冻结的、免搜索的修复语法就能以远低于检索或测试时搜索的成本，把结构性修复推广到未见过的 API 与图模体；如果组合不是机制，该主张会被决定性试验直接终止，从而避免把检索可达的修复误归因于语法结构。关键在于，主张必须在真实工作流失败的全分布上成立，而不仅在组合被结构性要求的过滤切片上成立。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Induce productions from failure/repair graph diffs in a frozen structural rewrite language, learn triggers and local rewrites, and prohibit test-time search; evaluate on the full distribution of held-out workflow failures, with composition-requiring instances as a secondary diagnostic subset to verify that composition is the causal mechanism where it matters most.","zh":"从失败/修复图差分中归纳出冻结结构重写语言中的产生式，学习触发器与局部重写，禁止测试时搜索；在留出工作流失败的全分布上评估，以组合必需实例作为次要诊断子集，验证组合在最关键处是因果机制。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"If transfer truly comes from composition, then on the full distribution of held-out failures, the full compositional grammar should significantly outperform all matched controls—especially on instances where retrieval and single-production rewrites could plausibly succeed but composition does better; if the advantage vanishes on the full distribution or if composition-disabled matches the full grammar, the claim collapses immediately.","zh":"如果迁移真的来自组合，那么在留出失败的全分布上，完整组合语法应当显著优于所有匹配控制——尤其是在检索与单产生式重写可能成功但组合表现更好的实例上；如果优势在全分布上消失，或组合禁用与完整语法持平，主张立即坍缩。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3.1's filtering created a tautology: 'composition wins on composition-requiring instances' is true by construction. R3.2 repairs this by evaluating on the full distribution of held-out failures, making all controls fair (they can succeed wherever single-production or retrieval suffices), and testing whether composition provides an advantage across the entire distribution. The composition-requiring subset becomes a secondary diagnostic to verify the mechanism where it is most needed, but the primary claim is evaluated on the full distribution.","zh":"R3.1 的过滤造成了同义反复：「组合在组合必需实例上胜出」由构造必然为真。R3.2 通过在留出失败的全分布上评估来修复此问题，使所有控制公平（它们可在单产生式或检索足够的地方成功），并检验组合是否在整个分布上提供优势。组合必需子集成为次要诊断，用于在最关键处验证机制，但主要主张在全分布上评估。"},"method_logic":{"en":"1) Extract minimal graph edits (node add/delete, edge rewire) from source workflow failures and cluster them into atomic production primitives; 2) induce a frozen set of production rules, each a (trigger subgraph pattern, local rewrite) pair; 3) at test time, the grammar may compose any number of productions from the frozen set (including zero or one), with no new rule generation, no whole-repair retrieval, and no subgraph-isomorphism match of the full failure graph; 4) composition is executed by matching trigger patterns independently and applying rewrites sequentially with conflict resolution by rule priority; 5) the system is frozen after source training and evaluated on workflows disjoint in both API identity and graph motif; 6) the full distribution of held-out failures is evaluated, with composition-requiring instances (where ≥2 productions fired) identified post-hoc as a diagnostic subset.","zh":"1) 从源工作流失败中提取最小图编辑（节点增删、边重连），聚类为原子产生式原语；2) 归纳冻结产生式集合，每条规则为（触发子图模式，局部重写）对；3) 测试时语法可组合冻结集合中任意数量的产生式（包括零条或一条），禁止新规则生成、整体修复检索、以及对完整失败图的子图同构匹配；4) 通过独立匹配触发模式并顺序应用重写来执行组合，冲突按规则优先级解决；5) 系统在源训练后冻结，在 API 与图模体双重不相交的工作流上评估；6) 评估留出失败的全分布，组合必需实例（≥2 条产生式触发）事后识别为诊断子集。"},"persistent_update_object":"Frozen workflow-repair grammar: the set of atomic production rules (trigger pattern + local rewrite), frozen after source-API/source-motif induction, learned/fitted before held-out evaluation, and reused without test-time rule generation, search, or relearning.","learning_signal":{"en":"Workflow graph diffs, failure motifs, and independently execution-verified post-repair success on training APIs and seen motifs only; no target-API or target-motif traces during grammar induction or trigger learning; all rule generation forbidden at test time.","zh":"仅在训练 API 与已见模体上的工作流图差分、失败模体、以及经独立执行验证的修复后成功（执行轨迹，非学习评分器）；在语法归纳或触发器学习期间不使用目标 API 或目标模体轨迹；测试时禁止一切规则生成。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Programmatic execution of the repaired workflow: re-run the repaired workflow graph on API-disjoint and motif-disjoint held-out instances against the actual API, verifying structural validity and task success by execution outcome (API calls, return values, task completion), never by grammar acceptance or a learned scorer. All instances in the full distribution are executed, not just those where composition was required.","zh":"程序化执行修复后的工作流：在 API 不相交且模体不相交的留出实例上实际运行修复后的工作流图，以执行结果（API 调用、返回值、任务完成）验证结构有效性与任务成功，而非以语法接受度或学习评分器判定。全分布中的所有实例均被执行，而非仅执行组合必需的实例。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"Three internal controls under identical resources, all evaluated on the full distribution with no structural exclusion: (1) retrieval-only—nearest-neighbor graph-diff/subgraph retrieval from source failures with no learned productions; (2) graph-diff template—direct application of stored diffs without production composition; (3) composition-disabled grammar—the same learned productions but prohibited from composing, applying only single-production rewrites. External Failure-Driven Workflow Refinement and HarnessFix are included as external baselines, but the three internal controls are the decisive comparison. All controls can succeed on any instance where their mechanism suffices.","zh":"三个在相同资源下的内部控制，均在全分布上评估且无结构性排除：(1) 仅检索——来自源失败的最近邻图差分/子图检索，无已学习产生式；(2) 图差分模板——直接应用存储的差分，不做产生式组合；(3) 组合禁用语法——同一已学习产生式但禁止组合，仅应用单产生式重写。外部的 Failure-Driven Workflow Refinement 与 HarnessFix 作为外部基线纳入，但三个内部控制是决定性比较。所有控制可在其机制足够的任何实例上成功。"},"matched_resources":["identical failure/repair graph diffs and failure corpora","identical failure-motif labels","identical workflow traces","identical production/retrieval budget and capacity (production rule set uses the same total parameter count as the retrieval index)","identical LLM calls for trace parsing","identical tokens","identical optimizer and minibatches/steps for any learned trigger weights","matched wall-clock","identical interventions: all arms evaluated on the full distribution of held-out failures with no structural exclusion","no arm may consume more compute than the full-grammar arm","composition-requiring subset identified post-hoc for diagnostic analysis only, not for primary claim evaluation"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"A single preregistered stratified 2×2×2 pilot on the full distribution of held-out workflow failures: factor A = {seen API, unseen API}, factor B = {seen motif, unseen motif}, factor C = {full compositional grammar, composition-disabled grammar (single-production rewrites only)}; retrieval-only and graph-diff-template controls are additionally run under identical resources. The primary endpoint is success rate across the full distribution; composition-requiring instances are a pre-registered secondary diagnostic subset. All arms are evaluated on all instances—no arm is structurally excluded from any test case.","zh":"在留出工作流失败的全分布上进行预注册分层 2×2×2 试验：因子 A = {已见 API，未见 API}，因子 B = {已见模体，未见模体}，因子 C = {完整组合语法，组合禁用语法（仅单产生式重写）}；另在相同资源下运行仅检索与图差分模板控制。主要终点是全分布上的成功率；组合必需实例为预注册次要诊断子集。所有臂在所有实例上评估——无任何臂被结构性排除于任何测试用例。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Terminate or collapse the claim if any of the following holds: (a) any control (retrieval-only, graph-diff template, composition-disabled) matches the full grammar on the full-distribution crossed API×motif holdout success within the preregistered δ, in which case the surviving contribution narrows to whichever control wins; (b) the full grammar's advantage over composition-disabled is statistically significant only within the composition-requiring diagnostic subset and not on the full distribution, indicating the claim is slice-dependent; (c) fewer than two learned productions fire on more than 50% of holdout workflows where the full grammar succeeds, indicating composition is rare; (d) retrieval-only matches or exceeds the full grammar on the full distribution. The claim survives only if the full grammar significantly outperforms all controls on the full distribution AND the advantage is not exclusively driven by the composition-requiring subset.","zh":"若出现以下任一情况即终止或坍缩主张：(a) 任一控制（仅检索、图差分模板、组合禁用）在全分布交叉 API×模体留出上的成功率与完整语法在预注册 δ 内持平，则存活贡献收窄至胜出的控制；(b) 完整语法相对于组合禁用的优势仅在组合必需诊断子集内统计显著而在全分布上不显著，表明主张依赖于切片；(c) 在完整语法成功的留出工作流中，超过 50% 的实例触发的已学习产生式少于两条，表明组合罕见；(d) 仅检索在全分布上匹配或超过完整语法。主张存活的唯一条件是：完整语法在全分布上显著优于所有控制，且优势并非完全由组合必需子集驱动。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"Compositional application of learned grammar productions achieves higher post-repair success on the full distribution of API-disjoint and motif-disjoint held-out workflow failures than retrieval-only, graph-diff templating, and composition-disabled single-production rewrites, under identical training data, compute, and evaluation budgets. This is an empirically falsifiable claim about composition as the causal mechanism of transfer across the full distribution of real failures—explicitly not a claim that composition is required for all repairs, nor that retrieval cannot represent individual repairs.","zh":"在相同训练数据、算力与评估预算下，已学习语法产生式的组合应用在 API 不相交且模体不相交的留出工作流失败全分布上，取得比仅检索、图差分模板化和组合禁用单产生式重写更高的修复后成功率。这是一个关于组合作为全分布真实失败迁移因果机制的经验上可证伪主张——明确不主张所有修复都需要组合，也不主张检索无法表示单个修复。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Nearest work: Failure-Driven Workflow Refinement (ICLR submission/2026, mechanism overlap), From Failed Trajectories to Reliable LLM Agents: Diagnosing and Repairing Harness Flaws (arXiv/2026, mechanism overlap), WISE-Flow (arXiv/2026, problem overlap). This idea differs by explicitly isolating the causal mechanism of transfer as novel production composition, tested via stratified full-distribution evaluation with composition-disabled/retrieval-only/graph-diff-template controls as the decisive comparison; it does not claim this literature does not exist or that it entirely lacks composition.","zh":"最近邻工作为 Failure-Driven Workflow Refinement（ICLR submission/2026，机制重叠）、From Failed Trajectories to Reliable LLM Agents: Diagnosing and Repairing Harness Flaws（arXiv/2026，机制重叠）、WISE-Flow（arXiv/2026，问题重叠）。本想法与它们的区别在于：将迁移的因果机制显式隔离为新颖产生式组合，并以分层全分布评估加组合禁用/仅检索/图差分模板控制作为决定性检验；不声称上述文献不存在，也不声称其完全未涉及组合。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"R3.2 repairs the selection bias and baseline unfairness identified by DeepSeek: (1) the test set is now the full distribution of held-out workflow failures, not filtered to composition-requiring instances; (2) all arms (full grammar, composition-disabled, retrieval-only, graph-diff template) are evaluated on all instances with no structural exclusion, making baselines fair; (3) composition-requiring instances are demoted to a pre-registered secondary diagnostic subset, not the primary test; (4) the stop condition now explicitly kills the claim if the full-grammar advantage is confined to the composition-requiring subset or if any control matches the full grammar on the full distribution.","zh":"R3.2 修复了 DeepSeek 识别的选择偏差与基线不公平：(1) 测试集现为留出工作流失败的全分布，而非过滤为组合必需实例；(2) 所有臂（完整语法、组合禁用、仅检索、图差分模板）在所有实例上评估，无结构性排除，使基线公平；(3) 组合必需实例降级为预注册次要诊断子集，而非主要检验；(4) 停止条件现明确规定：若完整语法优势仅限于组合必需子集，或任一控制在全分布上与完整语法持平，则主张终止。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"On the full distribution, most real failures may be solvable by single-production rewrites or retrieval, so the full grammar's advantage may be small in absolute terms even if composition is the true mechanism for hard cases; the composition-requiring diagnostic subset may be too small to provide statistical power; if the grammar's trigger learning is imperfect, it may fire single productions on instances where composition would be better, diluting the measured advantage.","zh":"在全分布上，大多数真实失败可能由单产生式重写或检索解决，因此即使组合是困难案例的真实机制，完整语法的优势在绝对值上可能很小；组合必需诊断子集可能太小而无法提供统计功效；如果语法的触发器学习不完美，它可能在组合更优的实例上触发单条产生式，从而稀释测得的优势。"}},{"idea_id":"restoration-clause-induction-v5","revision":"R3.1","title":{"en":"Restoration-Clause Induction v5: Crossed Isolation Against a Direct Order-Aware Composition-Risk Model","zh":"恢复子句归纳 v5：与直接序感知组合风险模型的交叉隔离比较"},"purpose":{"en":"Rollback localization can identify faulty updates, but without reusable composition rules the same regressions recur. This idea tests whether explicitly induced relational restoration clauses provide a transferable gating advantage for unseen update compositions, isolated against a direct composition-risk model that can represent the same function.","zh":"回滚定位可以识别有故障的更新，但若缺少可复用的组合规则，相同的回归会反复出现。本想法检验显式归纳的关系型恢复子句是否对未见更新组合提供可迁移的门控优势，并与能表示同一函数的直接组合风险模型进行隔离比较。"},"importance":{"en":"Self-evolving agents that apply many updates need composition-level safety rules that generalize beyond seen update tuples. Establishing whether symbolic clause structure beats an equally-resourced direct risk model determines whether the field should invest in explicit relational induction or in feature-based risk scoring for update gating.","zh":"应用大量更新的自进化智能体需要能泛化到已见更新元组之外的组合级安全规则。明确符号子句结构是否优于同等资源的直接风险模型，决定了该领域应投资于显式关系归纳还是基于特征的风险评分来做更新门控。"},"core_idea":{"en":"In a frozen typed update-descriptor language, induce confidence-bearing no-good, compatibility, and precedence clauses from randomized rollback interventions with explicit false-block control; freeze the clause library and compare it, on completely held-out composition templates, against a direct pairwise/higher-order/order-aware composition-risk model trained on the identical intervention table under identical capacity, compute, and false-block calibration.","zh":"在冻结的类型化更新描述语言中，从带回滚干预的随机化实验中归纳出带置信度的 no-good、兼容性与优先序子句，并进行显式的误阻塞控制；冻结该子句库，在完全留出的组合模板上，与在相同干预表上训练、容量/算力/误阻塞校准完全一致的直接成对/高阶/序感知组合风险模型进行比较。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"A direct risk model can in principle represent the same gating function as the clause library, so the claim is not representational necessity. The testable hypothesis is an inductive-bias/transfer claim: explicit symbolic clauses, constrained by the typed descriptor language, should generalize to unseen composition templates with lower false-block rate or higher utility retention than a feature-based risk model given identical data and budget.","zh":"直接风险模型原则上可以表示与子句库相同的门控函数，因此本主张并非表示能力上的必要性。可检验的假设是归纳偏置/迁移主张：受类型化描述语言约束的显式符号子句，在相同数据与预算下，应以更低的误阻塞率或更高的效用保持率泛化到未见组合模板，优于基于特征的风险模型。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3 found that the frozen relational clauses were not isolated from a direct interaction/order-aware composition-risk model. The smallest material repair is to keep the clause-induction mechanism unchanged and add the exact fully crossed template-held-out comparison R3 required, with both arms consuming identical interventions, descriptors, capacity, compute, and false-block calibration, under independent execution truth. The claim is honestly narrowed from representational advantage to a falsifiable inductive-bias/transfer advantage.","zh":"R3 发现冻结的关系子句未与直接的交互/序感知组合风险模型相隔离。最小的实质性修复是保持子句归纳机制不变，加入 R3 要求的完全交叉模板留出比较：两臂使用完全相同的干预、描述符、容量、算力与误阻塞校准，并以独立执行真值评估。主张被诚实地从表示优势收窄为可证伪的归纳偏置/迁移优势。"},"method_logic":{"en":"1) From one shared randomized intervention table (typed update descriptors, rollback outcomes, execution-verified restoration results, explicit false-block labels) collected on training composition templates only, induce the confidence-bearing no-good/compatibility/precedence clause library; freeze it. 2) Train the direct composition-risk model (pairwise, higher-order interaction, and order-aware features over the same descriptors) on the identical table with matched capacity and optimizer/steps; freeze it. 3) Calibrate both arms to the same false-block budget on a shared pre-holdout calibration split; freeze thresholds. 4) Evaluate both frozen arms on completely held-out composition templates using programmatic execution truth. 5) The factorial contrast is gating structure (symbolic clauses vs. direct risk features) × template (seen vs. unseen), all other factors held constant.","zh":"1）从一张共享的随机化干预表（类型化更新描述符、回滚结果、经执行验证的恢复结果、显式误阻塞标签，仅来自训练组合模板）归纳带置信度的 no-good/兼容性/优先序子句库并冻结。2）在完全相同的表上，以匹配的容量与优化器/步数训练直接组合风险模型（基于相同描述符的成对、高阶交互与序感知特征）并冻结。3）在共享的留出前校准划分上将两臂校准到相同的误阻塞预算并冻结阈值。4）在完全留出的组合模板上用程序化执行真值评估两个冻结臂。5）析因对比为门控结构（符号子句 vs 直接风险特征）× 模板（已见 vs 未见），其余因素全部保持恒定。"},"persistent_update_object":"Frozen update-composition clause library: confidence-bearing no-good, compatibility, and precedence clauses in the typed descriptor language, induced from the training-template intervention table, frozen before held-out evaluation, and applied to unseen composition templates with no test-time clause induction, relearning, or threshold refitting.","learning_signal":{"en":"Randomized rollback interventions, typed update descriptors, execution-verified restoration outcomes, and explicit false-block labels, drawn exclusively from training composition templates; the direct-risk arm receives the identical table. No held-out-template data is used for induction, training, or calibration.","zh":"随机化回滚干预、类型化更新描述符、经执行验证的恢复结果与显式误阻塞标签，全部仅来自训练组合模板；直接风险臂获得完全相同的表。留出模板数据不用于归纳、训练或校准。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Programmatic execution truth: held-out update compositions are actually applied (in the predicted safe order) to the live or simulated system, and regression occurrence, false-block events, and utility retention are measured from runtime behavior (test-suite pass/fail, performance metrics), never from the clause library's or the risk model's own scores.","zh":"程序化执行真值：留出的更新组合被实际应用（按预测的安全顺序）到真实或仿真系统中，回归发生、误阻塞事件与效用保持均从运行时行为（测试套件通过/失败、性能指标）测量，绝不使用子句库或风险模型自身的评分。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"A direct pairwise/higher-order/order-aware composition-risk model (PMA/ProbDD-style posterior risk gating; ANNEAL-style governed gating as an external reference) trained on the identical intervention table with identical descriptors, capacity, compute, and false-block calibration. This direct model is the decisive comparison because it can represent the same gating function; the clause library must win on inductive bias, not representational necessity.","zh":"在完全相同的干预表上以相同描述符、容量、算力与误阻塞校准训练的直接成对/高阶/序感知组合风险模型（PMA/ProbDD 式后验风险门控；ANNEAL 式受治理门控作为外部参照）。该直接模型是决定性对照，因为它能表示相同的门控函数；子句库必须在归纳偏置上取胜，而非表示必要性。"},"matched_resources":["identical randomized intervention table (same rollback experiments, outcomes, and false-block labels)","identical typed update descriptors for both arms","identical model capacity budget (clause count/confidence parameters vs. risk-model parameter count)","identical optimizer, minibatches, and training steps","identical compute and wall-clock budget","identical shared pre-holdout calibration split and false-block calibration procedure/threshold budget","identical held-out composition template split (templates fully excluded from all training/calibration)","identical independent execution-truth evaluation harness and metrics"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"A single preregistered fully crossed template-held-out test: factor A = gating mechanism {frozen clause library, direct pairwise/higher-order risk model, direct order-aware risk model}; factor B = composition template {seen, unseen}. All arms consume the identical intervention table, descriptors, capacity, compute, calibration split, and false-block budget. Primary endpoints under programmatic execution truth: regression prevention, false-block rate, and utility retention on unseen templates at equal calibrated false-block budget. The surviving claim is killed if any direct risk arm matches the clause arm within the preregistered δ on unseen templates.","zh":"单一预注册的完全交叉模板留出测试：因子 A = 门控机制 {冻结子句库，直接成对/高阶风险模型，直接序感知风险模型}；因子 B = 组合模板 {已见，未见}。所有臂使用完全相同的干预表、描述符、容量、算力、校准划分与误阻塞预算。在程序化执行真值下的主要终点：在相等校准误阻塞预算下，未见模板上的回归预防、误阻塞率与效用保持。若任何直接风险臂在未见模板上与子句臂的差距处于预注册 δ 之内，则存活主张被否决。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Stop if, on unseen composition templates at equal calibrated false-block budget, either direct risk model matches or exceeds the frozen clause library on regression prevention and utility retention within the preregistered δ — in which case the clause structure is unnecessary and the contribution collapses to interpretability only. Also stop if the clause arm's false-block rate exceeds the preregistered maximum relative to the direct arms.","zh":"若在相等校准误阻塞预算下，任一直接风险模型在未见组合模板上的回归预防与效用保持达到或超过冻结子句库（处于预注册 δ 之内），则终止——此时子句结构并非必要，贡献坍缩为仅具可解释性。若子句臂的误阻塞率相对直接臂超过预注册上限，同样终止。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"Explicitly induced relational restoration clauses (no-good, compatibility, precedence) achieve lower false-block rate or higher utility retention on unseen update compositions than a matched-capacity direct pairwise/higher-order/order-aware composition-risk model trained on the identical intervention data — a falsifiable inductive-bias/transfer claim. It is explicitly not a representational-impossibility claim: the direct model can represent the same gating function.","zh":"显式归纳的关系型恢复子句（no-good、兼容性、优先序）在未见更新组合上，相较在相同干预数据上训练的等容量直接成对/高阶/序感知组合风险模型，取得更低的误阻塞率或更高的效用保持——这是一个可证伪的归纳偏置/迁移主张。明确而言，这不是表示不可能性主张：直接模型可以表示相同的门控函数。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Nearest supplied work: ANNEAL (arXiv/2026) adapts LLM agents via governed symbolic patch learning, overlapping on mechanism (symbolic patch/rule gating); Governed Capability Evolution for Embodied Agents (arXiv/2026) covers safe upgrade, compatibility checking, and runtime rollback for capability modules, overlapping on combination. This idea differs from both as supplied: it does not claim a new gating mechanism per se, but a preregistered crossed isolation of explicit induced restoration clauses against an equally-resourced direct order-aware composition-risk model on held-out composition templates under programmatic execution truth. No claim is made that other literature does not exist.","zh":"所供最近工作：ANNEAL（arXiv/2026）通过受治理的符号补丁学习适配 LLM 智能体，在机制上重叠（符号补丁/规则门控）；面向具身智能体的受治理能力进化（arXiv/2026）涵盖能力模块的安全升级、兼容性检查与运行时回滚，在组合上重叠。本想法与二者的区别（仅基于所供信息）：它并不主张新的门控机制本身，而是主张在留出组合模板上、以程序化执行真值，对显式归纳的恢复子句与同等资源的直接序感知组合风险模型进行预注册的交叉隔离检验。不主张其他文献不存在。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"R3 found the frozen relational clauses were not isolated from a direct interaction/order-aware composition-risk model and required a fully crossed template-held-out test on the same intervention table, descriptors, capacity, compute, and false-block calibration with independent execution truth. The repair keeps the clause-induction mechanism unchanged and adds exactly that crossed comparison: a direct pairwise/higher-order/order-aware risk model trained on the identical table, both arms frozen, calibrated to the same false-block budget on a shared split, and evaluated on fully held-out composition templates under programmatic execution truth. The claim is honestly narrowed to a falsifiable inductive-bias/transfer advantage, explicitly acknowledging the direct model can represent the same gating function.","zh":"R3 发现冻结的关系子句未与直接交互/序感知组合风险模型隔离，并要求在相同干预表、描述符、容量、算力与误阻塞校准下进行完全交叉的模板留出测试，且使用独立执行真值。修复保持子句归纳机制不变，恰好加入该交叉比较：在相同表上训练直接成对/高阶/序感知风险模型，两臂均冻结，在共享划分上校准至相同误阻塞预算，并在完全留出的组合模板上以程序化执行真值评估。主张被诚实地收窄为可证伪的归纳偏置/迁移优势，并明确承认直接模型可表示相同的门控函数。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"The direct order-aware risk model may be strong enough that any clause advantage is confined to low-data regimes; the clause induction's reliance on the typed descriptor language could confound the comparison if descriptors are not equally usable by the direct model (mitigated by feeding identical descriptors to both arms); and if removing clause structure changes nothing on held-out templates, the surviving contribution reduces to interpretability.","zh":"直接序感知风险模型可能强到使子句优势仅存在于低数据区间；子句归纳对类型化描述语言的依赖可能在描述符不能被直接模型同等利用时混淆比较（通过向两臂提供完全相同的描述符来缓解）；若移除子句结构在留出模板上毫无影响，则存活贡献退化为仅具可解释性。"}},{"idea_id":"rubric-intervention-sparse-solver","revision":"R3.1","title":{"en":"Rubric Intervention Sparse Solver: Causal-Effect × Sparse-Constrained Factorial","zh":"Rubric 干预稀疏求解器：因果效应 × 稀疏约束因子分解"},"purpose":{"en":"Repair a rubric that suffers systematic bias from a few rubric atoms while avoiding whole-rubric rewriting that damages neutral dimensions. The goal is to isolate whether atom-level causal intervention effects, combined with a sparsity-constrained edit, are the minimal mechanism that reduces bias while preserving neutral dimensions.","zh":"修复因少数 rubric 原子导致系统性偏差的评分准则，同时避免整体重写破坏中立维度。目标是分离出原子级因果干预效应与稀疏约束编辑相结合，是否构成在保持中立维度的同时降低偏差的最小机制。"},"importance":{"en":"Rubric-based LLM judges and reward models are widely deployed, but small biased atoms can systematically distort rankings while naive rewriting harms neutral criteria. A minimal, causally grounded, neutral-preserving repair mechanism would give a principled way to fix judges without retraining or wholesale rubric replacement, directly relevant to reward modeling and open-ended evaluation.","zh":"基于 rubric 的 LLM 评判与奖励模型被广泛部署，但少数有偏差的原子会系统性扭曲排序，而朴素重写会损害中立标准。一个最小化、有因果依据且保持中立维度的修复机制，能在不重训练或整体替换 rubric 的情况下有原则地修复评判器，直接关系到奖励建模与开放式评估。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Build a rubric-atom effect matrix from externally labeled causal/neutral interventions and solve a constrained sparse add/drop/reweight edit that explicitly preserves neutral dimensions; the causal-effect estimation and the sparse constrained solver are the only claimed mechanisms.","zh":"从外部标注的因果/中立干预构建 rubric 原子效应矩阵，并求解一个显式保持中立维度的稀疏约束增/删/重加权编辑；因果效应估计与稀疏约束求解器是唯一声明的机制。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"Only interventions that actually change the ranking when a single atom is flipped identify which atoms carry causal bias; a sparsity constraint then forces the repair to touch the fewest atoms so neutral dimensions survive. Association alone cannot distinguish bias carriers from correlated bystanders, and unconstrained rewriting cannot guarantee neutrality.","zh":"只有当翻转单个原子真正改变排序时，干预才能识别哪些原子携带因果偏差；稀疏约束迫使修复触及最少原子，从而让中立维度得以保留。仅靠关联无法区分偏差携带者与其相关伴随变量，而无约束重写无法保证中立性。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3 found the surviving thesis to be atom-level causal intervention effects for minimal rubric repair, with executable/versioned packaging not novel. The repair therefore strips the packaging claim and isolates two identifiable factors — causal-vs-association effect representation and sparse-constrained-vs-generic updater — in a crossed design so each factor's contribution is falsifiable.","zh":"R3 认定幸存的命题是用于最小化 rubric 修复的原子级因果干预效应，而可执行/版本化封装本身不具新颖性。因此本修复剥离封装声明，在交叉设计中分离两个可识别因子——因果与关联效应表示、稀疏约束与通用更新器——使每个因子的贡献都可被证伪。"},"method_logic":{"en":"1) Preregister rubric atoms and single-atom interventions; obtain causal/neutral labels from an external source independent of the judge being repaired (human-verified annotations or a held-out intervention oracle). 2) Estimate the atom effect matrix either from interventional structure (flip one atom, hold others fixed, measure ranking change) or, in the association arm, from observational atom–outcome co-occurrence on the same data. 3) Apply either an L1-penalized sparse add/drop/reweight solver (max k atoms changed, neutral atoms constrained) or a generic greedy updater without sparsity. 4) Freeze the effect matrix and the resulting edited rubric before any held-out evaluation; reuse without test-time refitting. 5) Evaluate on frozen independent tasks with pre-existing ground-truth rankings via a separate held-out judge and human annotation.","zh":"1）预注册 rubric 原子与单原子干预；由独立于被修复评判器的外部来源（人工核验标注或留出干预预言机）获得因果/中立标签。2）从干预结构（翻转一个原子、固定其余、测量排序变化）估计原子效应矩阵，或在关联臂中基于相同数据上的观测性原子–结果共现进行估计。3）施加 L1 惩罚的稀疏增/删/重加权求解器（最多改 k 个原子、约束中立原子）或无稀疏约束的通用贪心更新器。4）在任何留出评估之前冻结效应矩阵与由此产生的编辑后 rubric；复用时不在测试时重新拟合。5）通过独立的留出评判器与人工标注，在带有预先存在真实排序的冻结独立任务上评估。"},"persistent_update_object":"Frozen rubric-atom effect matrix (per-atom causal effect sizes and neutral-preservation flags) together with the solved sparse edit, fitted on the calibration intervention set, frozen before held-out evaluation, and reused across all held-out tasks without test-time relearning; the edited rubric is applied with ordinary deterministic decoding, which is permitted because the claim concerns the learned effect matrix and edit, and every matched baseline receives the same decoder.","learning_signal":{"en":"Rubric-atom interventions with externally assigned causal/neutral labels, observed ranking changes on a calibration task set, and neutral-preservation labels; the association arm uses only correlational structure over the same atom–outcome observations, never additional data.","zh":"带有外部分配因果/中立标签的 rubric 原子干预、校准任务集上观测到的排序变化，以及中立维度保持标签；关联臂仅使用相同原子–结果观测上的相关结构，绝不使用额外数据。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Externally independent causal/neutral atom labels from a separate labeling pipeline (human-verified causal annotations or a held-out intervention oracle) not used by the solver; bias reduction, true-ranking recovery, and neutral-dimension preservation measured by executing the rubric on frozen independent tasks with pre-existing ground-truth rankings via a separate held-out judge — never the same learned judge or reward model under repair, and never the solver's own effect matrix.","zh":"来自独立标注流水线（人工核验因果标注或留出干预预言机）的外部独立因果/中立原子标签，求解器不使用这些标签的来源；通过在带有预先存在真实排序的冻结独立任务上执行 rubric，由独立的留出评判器测量偏差降低、真实排序恢复与中立维度保持——绝不使用同一被修复的学习评判器或奖励模型，也绝不使用求解器自身的效应矩阵。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"The three other factorial cells — association-based effect matrix + sparse solver, causal effect matrix + generic greedy updater, association matrix + greedy updater — plus generic whole-rubric rewriting (RRD/PReMISE-style on CROME interventions) and reward fine-tuning, all under identical budgets. The crossed internal controls are the decisive comparison; RRD/PReMISE/reward fine-tuning are external references.","zh":"其余三个因子单元——关联效应矩阵+稀疏求解器、因果效应矩阵+通用贪心更新器、关联矩阵+贪心更新器——外加通用整体 rubric 重写（基于 CROME 干预的 RRD/PReMISE 式方法）与奖励微调，全部在相同预算下。交叉内部控制是决定性比较；RRD/PReMISE/奖励微调为外部参照。"},"matched_resources":["identical rubric atoms and candidate edit space","identical number and set of single-atom interventions (causal and association arms use the same atom–outcome observations; the association arm receives no additional observational data)","identical externally sourced causal/neutral labels across all cells that use labels","identical calibration task set and identical held-out independent task set with ground-truth rankings","identical LLM-call budget for rubric execution and scoring","identical token budget","identical model capacity for judge/scorer components","identical optimizer, minibatch, and optimization-step budget for any fitted component (effect-matrix estimation, solver, fine-tuning baseline)","matched wall-clock","identical deterministic decoder for applying the edited rubric across all conditions"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"A single preregistered 2×2 factorial: Factor A = effect representation {causal (intervention-derived) vs. association (correlation-derived)}; Factor B = updater {sparse-constrained add/drop/reweight solver vs. generic greedy updater}. All four cells share identical atoms, interventions, labels, calibration tasks, LLM calls, tokens, capacity, optimization budget, and wall-clock. External causal/neutral labels are preregistered and fixed before any solver runs. Outcome metrics: bias reduction, true-ranking recovery, and neutral-dimension preservation on frozen independent tasks, with a preregistered non-inferiority margin δ. The causal×sparse cell must beat all three other cells and the generic-rewriting baseline for the claim to survive.","zh":"单一预注册 2×2 因子实验：因子 A = 效应表示 {因果（干预导出） vs. 关联（相关导出）}；因子 B = 更新器 {稀疏约束增/删/重加权求解器 vs. 通用贪心更新器}。四个单元共享相同的原子、干预、标签、校准任务、LLM 调用、token、容量、优化预算与墙钟时间。外部因果/中立标签在任何求解器运行前预注册并固定。结果指标：冻结独立任务上的偏差降低、真实排序恢复与中立维度保持，并设定预注册的非劣效界 δ。因果×稀疏单元必须优于其余三个单元及通用重写基线，命题方能成立。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Terminate or collapse the claim if: (a) the causal×sparse cell does not outperform the association×sparse cell (causal representation unnecessary), or (b) it does not outperform the causal×greedy cell (sparse constraint unnecessary), or (c) any simpler cell or generic whole-rubric rewriting ties within the preregistered δ on bias reduction and neutral preservation, or (d) neutral dimensions are not preserved better than generic rewriting. If a simpler cell ties, the surviving contribution narrows to that cell and the causal/sparse claim is abandoned.","zh":"若出现以下情形则终止或收缩命题：(a) 因果×稀疏单元未优于关联×稀疏单元（因果表示非必要）；或 (b) 未优于因果×贪心单元（稀疏约束非必要）；或 (c) 任何更简单单元或通用整体重写在预注册 δ 内于偏差降低与中立保持上打平；或 (d) 中立维度保持不优于通用重写。若更简单单元打平，幸存贡献收缩至该单元，并放弃因果/稀疏声明。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"Atom-level causal intervention effects (not mere association), combined with a sparsity-constrained edit (not greedy rewriting), achieve greater bias reduction with better neutral-dimension preservation than the other three factorial cells and generic rewriting, under identical budgets and evaluation on independent tasks with ground-truth rankings — an empirically falsifiable inductive-bias claim about the value of causal structure and sparsity for minimal rubric repair, with no claim that executable/versioned packaging is novel.","zh":"原子级因果干预效应（而非仅关联）与稀疏约束编辑（而非贪心重写）相结合，在相同预算下、于带真实排序的独立任务上，相比其余三个因子单元与通用重写取得更大的偏差降低与更好的中立维度保持——这是一个关于因果结构与稀疏性对最小化 rubric 修复价值的可实证证伪的归纳偏置声明，且不声称可执行/版本化封装具有新颖性。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Nearest supplied work: 'Rethinking Rubric Generation for Improving LLM Judge and Reward Modeling for Open-ended Tasks' (arXiv 2026) overlaps at the mechanism level on rubric generation/improvement; 'PReMISE: Policy Rubrics as Measurement Specifications for LLM Judges' (arXiv 2026) and 'RubricBench: Aligning Model-Generated Rubrics with Human Standards' (ACL 2026) overlap at the problem level on rubric quality and alignment. This idea differs by claiming neither rubric generation nor packaging novelty, but specifically the crossed necessity of causal (vs. associational) atom-effect estimation and sparsity-constrained (vs. greedy) editing for neutral-preserving minimal repair; no claim is made that this specific factorial isolation exists or does not exist in the literature beyond the supplied context.","zh":"最接近的已有工作：《Rethinking Rubric Generation for Improving LLM Judge and Reward Modeling for Open-ended Tasks》（arXiv 2026）在机制层面与 rubric 生成/改进重叠；《PReMISE: Policy Rubrics as Measurement Specifications for LLM Judges》（arXiv 2026）与《RubricBench: Aligning Model-Generated Rubrics with Human Standards》（ACL 2026）在问题层面与 rubric 质量及对齐重叠。本想法不声称 rubric 生成或封装的新颖性，而专门声称因果（相对关联）原子效应估计与稀疏约束（相对贪心）编辑对保持中立维度的最小化修复的交叉必要性；除所给上下文外，不就文献中是否存在该特定因子分离作任何主张。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"R3 identified the surviving thesis as atom-level causal intervention effects for minimal rubric repair and required externally independent causal/neutral labels plus a preregistered causal-vs-association × sparse-constrained-vs-generic factorial under identical budgets. The repair (i) drops the non-novel executable/versioned packaging claim, (ii) sources causal/neutral labels from an external pipeline independent of the judge under repair, (iii) preregisters the exact 2×2 factorial with identical atoms, interventions, labels, calls, tokens, capacity, optimization budget, and wall-clock across all four cells, and (iv) evaluates on frozen independent tasks with ground-truth rankings via a separate held-out judge, with a stop rule that collapses the claim if any simpler cell ties.","zh":"R3 认定幸存命题为用于最小化 rubric 修复的原子级因果干预效应，并要求外部独立的因果/中立标签，以及在相同预算下预注册的因果对关联 × 稀疏约束对通用因子实验。本修复：(i) 放弃不具新颖性的可执行/版本化封装声明；(ii) 由独立于被修复评判器的外部流水线获取因果/中立标签；(iii) 预注册严格的 2×2 因子实验，四个单元共享相同原子、干预、标签、调用、token、容量、优化预算与墙钟时间；(iv) 通过独立的留出评判器在带真实排序的冻结独立任务上评估，并设有在任意更简单单元打平时收缩命题的停止规则。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"Externally sourced causal/neutral labels may be noisy or expensive at scale; if confounding is low, the association representation may closely approximate causal effects, shrinking the causal factor's advantage and making it regime-dependent; if the sparse constraint merely regularizes, a greedy updater with early stopping could match it. Each failure mode is covered by the factorial stop rule, which falsifies the corresponding factor.","zh":"外部来源的因果/中立标签可能含噪或在大规模下昂贵；若混杂较低，关联表示可能近似因果效应，使因果因子的优势变小且依赖于具体情境；若稀疏约束仅起正则化作用，带早停的贪心更新器可能与之打平。每种失效模式均被因子化停止规则覆盖，可证伪相应因子。"}},{"idea_id":"update-history-semantic-compactor","revision":"R3.1","title":{"en":"Update-History Semantic Compactor: Non-Local Order-Sensitivity Isolated by a Crossed Semantic-Dedup Ablation","zh":"更新历史语义压缩器：以交叉语义去重消融隔离非局部顺序敏感性"},"purpose":{"en":"Long prompt/memory/workflow version chains accumulate redundant and shadowed rules, increasing conflict and maintenance cost. The goal is a canonicalized persistent update state that preserves behavior and supports reliable rollback under a fixed compression budget.","zh":"长提示/记忆/工作流版本链会积累冗余与被遮蔽的规则，增加冲突与维护成本。目标是得到一个规范化的持久更新状态，在固定压缩预算下保持行为并支持可靠回滚。"},"importance":{"en":"If validated, the result tells practitioners when structured history compaction is worth its complexity versus cheap semantic deduplication, and gives a reusable methodology (crossed mechanism × topology ablation with matched replay/rollback infrastructure) for isolating memory-mechanism claims.","zh":"若被验证，该结果能告诉实践者何时值得使用结构化历史压缩而非廉价的语义去重，并提供一种可复用的方法论（机制×拓扑的交叉消融 + 匹配的回放/回滚设施），用于隔离记忆机制类主张。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Keep the typed behavioral-constraint graph compactor, but narrow the claim to a falsifiable inductive-bias/efficiency statement: on non-local/order-sensitive histories the graph compactor should beat an equally resourced semantic-deduplication/reconciliation compactor, and on local/commutative histories the advantage should shrink. Isolate the mechanism with a preregistered 2×2 crossed factorial: {compactor: graph vs. semantic-dedup} × {history family: non-local/order-sensitive vs. local/commutative}, with identical replay probes, rollback metadata, verifier access, compression budget, and disjoint programmatic held-out evaluation.","zh":"保留类型化行为约束图压缩器，但将主张收窄为可证伪的归纳偏置/效率命题：在非局部/顺序敏感历史上，图压缩器应优于资源完全匹配的语义去重/调和压缩器；在局部/可交换历史上优势应缩小。用预注册的 2×2 交叉因子设计隔离机制：{压缩器：图 vs. 语义去重} × {历史族：非局部/顺序敏感 vs. 局部/可交换}，两臂具有相同的回放探针、回滚元数据、验证器访问、压缩预算，并使用不相交的程序化留出评估。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"If the graph's only advantage came from shared replay probes, rollback metadata, and verifier access, then a semantic-dedup compactor given those same resources should match it. The graph should win only where non-local/order-sensitive shadowing actually exists; the interaction (mechanism × history family) is the evidence, and its absence kills the claim.","zh":"如果图的优势仅来自共享的回放探针、回滚元数据和验证器访问，那么获得同样资源的语义去重压缩器应当能与之持平。图压缩器只应在真正存在非局部/顺序敏感遮蔽的历史上获胜；机制×历史族的交互作用才是证据，交互不显著则主张被证伪。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3's objection is that the graph mechanism was not isolated from semantic deduplication with identical replay/rollback metadata. The smallest repair is not to replace the mechanism but to test it in a crossed design where the only difference between arms is whether non-local/order-sensitive structure is exploited, and where history family moderates whether that structure should matter. Following the honest-claim rule, we do not claim semantic dedup cannot represent the same function—only that the graph's order-sensitive inductive bias yields better compression fidelity and rollback recovery specifically on order-sensitive histories, a claim the interaction test can falsify.","zh":"R3 的反对意见是图机制未与拥有相同回放/回滚元数据的语义去重相隔离。最小修复不是替换机制，而是在交叉设计中检验它：两臂唯一差别在于是否利用非局部/顺序敏感结构，且历史族决定该结构是否应当起作用。遵循诚实主张原则，我们不声称语义去重无法表示相同函数——仅声称图的顺序敏感归纳偏置在顺序敏感历史上带来更好的压缩保真度与回滚恢复，该主张可被交互检验证伪。"},"method_logic":{"en":"Both compactors emit a canonical state plus rollback mapping under the same fixed budget from the same version-history input. The graph compactor performs non-local, order-aware shadowing/equivalence detection via counterfactual replay over the typed constraint graph; the baseline performs only local pairwise semantic deduplication/reconciliation over the same updates with the same replay probes and metadata. The mechanisms differ only in whether non-local/order-sensitive structure is exploited, and history family moderates whether that structure exists to exploit.","zh":"两种压缩器在相同固定预算下从相同的版本历史输入产出规范状态与回滚映射。图压缩器通过在类型化约束图上进行反事实回放，执行非局部、顺序感知的遮蔽/等价检测；基线仅在相同更新上执行局部成对语义去重/调和，使用相同的回放探针与元数据。两机制唯一区别在于是否利用非局部/顺序敏感结构，而历史族决定这种结构是否存在、可被利用。"},"persistent_update_object":"Frozen canonicalized persistent update state with rollback mapping, compiled once per history by each arm's compactor, frozen before held-out behavioral and rollback evaluation, and reused without any test-time relearning; both arms use the same deterministic decoder/verifier interface.","learning_signal":{"en":"Version history, update dependencies/timestamps, and counterfactual replay outcomes. The semantic-dedup baseline receives exactly the same history, dependency annotations, and replay-outcome observations; the compactor is fitted on training histories and frozen before held-out evaluation.","zh":"版本历史、更新依赖/时间戳与反事实回放结果。语义去重基线获得完全相同的历史、依赖标注与回放结果观测；压缩器在训练历史上拟合后在留出评估前冻结。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Behavioral equivalence, regression outcomes, rollback recovery, and context cost are computed by programmatic replay harnesses and token/cost measurement on held-out histories disjoint from any tuning data; no learned judge or scorer shared with either compactor is used.","zh":"行为等价性、回归结果、回滚恢复与上下文成本均由程序化回放框架和 token/成本测量在留出历史上计算，留出历史与任何调参数据不相交；不使用与任一压缩器共享参数的学习型评判器或打分器。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"Semantic-deduplication/reconciliation compactor receiving identical replay probes, rollback metadata, verifier access, compression budget, model, calls, and tokens, crossed over the same history families; keep-all, text summarization, and last-version-only are retained as reference points.","zh":"语义去重/调和压缩器，获得相同的回放探针、回滚元数据、验证器访问、压缩预算、模型、调用次数与 token，并在相同历史族上交叉比较；同时保留全量保留、文本摘要与仅保留末版作为参照点。"},"matched_resources":["identical version-history sequences and update dependency/timestamp annotations","identical counterfactual replay probe set and replay outcomes","identical rollback metadata format and rollback-target probes","identical verifier access and number of verifier queries","identical fixed canonical-state compression budget (token count)","identical base model, capacity, decoding settings, LLM calls, and token budget","identical optimizer/minibatches/steps for any fitted components","identical held-out task/history evaluation sets, disjoint from tuning data","identical wall-clock measurement protocol for compilation and evaluation"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"Single preregistered 2×2 crossed factorial: Factor A = compactor (typed graph vs. semantic-dedup/reconciliation), Factor B = history family (non-local/order-sensitive vs. local/commutative), with 10–30 round histories per cell. All cells share identical replay probes, rollback metadata, verifier access, compression budget, model, calls, and tokens. Evaluate on disjoint held-out histories with programmatic behavioral-equivalence, regression, rollback-recovery, and context-cost measurements. The claim survives only if the graph compactor wins on rollback recovery and behavioral preservation in the non-local/order-sensitive family at equal budget AND the mechanism × family interaction is significant (preregistered threshold), while the advantage shrinks on the local/commutative family.","zh":"单一预注册 2×2 交叉因子实验：因子 A = 压缩器（类型化图 vs. 语义去重/调和），因子 B = 历史族（非局部/顺序敏感 vs. 局部/可交换），每格使用 10–30 轮历史。所有格子共享相同的回放探针、回滚元数据、验证器访问、压缩预算、模型、调用次数与 token。在不相交的留出历史上用程序化手段测量行为等价性、回归、回滚恢复与上下文成本。主张存活的唯一条件：图压缩器在等预算下于非局部/顺序敏感族上的回滚恢复与行为保持更优，且机制×历史族交互显著（预注册阈值），同时优势在局部/可交换族上缩小。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Stop (or collapse the claim to 'no advantage over matched semantic dedup') if any of: (1) the graph compactor fails to beat the semantic-dedup arm on rollback recovery or behavioral preservation on non-local/order-sensitive histories at equal budget; (2) the mechanism × history-family interaction is not significant at the preregistered threshold; (3) the semantic-dedup arm matches the graph arm within the preregistered equivalence margin on either family; or (4) rollback mapping is unreliable on held-out histories.","zh":"若出现以下任一情况则终止（或将主张坍缩为“相对匹配的语义去重无优势”）：(1) 图压缩器在等预算下未能在非局部/顺序敏感历史上于回滚恢复或行为保持超过语义去重臂；(2) 机制×历史族交互未达预注册显著性阈值；(3) 语义去重臂在任一历史族上与图臂的差距处于预注册等价界内；(4) 回滚映射在留出历史上不可靠。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"On update histories with non-local/order-sensitive shadowing, a typed behavioral-constraint graph compactor preserves behavioral equivalence and rollback recovery at higher compression than an equally resourced semantic-deduplication compactor, and this advantage shrinks on local/commutative histories—an efficiency/inductive-bias claim, not a representational-impossibility claim, falsifiable by the preregistered interaction test.","zh":"在具有非局部/顺序敏感遮蔽的更新历史上，类型化行为约束图压缩器在更高压缩率下比资源完全匹配的语义去重压缩器更好地保持行为等价性与回滚恢复，且该优势在局部/可交换历史上缩小——这是一个效率/归纳偏置主张，而非表示不可能性主张，可由预注册的交互检验证伪。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Nearest supplied work: Graph-Native Cognitive Memory (arXiv 2026) overlaps on graph-based memory mechanisms; ChronoMem (arXiv 2026) overlaps on version control and semantic rollback for agent memory; TRUSTMEM (arXiv 2026) overlaps on the memory consolidation problem. The surviving claim is narrower than all three: it concerns only whether non-local/order-sensitive structure in update histories yields a compression/rollback advantage over an equally resourced semantic-deduplication compactor, tested by a preregistered crossed factorial with matched replay/rollback infrastructure. No claim is made that prior work lacks this comparison; only that within the supplied context, the isolating crossed ablation is the contribution.","zh":"最近的已提供工作：Graph-Native Cognitive Memory（arXiv 2026）在基于图的记忆机制上重叠；ChronoMem（arXiv 2026）在智能体记忆的版本控制与语义回滚上重叠；TRUSTMEM（arXiv 2026）在记忆固化问题上重叠。存活主张比三者都更窄：仅关注更新历史中的非局部/顺序敏感结构是否在匹配资源的语义去重压缩器之上带来压缩/回滚优势，并通过预注册的、回放/回滚设施匹配的交叉因子实验检验。不主张先前工作缺少该比较；仅主张在已提供的上下文中，这一隔离性交叉消融是贡献点。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"R3 found the non-local/order-sensitive graph mechanism was not isolated from semantic deduplication plus identical replay/rollback metadata. The repair keeps the original graph compactor and problem, narrows the claim to an inductive-bias/efficiency statement moderated by history family, and adds a single preregistered 2×2 crossed factorial (compactor × history family) with fully matched replay probes, rollback metadata, verifier access, budget, and disjoint programmatic evaluation. The claim dies if the matched semantic-dedup arm ties on order-sensitive histories or the interaction is absent.","zh":"R3 指出非局部/顺序敏感图机制未与“语义去重 + 相同回放/回滚元数据”隔离。修复保留了原始图压缩器与问题，将主张收窄为由历史族调节的归纳偏置/效率命题，并加入单一预注册 2×2 交叉因子实验（压缩器×历史族），回放探针、回滚元数据、验证器访问、预算完全匹配，评估为不相交的程序化留出评估。若匹配的语义去重臂在顺序敏感历史上持平或交互不显著，主张即终止。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"If semantic deduplication augmented with simple rule-ordering heuristics approximates non-local shadow detection, the interaction may vanish and the claim collapses entirely. Also, if order-sensitive histories are rare in practice, the pilot must report family prevalence or the claim narrows to order-sensitive settings only.","zh":"若加入简单规则排序启发式的语义去重能近似非局部遮蔽检测，交互可能消失，主张将整体坍缩。此外，若顺序敏感历史在实践中稀少，试点必须报告该历史族的占比，否则主张收窄为仅适用于顺序敏感场景。"}},{"idea_id":"bounded-probe-api-transition-operator","revision":"R3.2","title":{"zh":"限探针 API 转移算子：跨源学习参数化 vs 同构非学习实例化","en":"Bounded-Probe API Transition Operator: Cross-Source Learned Parameterization vs. Identically-Structured Non-Learned Instantiation"},"purpose":{"zh":"在 API 迁移中，名称与模式相似的调用仍可能在前置条件、状态副作用与错误恢复语义上存在差异，导致主流程可运行而恢复分支静默失效。本想法旨在以固定的 N 次目标 API 探针预算，将源工作流可靠迁移到未见过的新 API，并重点保护恢复分支语义。","en":"Across API migrations, calls with similar names and schemas can still differ in preconditions, state effects, and error-recovery semantics, so the main workflow may execute while recovery branches silently break. This idea aims to migrate a source workflow to an unseen target API under a fixed budget of N target probes, with emphasis on preserving recovery-branch semantics."},"importance":{"zh":"真实且重要：生产环境中的 API 迁移常因隐式前置条件与恢复语义差异引入难以发现的故障。若能在严格受限的探针预算下保持恢复分支语义，可显著降低迁移风险与人工审计成本。","en":"The problem is real and important: production API migrations often introduce hard-to-detect failures via implicit precondition and recovery-semantics differences. Preserving recovery branches under a tightly bounded probe budget would substantially reduce migration risk and manual auditing cost."},"core_idea":{"zh":"将每个 API 操作表示为类型化转移算子 T=(P,E,X)：P 为可判定的调用前状态谓词，E 为成功后状态增量，X 将错误类别映射到可恢复状态与可采纳的恢复动作。关键修复：同一 P/E/X 类型化表示被用于两个臂——(a) 跨源学习参数化：在多个源 API 族上通过受控状态对与故障注入监督训练共享参数化；(b) 非学习实例化：通过确定性规则从目标 API 文档、模式与同样的 N 次探针直接填充 P/E/X 字段。两臂使用完全相同的表示结构、编译流水线与预算；唯一差异是参数来自跨源学习还是固定规则实例化。N 次探针后，算子与编译后的工作流均被冻结，评估期间无执行-修复循环。","en":"Represent every API operation as a typed transition operator T=(P,E,X): P is a decidable pre-call state predicate, E is the post-success state delta, and X maps error classes to recoverable states and admissible recovery actions. Key repair: the identical P/E/X typed representation is used in two arms—(a) cross-source learned parameterization, where a shared parameterization is trained on controlled state pairs and fault injections across multiple source API families; and (b) non-learned instantiation, where the same P/E/X fields are filled by deterministic rules from target documentation, schemas, and the same N probes. Both arms share the exact same representational structure, compilation pipeline, and budget; the only difference is whether parameters come from cross-source learning or fixed-rule instantiation. After the N probes, both the operator and the compiled workflow are frozen with no execution-repair loop during evaluation."},"core_intuition":{"zh":"类型化 P/E/X 结构本身可能已足以表达恢复语义；因此可信的剩余主张不是“该表示不可或缺”，而是“跨源学习参数化在相同表示与预算下，比仅从目标文档/模式/探针的非学习实例化更能泛化到未见过 API 的隐藏恢复分支”。这是一个可证伪的迁移/效率主张，而非表示不可能性主张。","en":"The typed P/E/X structure itself may already suffice to express recovery semantics; therefore the credible remaining claim is not that the representation is indispensable, but that cross-source learned parameterization generalizes better to hidden recovery branches on unseen APIs than non-learned instantiation from the same target documentation, schemas, and probes, under identical representation and budget. This is a falsifiable transfer/efficiency claim, not a representational-impossibility claim."},"rationale":{"zh":"R3 指出：限探针迁移问题成立，但学习得到的类型化转移表示未与“由模式、文档与探针非学习实例化的同一类型化结构”相识别。R3.1 的最小实质修复是加入一个使用完全相同 P/E/X 表示、相同容量、相同 N 探针与相同端到端预算的非学习基线，使唯一变量为跨源学习参数化。R3.2 进一步识别出：非学习实例化规则的提取质量本身是一个混淆——若规则过弱，学习臂的胜利仅反映基线弱点而非跨源学习收益。因此 R3.2 新增预注册的规则质量验证步骤：在决定性试点之前，先在源 API（其真实状态转移与恢复语义已知）上运行固定非学习规则，确认其能产生合理的 P/E/X 字段；若规则未通过此合理性检查，则必须在预注册协议下改进，或主张相应收缩。","en":"R3 found that the bounded-probe transfer problem survives, but the learned typed transition representation is not identified against the same typed structure instantiated non-learnedly from schemas, documentation, and probes. R3.1's smallest material repair was to add a non-learned baseline using the exact same P/E/X representation, matched capacity, the same N probes, and the same end-to-end budget, so that the only varying factor is cross-source learned parameterization. R3.2 further identifies that the extraction quality of the non-learned instantiation rules is itself a confound—if the rules are weak, the learned arm wins by baseline weakness rather than cross-source learning benefit. Therefore R3.2 adds a preregistered rule-quality validation step: before the decisive pilot, run the fixed non-learned rules on source APIs (where ground-truth state transitions and recovery semantics are known) and confirm they produce reasonable P/E/X fields; if the rules fail this sanity check, they must be improved under a preregistered protocol, or the claim narrows accordingly."},"method_logic":{"zh":"两种方法均将源工作流编译为同一类型化 P/E/X 表示上的算子图，并发射目标调用与恢复边。学习臂通过跨源监督训练填充算子参数；基线臂通过固定解析/推理规则从文档、模式与探针结果填充相同字段。表示、探针预算、编译流水线与冻结协议保持恒定。R3.2 新增：在决定性试点之前，执行预注册的规则质量验证——将固定非学习规则应用于源 API（其真实状态转移与恢复语义从训练数据已知），并检查所产生的 P/E/X 字段是否达到预注册的合理性阈值。若规则未通过验证，则在预注册协议下改进规则并重新验证，或明确报告非学习实例化为弱基线并相应收缩主张。评估在隐藏故障注入下进行，比较两臂在未揭示恢复分支上的语义保持与端到端成功率。","en":"Both methods compile the source workflow into an operator graph over the same typed P/E/X representation and emit target calls plus recovery edges. The learned arm fills operator parameters via cross-source supervised training; the baseline arm fills the same fields via fixed parsing/inference rules from documentation, schemas, and probe outcomes. Representation, probe budget, compilation pipeline, and freezing protocol are held constant. R3.2 adds: before the decisive pilot, execute a preregistered rule-quality validation—apply the fixed non-learned rules to source APIs (whose ground-truth state transitions and recovery semantics are known from training data) and check whether the resulting P/E/X fields meet preregistered reasonableness thresholds. If the rules fail validation, improve them under a preregistered protocol and re-validate, or explicitly report the non-learned instantiation as a weak baseline and narrow the claim accordingly. Evaluation runs under hidden fault injections, comparing the two arms on semantic preservation of unrevealed recovery branches and end-to-end success."},"persistent_update_object":"frozen precondition-effect-error transition operator library and compiled target workflow, identical in structure for both arms, frozen after the N probes with no execution-repair loop during evaluation","learning_signal":{"zh":"学习臂：来自多个源 API 族的执行前后状态差、注入错误类别、恢复后状态，以及跨语义对应操作的转移一致性损失；在目标 API 上仅使用同样的 N 次探针。非学习臂：使用相同的探针结果与文档/模式，通过固定规则映射到 P/E/X。规则质量验证：在源 API 上，将固定规则产生的 P/E/X 字段与已知的真实状态转移和恢复语义进行比较，计算预注册的合理性指标。","en":"Learned arm: pre/post execution state differences, injected-error classes, post-recovery states, and transition-consistency losses across semantically corresponding operations from multiple source API families; on the target API only the same N probes are used. Non-learned arm: the same probe outcomes and documentation/schemas, mapped into P/E/X by fixed rules. Rule-quality validation: on source APIs, compare the P/E/X fields produced by the fixed rules against known ground-truth state transitions and recovery semantics, computing preregistered reasonableness metrics."},"independent_ground_truth":{"zh":"一个独立的测试线束，对两种方法的训练与探针选择均不可见，为每个目标 API 指定隐藏前置条件、期望副作用与故障-恢复预言机，并通过执行在未揭示的恢复分支上评估语义保持。规则质量验证使用源 API 上已知的真实状态转移与恢复语义作为独立真值，该真值对规则设计过程可见但对目标 API 评估保持隐藏。","en":"An independent test harness, excluded from training and probe selection for both arms, specifies hidden preconditions, expected effects, and fault-recovery oracles for each target API and evaluates semantic preservation on unrevealed recovery branches via execution. Rule-quality validation uses known ground-truth state transitions and recovery semantics on source APIs as independent truth, which is visible to the rule-design process but remains hidden for target API evaluation."},"strongest_baseline":{"zh":"最强简化基线：由相同文档、模式与 N 次探针非学习实例化的同构 P/E/X 类型化转移算子，容量匹配，编译流水线与端到端预算相同，N 次探针后同样冻结。该基线的固定规则必须通过预注册的规则质量验证：在源 API（其真实状态转移与恢复语义已知）上运行，确认所产生的 P/E/X 字段达到预注册的合理性阈值。若规则未通过验证，则在预注册协议下改进并重新验证，或明确报告为弱基线。附加对照：使用相同文档、模式、N 探针、token 与调用的直接 LLM 工作流改写，加相同的有界执行-修复预算；以及经由固定手工设计通用 IR 的编译。","en":"Strongest simplification: the identically-structured P/E/X typed transition operator instantiated non-learnedly from the same documentation, schemas, and N probes, with matched capacity, the same compilation pipeline and end-to-end budget, and likewise frozen after N probes. The fixed rules of this baseline must pass preregistered rule-quality validation: run on source APIs (whose ground-truth state transitions and recovery semantics are known) and confirm the resulting P/E/X fields meet preregistered reasonableness thresholds. If the rules fail validation, improve them under a preregistered protocol and re-validate, or explicitly report as a weak baseline. Additional controls: direct LLM workflow rewriting with the same documentation, schemas, N probes, tokens, and calls plus the same bounded execution-repair budget; and compilation through a fixed hand-designed general IR."},"matched_resources":["identical source/target documentation and schemas","identical N actively selected target probes (same probe selection policy inputs)","identical P/E/X representational capacity and operator-graph compilation pipeline","identical tokens and model calls for any LLM components","identical model capacity, optimizer, minibatches, and training steps for the learned arm's fitting budget accounted against the baseline's instantiation budget","identical frozen-after-N-probes protocol with no test-time relearning","identical bounded execution-repair budget where applicable","identical wall-clock budget for probe execution and evaluation","identical hidden fault-injection suite and evaluation endpoints","preregistered rule-quality validation on source APIs with known ground-truth state transitions and recovery semantics, applied to the fixed non-learned P/E/X extraction rules before the decisive pilot"],"decisive_pilot":{"zh":"预注册 2×2 交叉析因实验：{跨源学习 P/E/X 参数化, 非学习模式实例化 P/E/X} × {未见过 API 族 A, 未见过 API 族 B}。迁移包含正常路径与多条恢复分支的小型工作流。每个方法获得完全相同的文档、模式、N 次目标探针、token、调用与修复预算；N 次探针后全部冻结。在交叉析因实验之前，执行预注册的规则质量验证：将固定非学习规则应用于源 API（其真实状态转移与恢复语义已知），确认所产生的 P/E/X 字段在预注册指标上达到合理性阈值。若规则未通过验证，则在预注册协议下改进规则并重新验证，或明确报告非学习实例化为弱基线并相应收缩主张。独立隐藏线束在隐藏故障注入下评估恢复分支语义保持与端到端成功率。仅当学习臂在相同预算下显著提升隐藏恢复分支语义保持，且该增益在第二个 API 族上复现时，机制主张才存活。","en":"A single preregistered 2×2 crossed factorial: {cross-source learned P/E/X parameterization, non-learned schema-instantiated P/E/X} × {unseen API family A, unseen API family B}. Migrate small workflows containing normal paths and multiple recovery branches. Every method receives identical documentation, schemas, N target probes, tokens, calls, and repair budget; everything is frozen after N probes. Before the crossed factorial, execute preregistered rule-quality validation: apply the fixed non-learned rules to source APIs (whose ground-truth state transitions and recovery semantics are known) and confirm the resulting P/E/X fields meet preregistered reasonableness thresholds on preregistered metrics. If the rules fail validation, improve them under a preregistered protocol and re-validate, or explicitly report the non-learned instantiation as a weak baseline and narrow the claim accordingly. The independent hidden harness evaluates recovery-branch semantic preservation and end-to-end success under hidden fault injections. The mechanism claim survives only if the learned arm significantly improves hidden recovery-branch semantic preservation at equal budget and the gain replicates on the second API family."},"stop_condition":{"zh":"若跨源学习的 P/E/X 算子在相同 N 探针、调用与修复预算下未显著优于由相同文档/模式/探针非学习实例化的同构 P/E/X 算子，或优势仅出现在两种方法本已成功的正常路径上，或优势在第二个未见过 API 族上消失，则终止该机制主张；此时想法收缩为在文档稀疏或歧义情形下的样本效率/鲁棒性主张。此外，若非学习实例化规则未通过预注册的规则质量验证（即在源 API 上产生的 P/E/X 字段未达到预注册合理性阈值），且无法在预注册协议下改进至通过验证，则机制主张同样终止；此时必须明确报告非学习实例化为弱基线，主张收缩为“跨源学习参数化优于当前最佳非学习规则”的相对主张，而非“跨源学习参数化优于同构非学习实例化”的识别性主张。","en":"Terminate the mechanism claim if the cross-source learned P/E/X operator does not significantly outperform the identically-structured non-learned P/E/X instantiation under identical N-probe, call, and repair budgets, or if the advantage is confined to normal-path success where both methods already succeed, or if the advantage disappears on the second unseen API family; in that case the idea collapses to a sample-efficiency/robustness claim under sparse or ambiguous documentation. Additionally, if the non-learned instantiation rules fail preregistered rule-quality validation (i.e., the P/E/X fields produced on source APIs do not meet preregistered reasonableness thresholds) and cannot be improved to pass validation under a preregistered protocol, the mechanism claim is likewise terminated; in that case it must be explicitly reported that the non-learned instantiation is a weak baseline, and the claim narrows to a relative claim that 'cross-source learned parameterization outperforms the current best non-learned rules' rather than the identifying claim that 'cross-source learned parameterization outperforms identically-structured non-learned instantiation.'"},"surviving_claim":{"zh":"在相同类型化表示与相同探针/调用/修复预算下，跨源学习的 P/E/X 参数化相比由相同文档、模式与探针非学习实例化的同构表示，能在未见过目标 API 上严格更好地保持隐藏恢复分支语义，且该增益跨 API 族复现。该主张仅在非学习实例化规则通过预注册的规则质量验证（即在源 API 上产生的 P/E/X 字段达到预注册合理性阈值）后成立。这是一个可证伪的迁移/效率主张，而非表示不可能性主张——基线能够表达相同的算子。","en":"Under the identical typed representation and identical probe/call/repair budgets, cross-source learned parameterization of P/E/X yields strictly better hidden recovery-branch semantic preservation on unseen target APIs than the identically-structured representation instantiated non-learnedly from the same documentation, schemas, and probes, and the gain replicates across API families. This claim holds only after the non-learned instantiation rules pass preregistered rule-quality validation (i.e., the P/E/X fields produced on source APIs meet preregistered reasonableness thresholds). This is a falsifiable transfer/efficiency claim, not a representational-impossibility claim—the baseline can express the same operators."},"collision_boundary":{"zh":"与 Agent-First Tool API 的区别：该工作使恢复语义在面向智能体的语义接口中显式化，但并不从有界目标探针中学习迁移算子；本想法的核心是比较跨源学习参数化与同构非学习实例化。与 ProEvolve 的区别：该工作以类型化关系图表示版本关联的工具/模式演化，但它是基准生成框架而非限探针迁移学习器。不主张这些文献不存在或未覆盖相关问题，仅主张本想法的识别性比较（学习 vs 同构非学习、限探针、隐藏恢复分支评估）未被其直接覆盖。","en":"Difference from Agent-First Tool API: that work makes recovery semantics explicit in an agent-oriented semantic interface but does not learn migration operators from bounded target probes; this idea's core is comparing cross-source learned parameterization against an identically-structured non-learned instantiation. Difference from ProEvolve: that work represents version-linked tool/schema evolution with typed relational graphs but is a benchmark-generation framework rather than a bounded-probe migration learner. We do not claim this literature does not exist or fails to cover related problems, only that the identifying comparison here (learned vs. identically-structured non-learned, bounded probes, hidden recovery-branch evaluation) is not directly covered by it."},"r3_repair_summary":{"zh":"R3 认定学习得到的类型化表示未与“同一类型化结构的非学习实例化”相识别。R3.1 修复：新增一个使用完全相同 P/E/X 表示、相同容量、相同 N 探针与相同端到端预算的非学习基线，两臂仅在参数来源（跨源学习 vs 固定规则实例化）上不同；评估由独立隐藏线束在未揭示恢复分支上执行；决定性实验为预注册 2×2 交叉析因。R3.2 进一步修复：识别出非学习实例化规则的提取质量是残余混淆——若规则过弱，学习臂的胜利仅反映基线弱点。因此新增预注册的规则质量验证步骤：在决定性试点之前，在源 API（其真实状态转移与恢复语义已知）上运行固定非学习规则，确认所产生的 P/E/X 字段达到预注册合理性阈值；若规则未通过验证，则在预注册协议下改进并重新验证，或明确报告为弱基线并相应收缩主张。由此任何剩余优势必须来自跨源学习参数化而非表示结构本身或基线弱点。","en":"R3 found the learned typed representation unidentified against the same typed structure instantiated non-learnedly. R3.1 repair: add a non-learned baseline using the exact same P/E/X representation, matched capacity, the same N probes, and the same end-to-end budget, so the arms differ only in parameter provenance (cross-source learning vs. fixed-rule instantiation); evaluation is executed by an independent hidden harness on unrevealed recovery branches; the decisive test is a preregistered 2×2 crossed factorial. R3.2 further repair: identify that the extraction quality of the non-learned instantiation rules is a residual confound—if the rules are weak, the learned arm wins by baseline weakness. Therefore add a preregistered rule-quality validation step: before the decisive pilot, run the fixed non-learned rules on source APIs (whose ground-truth state transitions and recovery semantics are known) and confirm the resulting P/E/X fields meet preregistered reasonableness thresholds; if the rules fail validation, improve them under a preregistered protocol and re-validate, or explicitly report as a weak baseline and narrow the claim accordingly. Any remaining advantage must therefore come from cross-source learned parameterization rather than the representational structure itself or baseline weakness."},"remaining_risk":{"zh":"若目标 API 文档/模式异常完整，非学习实例化可能匹配学习算子，使主张收缩为文档稀疏或歧义情形；试点应将文档完整性作为调节变量报告。此外，尽管规则质量验证降低了基线弱点风险，但源 API 上的规则质量可能不完全迁移到目标 API 的文档风格或结构；试点应报告规则在源 API 上的验证指标作为基线质量的代理，并在目标 API 上报告规则提取的置信度或覆盖率指标。","en":"If target API documentation/schemas are unusually complete, the non-learned instantiation may match the learned operator, narrowing the claim to sparse or ambiguous documentation settings; the pilot should report documentation completeness as a moderator. Additionally, although rule-quality validation reduces the risk of baseline weakness, rule quality on source APIs may not fully transfer to target APIs with different documentation styles or structures; the pilot should report rule-validation metrics on source APIs as a proxy for baseline quality and report rule-extraction confidence or coverage metrics on target APIs."}},{"idea_id":"interventional-permission-triage-under-ceiling","revision":"R3.1","title":{"zh":"固定权限上限下的干预式重授权筛选：冻结租约门控 vs 确定性迁移包络","en":"Interventional Reauthorization Triage Under a Fixed Ceiling: Frozen Lease Gating vs. Deterministic Transition Envelope"},"purpose":{"zh":"在代理更新后，全量重授权成本高昂，而声明式差异可能遗漏那些表面未变但可达行为已改变的权限。目标是在绝不扩大现有权限上限的前提下，减少重授权工作量。","en":"After an agent update, full reauthorization is costly, while declared diffs can miss permissions whose reachable behavior changed despite an unchanged surface. The goal is to reduce reauthorization work without ever expanding the existing authority ceiling."},"importance":{"zh":"代理在持续演化中频繁更新，每次更新后对所有既有授权进行人工或金丝雀重授权会迅速成为运维瓶颈。一个能在固定上限下安全缩小重授权范围的机制，可显著降低安全运维成本，同时保持最小权限原则。","en":"Agents evolve continuously, and reauthorizing every existing grant after each update quickly becomes an operational bottleneck. A mechanism that safely narrows the reauthorization scope under a fixed ceiling can substantially reduce security-operations cost while preserving least privilege."},"core_idea":{"zh":"对每个代理突变，计算提示、记忆、技能、工作流和依赖的结构化差异，并为每个既有授权生成差异-权限特征。在训练环境中，随机启用、禁用或限制单个权限，同时运行生成与评分均独立于风险模型的任务和金丝雀；这些干预标记该权限在该突变下是否产生新的越权或越上限效果。学习 q(diff, permission)，即新诱发风险的概率。部署时，首先强制执行不可变的效果上限；所有新请求的权限遵循普通授权流程。对于仍在上限内的既有授权，仅当 q 超过保守阈值时，才将其标记为需金丝雀重授权，且在该授权被清除前禁止执行。未被选中的授权最多保留原有权限，绝不可升级。筛选决策被持久化到下一版本的租约状态中，并在执行时冻结。","en":"For each agent mutation, compute structured diffs over prompt, memory, skills, workflows, and dependencies and form diff-permission features for every existing grant. In training environments, randomly enable, disable, or restrict individual permissions while running tasks and canaries whose generation and scoring are independent of the risk model; these interventions label whether the permission creates a newly unauthorized or out-of-ceiling effect under that mutation. Learn q(diff, permission), the probability of newly induced risk. At deployment, first enforce an immutable effect ceiling; all newly requested authority follows ordinary authorization. Among existing grants still within the ceiling, only permissions whose q exceeds a conservative threshold are marked for canary reauthorization and cannot execute until cleared. Unselected grants can at most retain prior authority and can never be upgraded. The triage decision is persisted in the next version's lease state and frozen for execution."},"core_intuition":{"zh":"代码或配置层面的差异并不总是导致可达行为的变化；干预式训练可以识别那些尽管存在代码差异但可达效果集未变的授权，从而避免不必要的重授权。","en":"Code- or configuration-level diffs do not always imply changes in reachable behavior; interventional training can identify grants whose reachable-effect set is unchanged despite code-level diffs, thereby avoiding unnecessary reauthorization."},"rationale":{"zh":"通过将学习到的筛选决策冻结为执行时实际查询的租约字段，q 不再是仅用于评估的旁路指标，而是直接控制执行路径。与确定性迁移包络基线共享相同的突变表示、金丝雀库和重授权预算，可以隔离出干预训练相对于静态可达性分析的附加价值。","en":"By freezing the learned triage decision as a lease field that execution actually consults, q is no longer an evaluation-only side metric but directly governs the execution path. Sharing identical mutation representation, canary library, and reauthorization budget with the deterministic transition-envelope baseline isolates the added value of interventional training over static reachability analysis."},"method_logic":{"zh":"两个分支均强制执行不可变效果上限，并将新请求的权限路由至普通授权。对于上限内的既有授权，学习分支仅对冻结 q 超过保守阈值的权限进行重授权；确定性分支仅对声明清单、可达效果集或依赖图发生变化的权限进行重授权。两个分支的选中子集均被持久化到租约中并在执行时冻结。","en":"Both arms enforce the immutable effect ceiling and route newly requested authority through ordinary authorization. For existing grants within the ceiling, the learned arm reauthorizes only permissions whose frozen q exceeds a conservative threshold; the deterministic arm reauthorizes only permissions whose declared manifest, reachable-effect set, or dependency graph changed. The selected subset is persisted in the lease and frozen for execution in both arms."},"persistent_update_object":"versioned permission lease with frozen intervention-trained reauthorization triage, where each grant's lease field gates execution (allow vs. require canary reauthorization)","learning_signal":{"zh":"在训练环境中进行随机化的权限启用/禁用/限制干预，由独立的金丝雀和环境日志判定实现的效果差异，从而监督突变-权限对是否产生新诱发风险。","en":"Randomized permission enable/disable/restriction interventions in training environments, with realized effect differences judged by independent canaries and environment logs, supervise whether a mutation-permission pair creates newly induced risk."},"independent_ground_truth":{"zh":"独立的安全测试平台使用实现的外部效果日志和固定权限上限来判定未授权效果；金丝雀的生成、评分和效果裁定均不使用 q 或确定性包络。","en":"An independent safety harness uses realized external-effect logs and the fixed authority ceiling to determine unauthorized effects; canary generation, scoring, and effect adjudication do not use q or the deterministic envelope."},"strongest_baseline":{"zh":"确定性固定上限迁移包络/租约筛选：仅对声明清单、可达效果集或依赖图发生变化的权限进行重授权，使用相同的突变表示、金丝雀、标签、调用次数和预算；同时以 Progent 式动态策略和全量重授权作为参考。","en":"Deterministic fixed-ceiling transition-envelope/lease triage that reauthorizes only permissions whose declared manifest, reachable-effect set, or dependency graph changed, using identical mutation representation, canaries, labels, calls, and budget; Progent-style dynamic policies and full reauthorization serve as references."},"matched_resources":["identical structured diffs over prompt, memory, skills, workflows, and dependencies","identical canary library and scoring","identical intervention-derived labels and environment logs","identical LLM calls, tokens, and wall-clock","identical reauthorization budget","identical independent safety harness","identical authority ceiling","identical optimizer/minibatches/steps for any learned components"],"decisive_pilot":{"zh":"在公开的代理/工具沙箱中，使用训练突变算子从随机化权限干预中训练 q；在完全未见过的测试算子（语义等价提示重写、记忆注入、技能实现替换、间接依赖变更）上评估。交叉设计 {筛选机制} × {突变算子族}，所有方法使用相同的突变表示、金丝雀、标签、调用次数和重授权预算。主要终点：每版本需重授权的权限/金丝雀数量；安全约束：零未授权实现效果，或不超过预注册的全量重授权上限，由独立测试平台裁定。","en":"In a public agent/tool sandbox, train q from randomized permission interventions on training mutation operators; test on completely unseen operators (semantically equivalent prompt rewrites, memory injections, skill implementation swaps, indirect dependency changes). Cross {triage mechanism} × {mutation-operator family} with identical mutation representation, canaries, labels, calls, and reauthorization budget. Primary endpoint: permissions/canaries reauthorized per version; safety constraint: zero unauthorized realized effects or no increase beyond the preregistered full-reauthorization bound, adjudicated by the independent harness."},"stop_condition":{"zh":"如果学习到的筛选在未见过的突变算子上无法相对于确定性固定上限迁移包络/租约筛选减少重授权工作量，或者任何节省导致未授权实现效果增加，则停止。","en":"Stop if learned triage cannot reduce reauthorization work relative to deterministic fixed-ceiling transition-envelope/lease triage on unseen mutation operators, or if any savings increase unauthorized realized effects."},"surviving_claim":{"zh":"在固定上限下，一个冻结的、执行相关的学习筛选租约，相比资源相同的确定性迁移包络租约，能在未见过的突变算子上显著减少每版本重授权数量，且不增加未授权实现效果；这是一个效率主张，而非声称确定性包络无法表达相同的划分。","en":"A frozen, execution-relevant learned triage lease materially reduces per-version reauthorization on unseen mutation operators compared with an equally resourced deterministic transition-envelope lease, without increasing unauthorized realized effects; this is an efficiency claim under a fixed ceiling, not a claim that the deterministic envelope cannot express the same partition."},"collision_boundary":{"zh":"Progent 在工具调用时执行确定性的符号化最小权限控制，而非突变条件下的重授权筛选。信息流控制方法在运行时执行确定性的信息流策略，而非更新后的授权筛选。AuthBench 关注权限边界推断和授权分解，而非更新后的授权租约筛选。","en":"Progent enforces deterministic symbolic least-privilege at tool-call time, not mutation-conditioned reauthorization triage. Information-flow control methods enforce deterministic runtime policies, not post-update grant triage. AuthBench addresses permission-boundary inference and authorization decomposition, not post-update lease triage."},"r3_repair_summary":{"zh":"通过将 q 的冻结输出写入执行时实际查询的租约状态，使其具有执行相关性；同时新增确定性固定上限迁移包络/租约筛选基线，该基线使用相同的突变表示、金丝雀、标签、调用次数和重授权预算，从而直接检验干预训练相对于静态可达性分析的附加价值。","en":"Made q's frozen output execution-relevant by writing the triage decision into the lease state that execution actually consults, and added a deterministic fixed-ceiling transition-envelope/lease triage baseline using identical mutation representation, canaries, labels, calls, and reauthorization budget, thereby directly testing the added value of interventional training over static reachability analysis."},"remaining_risk":{"zh":"如果未见过的突变算子产生的差异特征与训练分布相差甚远，q 可能校准不良；保守阈值和冻结租约可缓解此风险，但任何越权增加都会触发停止条件。","en":"If unseen mutation operators produce diff features far from the training distribution, q may miscalibrate; conservative thresholding and the frozen lease mitigate this, but any increase in overreach triggers the stop condition."}},{"idea_id":"nested-pathway-memory-repair","revision":"R3.1","title":{"zh":"嵌套路径识别记忆修复","en":"Nested-Pathway Memory Repair"},"purpose":{"zh":"解决记忆复用后失败的归因与修复问题：失败可能源于某条记忆是否被检索、其内容、其排序位置，或它与共检索记忆的交互。将这些机制压缩为二元“有害”标签会误删有用内容或修错对象。本方法旨在识别具体致害路径并施加最小持久修复。","en":"Address attribution and repair of failures after memory reuse: a failure may arise from whether an item is retrieved, its content, its rank, or its interaction with co-retrieved memories. Collapsing these mechanisms into a binary harmful label can delete useful content or repair the wrong object. The method aims to identify the specific harm pathway and apply a minimal persistent repair."},"importance":{"zh":"长期智能体依赖持久记忆，但复用记忆可能造成持续的下游行为扭曲。若不能区分检索、内容、排序与共检索交互四类机制，修复策略会过度删除（损失无害记忆的效用）或修复不足（残留致害路径）。机制特异的持久修复能在恢复任务成功率的同时保留无害记忆效用，对可靠的长期记忆智能体具有直接价值。","en":"Long-horizon agents rely on persistent memory, but reused memories can cause persistent downstream behavioral distortion. Without distinguishing retrieval, content, rank, and co-retrieval interaction mechanisms, repair policies either over-delete (losing harmless memory utility) or under-repair (leaving the harm pathway intact). Mechanism-specific persistent repair can recover task success while retaining harmless memory utility, which is directly valuable for reliable long-horizon memory agents."},"core_idea":{"zh":"预注册一个嵌套结构因果模型：先随机化目标记忆是否进入检索集 R；仅当 R=1 时，在原始、无害化与匹配对照变体之间随机化内容 C；在内容存在条件下随机化排序桶 K；在同一 K 内随机化指定共记忆 G 是否出现。这些有效干预估计四个可识别量：检索效应、内容中介效应、排序中介效应与共检索交互。估计值及不确定性映射到最小持久动作集（排除、改写、限位、互斥分组），实际修改记忆库内容或元数据。估计器与修复策略在训练后冻结并复用于未来 episode。显式路径分解仅在优于获得相同结构标签与生成器元数据的直接修复学习器时才成立。","en":"Preregister a nested SCM: first randomize whether the target memory enters the retrieved set R; only when R=1, randomize content C among original, neutralized, and matched-control variants; conditional on content being present, randomize a rank bucket K; within the same K, randomize the presence of a designated co-memory G. These valid interventions estimate four identifiable quantities: retrieval effect, content-mediated effect, rank-mediated effect, and co-retrieval interaction. The estimates and their uncertainty map to a minimal persistent action set (exclude, rewrite, rank-cap, mutex-group) that modifies actual memory-store content or metadata. The estimator and repair policy are frozen after training and reused for future episodes. The explicit pathway decomposition is claimed only insofar as it beats a direct repair learner given the same structural labels and generator metadata."},"core_intuition":{"zh":"直觉：不同致害路径需要不同修复——检索问题用排除、内容问题用改写、排序问题用限位、交互问题用互斥分组。显式估计四条路径的中介量，相当于给修复策略施加因果结构归纳偏置，可能比直接把特征映射到动作的通用策略在未见生成器参数下泛化更好、或用更少干预达到同等修复质量。但若一个获得相同结构标签作为普通特征的直接 bandit 就能匹配其表现，则显式分解并非必要。","en":"Intuition: different harm pathways need different repairs—exclusion for retrieval, rewriting for content, rank-caps for rank, mutex-groups for interaction. Explicitly estimating the four mediation quantities imposes a causal-structure inductive bias on the repair policy, which may generalize better to unseen generator parameters or need fewer interventions than a generic feature-to-action policy. But if a direct bandit given the same structural labels as ordinary features matches it, the explicit decomposition is unnecessary."},"rationale":{"zh":"R3 指出：嵌套干预设计有效，但除非显式路径分解能优于获得相同结构路径标签与生成器元数据的直接修复学习器，否则分解并非必要。因此本版将直接 bandit 基线升级为获得相同结构标签与元数据作为普通输入特征（无显式路径estimand），使任何残余优势只能归因于显式中介estimand与因果结构，而非信息不对称。存活主张被收窄为可证伪的归纳偏置/效率主张。","en":"R3 held that the nested intervention design is valid, but explicit pathway decomposition is unnecessary unless it beats a direct repair learner with the same structural pathway labels and generator metadata. This version therefore upgrades the direct bandit baseline to receive the same structural labels and metadata as ordinary input features (without explicit pathway estimands), so any remaining advantage is attributable to the explicit mediation estimands and causal structure rather than information asymmetry. The surviving claim is narrowed to a falsifiable inductive-bias/efficiency claim."},"method_logic":{"zh":"两种方法观测完全相同的嵌套干预/上下文/动作元组以及相同的结构路径标签与生成器元数据。分解方法估计检索、内容中介、排序中介与共检索交互四类效应，并连同不确定性映射到最小修复动作；bandit 将相同特征（含结构标签与元数据作为普通特征）直接映射到同一动作集（排除、改写、限位、互斥分组），不显式估计任何中介量。两者在留出评估前均冻结所得修复策略，在未来复用 episode 上无再学习地复用。比较在未见生成器参数下的留出修复增益、无害记忆效用保留与干预样本效率曲线。","en":"Both methods observe exactly the same nested intervention/context/action tuples and the same structural pathway labels and generator metadata. The decomposition method estimates retrieval, content-mediated, rank-mediated, and co-retrieval interaction effects and maps them with uncertainty to minimal repair actions; the bandit maps the same features (including structural labels and metadata as ordinary features) directly to the same action set (exclude, rewrite, rank-cap, mutex-group) without estimating any mediation quantity. Both freeze the resulting repair policy before held-out evaluation and reuse it without relearning on future episodes. Comparison is on held-out repair gain, retention of harmless memory utility, and intervention sample-efficiency curves under unseen generator parameters."},"persistent_update_object":"frozen pathway-conditioned memory content and retrieval-metadata repair policy (exclude, rewrite, rank-cap, mutex-group) applied to the actual memory store, fitted before held-out evaluation, frozen, and reused on future episodes without test-time relearning","learning_signal":{"zh":"任务成功率、违规/错误事件，以及嵌套随机干预下的下游行为差异；两种方法额外获得相同的结构路径标签与生成器元数据——bandit 作为普通输入特征，分解方法作为estimand目标。","en":"Task success, violation/error events, and downstream behavioral differences under nested randomized interventions; both methods additionally receive the same structural pathway labels and generator metadata—the bandit as ordinary input features, the decomposition method as estimand targets."},"independent_ground_truth":{"zh":"训练期间，独立的合成/半合成记忆生成器记录真实结构致害路径。最终评估在未参与路径标注或特征抽取的未来复用 episode 上，以程序化方式（执行结果与任务校验，非学习得到的评判器）度量修复增益与附带效用。","en":"During training, an independent synthetic/semisynthetic memory generator records the actual structural harm pathway. Final evaluation measures repair gain and collateral utility programmatically (execution outcomes and task checkers, not a learned judge) on future reuse episodes not involved in pathway labeling or feature extraction."},"strongest_baseline":{"zh":"在完全相同的嵌套干预/上下文/动作元组上训练的上下文 bandit，并以相同的结构路径标签与生成器元数据作为普通输入特征，在排除、改写、限位、互斥分组中选择动作，不显式估计任何中介路径estimand。","en":"A contextual bandit trained on exactly the same nested intervention/context/action tuples, with the same structural pathway labels and generator metadata as ordinary input features, choosing among exclude, rewrite, rank-cap, and mutex-group without explicitly estimating any mediation pathway estimand."},"matched_resources":["identical nested intervention/context/action tuples","identical structural pathway labels and generator metadata (bandit: ordinary features; decomposition: estimand targets)","identical action set (exclude, rewrite, rank-cap, mutex-group)","identical number of interventions / intervention budget","identical model capacity, LLM calls, and token budget","identical optimizer, minibatches, and training steps","identical wall-clock budget","identical frozen evaluation protocol on the same future-reuse episodes"],"decisive_pilot":{"zh":"单一预注册交叉检验：{修复学习器：嵌套路径 SCM 分解 vs 带结构标签与元数据特征的直接上下文 bandit} × {机制设置：四个单机制致害 + 两个混合机制} × {未见生成器参数}。使用带可控记忆封装的公开智能体基准生成半合成 episode，所有方法干预次数固定。在冻结修复策略后，比较未来复用任务恢复率、无害记忆效用保留与干预样本效率曲线。判定性结果要求：在相同干预数下获得更高留出修复增益，或以显著更少干预达到同等修复质量。","en":"A single preregistered crossed test: {repair learner: nested-pathway SCM decomposition vs. direct contextual bandit with structural-label-and-metadata features} × {mechanism setting: four single-mechanism harms + two mixed-mechanism settings} × {unseen generator parameters}. Use a public agent benchmark with a controllable memory wrapper to generate semisynthetic episodes with a fixed intervention count for all methods. After freezing repair policies, compare future-reuse task recovery, retention of harmless memory utility, and intervention sample-efficiency curves. The decisive result requires either better held-out repair gain at the same intervention count or materially fewer interventions to reach the same repair quality."},"stop_condition":{"zh":"若出现以下任一情况即终止或坍缩主张：(1) 路径分解无法恢复独立路径真值；(2) 获得相同干预数据、结构标签与元数据特征的直接上下文 bandit 在未见生成器参数上的未来复用修复增益与干预样本效率与分解方法持平——此时显式分解必要性被证伪，主张坍缩为 bandit 等价结果或被放弃。","en":"Terminate or collapse the claim if either: (1) the pathway decomposition cannot recover independent pathway ground truth; or (2) the direct contextual bandit with identical intervention data and structural-label/metadata features matches the decomposition in future-reuse repair gain and intervention sample efficiency on unseen generator parameters—in which case decomposition necessity is falsified and the claim collapses to the bandit-equivalent result or is abandoned."},"surviving_claim":{"zh":"显式嵌套路径分解通过施加因果结构归纳偏置，在相同干预数下比获得相同结构标签与元数据作为普通特征的直接修复学习器取得更高留出修复增益，或以显著更少干预达到同等修复质量；若被持平，则分解必要性被证伪。","en":"Explicit nested pathway decomposition, by imposing a causal-structure inductive bias, achieves better held-out repair gain at equal intervention count, or materially fewer interventions for equal repair quality, than a direct repair learner given the same structural labels and metadata as ordinary features; matching performance falsifies decomposition necessity."},"collision_boundary":{"zh":"与最近工作的边界：Causal Intervention-Based Memory Selection 通过受控干预估计候选记忆是否有害并抑制之，但不区分检索/内容/排序/共检索交互路径，也不做机制特异修复；Memory-Induced Tool-Drift 记录检索记忆导致的持续下游行为扭曲，但不提供干预式路径归因或修复；ActMem 使用结构化因果表示与反事实推理做智能体记忆，但未做随机化嵌套路径识别后接机制特异持久修复。本方法的差异点仅在显式路径estimand，且仅在优于获得相同结构标签的直接 bandit 时成立。","en":"Boundary with nearest work: Causal Intervention-Based Memory Selection estimates via controlled interventions whether candidate memories help or harm and suppresses harmful ones, but does not distinguish retrieval/content/rank/co-retrieval pathways or apply mechanism-specific repair; Memory-Induced Tool-Drift documents persistent downstream distortion from retrieved memories but provides no interventional pathway attribution or repair; ActMem uses structured causal representations and counterfactual reasoning for agent memory, but not randomized nested pathway identification followed by mechanism-specific persistent repair. The present difference lies only in the explicit pathway estimands, and holds only insofar as it beats a direct bandit given the same structural labels."},"r3_repair_summary":{"zh":"按 R3 要求，将直接修复 bandit 基线升级为获得与分解方法完全相同的结构路径标签与生成器元数据（作为普通输入特征，无显式路径estimand），并保持干预元组、动作集、干预预算、模型容量、调用/token、优化器/步数、wall-clock 与冻结评估协议完全一致。由此消除信息不对称，使任何残余优势只能归因于显式中介estimand；若 bandit 持平则分解必要性被证伪。","en":"Per R3, the direct-repair bandit baseline is upgraded to receive exactly the same structural pathway labels and generator metadata as the decomposition method (as ordinary input features, without explicit pathway estimands), with identical intervention tuples, action set, intervention budget, model capacity, calls/tokens, optimizer/steps, wall-clock, and frozen evaluation protocol. This removes information asymmetry so any remaining advantage is attributable only to the explicit mediation estimands; if the bandit matches, decomposition necessity is falsified."},"remaining_risk":{"zh":"带结构特征的 bandit 可能隐式学到相同因果结构，使显式分解无增益；此外结构标签在半合成设置之外可能有噪声或获取成本高，分解优势未必迁移到真实标签质量场景——试点需记录标签质量依赖性。","en":"The bandit with structural features may implicitly learn the same causal structure, nullifying the decomposition's advantage; moreover, structural labels may be noisy or costly outside semisynthetic settings, so the decomposition's edge may not transfer to realistic label-quality regimes—the pilot should record label-quality dependence."}},{"idea_id":"constraint-complete-typed-memory-order-logic","revision":"R3.1","title":{"zh":"约束完备型类型化记忆顺序逻辑：表征 × 解码器分解","en":"Constraint-Complete Typed Memory-Order Logic: Representation × Decoder Factorization"},"purpose":{"zh":"解决智能体记忆检索中的真实问题：当多个类型化记忆（异常、策略、安全约束、工具模式、观察）被共同检索时，其合法执行顺序取决于高阶、上下文相关的约束，而非简单成对偏好。目标是判断一种持久化的符号约束表征能否在未见过的类型组合上实现系统性泛化，以及编译后的免搜索解码能否在保持精度的同时降低推理成本。","en":"Addresses the real problem of ordering co-retrieved typed memories (exceptions, policies, safety constraints, tool schemas, observations) in agents, where legal execution order depends on higher-order, context-dependent constraints rather than simple pairwise preferences. The goal is to determine whether a persistent symbolic constraint representation yields systematic generalization to unseen type compositions, and whether a compiled search-free decoder preserves accuracy at lower inference cost."},"importance":{"zh":"记忆增强智能体在组合多个检索到的记忆时，顺序错误会导致硬约束违反（如安全检查被观察隔开、异常处理先于策略加载）。若符号约束表征在同等表达力的神经表征下仍展现出可证伪的组合外推优势，或编译解码在同等精度下严格降低推理成本，这将为智能体自我演化中的持久记忆结构设计提供可复用的证据。","en":"Memory-augmented agents that compose multiple retrieved memories can violate hard constraints through ordering errors (e.g., an observation interposed between a safety rule and a tool schema, or an exception handled before its policy loads). If a symbolic constraint representation shows a falsifiable compositional-extrapolation advantage over an equally expressive neural representation under an identical decoder, or if compilation strictly reduces inference cost at equal accuracy, this provides reusable evidence for designing persistent memory structures in agent self-evolution."},"core_idea":{"zh":"保留来源/函数定义的记忆类型与随机置换干预，但将机制重构为预注册的 2×2 表征 × 解码器析因设计。表征因子：(a) 由 MDL 式子句选择诱导的最小符号约束程序（类型化变量、条件反转与交换性子句）；(b) 在相同类型化变量、共现统计与元数覆盖上定义的匹配类型化 n 元因子模型。解码器因子：(i) 测试时精确约束求解器；(ii) 训练后一次性编译并冻结的免搜索解码器（对完整类型化集合的编译策略/查找，无测试时求解）。四个单元共享全部数据、容量与预算。","en":"Retain provenance/function-defined memory types and randomized permutation interventions, but restructure the mechanism as a preregistered 2×2 representation × decoder factorial. Representation factor: (a) a minimal symbolic constraint program induced by MDL-style clause selection (typed variables, conditional-reversal and commutativity clauses); (b) a matched typed n-ary factor model defined over the same typed variables, co-occurrence statistics, and arity coverage. Decoder factor: (i) an exact test-time constraint solver; (ii) a frozen search-free decoder compiled once after training (compiled policy/lookup over complete typed sets, no test-time solving). All four cells share all data, capacity, and budgets."},"core_intuition":{"zh":"R3 指出的混淆在于：符号表征的持久性并不意味着免搜索行为——精确求解仍在测试时重算。将表征与解码器正交化后，可以分别检验两个可证伪命题：符号子句是否在相同解码器下比同等表达力的 n 元因子更好地外推到新类型组合（归纳偏置命题）；编译解码器是否在不损失精度的前提下严格降低推理成本（效率命题）。由于 n 元因子模型在原理上可以表达相同的高阶约束，本方案不作表征不可能性断言，只作可被实验杀死的偏置/效率断言。","en":"R3 flagged a conflation: persistence of a symbolic representation does not imply search-free behavior, since exact solving is still recomputed at test time. Orthogonalizing representation and decoder allows two separately falsifiable claims: whether symbolic clauses extrapolate better to new type compositions than equally expressive n-ary factors under an identical decoder (inductive-bias claim), and whether the compiled decoder strictly reduces inference cost without accuracy loss (efficiency claim). Because the n-ary factor model can in principle express the same higher-order constraints, no representational-impossibility claim is made—only bias/efficiency claims that experiments can kill."},"rationale":{"zh":"原始版本把符号子句注册表与精确求解器绑定，导致无法区分优势来自表征形式还是解码器形式，且缺少共享解码器的匹配 n 元因子控制。2×2 设计是关闭该边界的最小物质修复：它只增加一个共享求解器的 n 元因子单元与两个编译单元，不引入额外数据、标签或容量差异。","en":"The original version bound the symbolic clause registry to the exact solver, making it impossible to distinguish whether any advantage comes from the representational form or the decoder, and lacked a matched n-ary factor control sharing the decoder. The 2×2 design is the smallest material repair closing this boundary: it adds only an n-ary factor cell sharing the solver and two compiled cells, introducing no extra data, labels, or capacity differences."},"method_logic":{"zh":"训练阶段：对每个训练共检索集合，随机化或系统枚举充分多的置换并独立评估，得到置换-结果数据。符号单元用 MDL 式子句选择保留解释多个独立训练组合的子句；n 元单元在相同类型化变量与元数覆盖上训练因子，参数/子句容量与正则化预算与子句稀疏度匹配。编译阶段（训练后一次性）：将符号子句与 n 元因子分别蒸馏/编译为对完整类型化集合的免搜索解码器并冻结。测试阶段：四个单元全部冻结，在完全保留的新类型组合上比较。","en":"Training: for each training co-retrieved set, randomize or systematically enumerate sufficiently many permutations and evaluate them independently, yielding permutation-outcome data. The symbolic cells use MDL-style clause selection retaining clauses that explain multiple independent training compositions; the n-ary cells train factors over the same typed variables and arity coverage, with parameter/clause capacity and regularization budget matched to clause sparsity. Compilation (once, after training): distill/compile both symbolic clauses and n-ary factors into search-free decoders over complete typed sets and freeze them. Test: all four cells frozen, compared on fully held-out new type compositions."},"persistent_update_object":"frozen_symbolic_clause_registry_and_frozen_typed_n_ary_factor_parameters__each_paired_with_either_the_shared_exact_solver_or_a_frozen_compiled_search_free_decoder__no_object_retrained_reinduced_or_recompiled_after_held_out_evaluation_begins","learning_signal":{"zh":"全部四个单元接收完全相同的训练共检索集合、预定义类型、随机化/枚举置换结果与评估反馈计数；唯一差异是表征形式（子句 vs n 元因子）与解码器形式（求解器 vs 编译）。MDL 子句稀疏度由 n 元单元中等量规模的因子选择/正则化预算匹配；没有任何单元获得额外标签。","en":"All four cells receive identical training co-retrieved sets, predefined types, randomized/enumerated permutation outcomes, and evaluation-feedback counts; the only differences are representational form (clauses vs n-ary factors) and decoder form (solver vs compiled). MDL clause sparsity is matched by an equivalent-sized factor-selection/regularization budget in the n-ary cells; no cell receives extra labels."},"independent_ground_truth":{"zh":"测试真值来自对隐藏类型组合独立执行每一个可行置换，得到真实成功置换集合与硬约束违反。该枚举结果仅用于评估，不向任何冻结注册表、因子模型或编译解码器提供测试时反馈。真值是程序化执行结果，绝非任何学习型评分器或裁判。","en":"Test ground truth comes from independently executing every feasible permutation for hidden type compositions, yielding the true successful-permutation set and hard-constraint violations. Enumeration is evaluation-only and gives no test-time feedback to any frozen registry, factor model, or compiled decoder. Ground truth is programmatic execution truth, never a learned scorer or judge."},"strongest_baseline":{"zh":"最强对照为单元 B：与符号子句共享同一精确求解器的类型化 n 元因子模型，匹配参数/子句容量、相同类型、完整集合、置换结果、训练预算与推理候选预算；单元 D（蒸馏为同一免搜索形式的 n 元因子）为免搜索匹配控制。条件成对因子模型与通用集合能量模型保留为次级表达力对照。","en":"The strongest control is Cell B: a typed n-ary factor model sharing the identical exact solver, with matched parameter/clause capacity, identical types, complete sets, permutation outcomes, training budget, and inference candidate budget; Cell D (n-ary factors distilled into the same search-free form) is the search-free matched control. Conditional Pairwise Factor and Generic Set-Energy Model remain as secondary expressivity controls."},"matched_resources":["identical predefined memory types and provenance/function definitions","identical training and held-out co-retrieved complete typed sets","identical randomized/enumerated permutation-outcome data and evaluation-feedback counts","matched parameter/clause capacity and regularization/MDL budget","identical number of training permutations and optimizer steps/minibatches where applicable","identical exact solver with identical candidate budget for solver cells","identical compiled search-free decoder architecture for compiled cells","matched end-to-end inference wall-clock and token budgets across all four cells","no test-time relearning, re-induction, or recompilation for any cell"],"decisive_pilot":{"zh":"预注册单一 2×2 析因测试：仅在训练类型组合子集上训练，完全保留需要系统性重组已知约束的新组合（如异常-策略优先规则与安全三元规则的首次共现，或第三类型出现时必须反转的对）。冻结全部四个单元，测量精确成功率、约束违反率、相对穷举 oracle 的遗憾，以及端到端推理成本。符号表征命题仅当符号单元在相同解码器内显著优于匹配 n 元单元时存活；编译命题仅当编译单元在严格更低推理成本下精度不劣于求解器单元时存活。","en":"Preregister a single 2×2 factorial test: train only on a subset of type compositions and fully hold out new compositions requiring systematic recombination of known constraints (e.g., first co-occurrence of an Exception-Policy precedence rule with a Safety ternary rule, or a pair whose order must reverse when a third type appears). Freeze all four cells; measure exact-success rate, constraint-violation rate, regret to the exhaustive oracle, and end-to-end inference cost. The symbolic-representation claim survives only if symbolic cells beat matched n-ary cells within the same decoder; the compilation claim survives only if compiled cells match solver-cell accuracy at strictly lower inference cost."},"stop_condition":{"zh":"若共享同一求解器的类型化 n 元因子模型在保留类型组合与精确约束满足上匹配子句注册表，则终止符号系统性命题；若编译解码器相对其求解器对应物损失实质精度，或未能在匹配预算下降低端到端推理成本，则终止免搜索命题；若任何优势仅出现在被人为限制表达力的基线上，则两个命题同时终止并坍缩为无差异结论。","en":"Stop the symbolic-systematicity claim if the typed n-ary factor model with the identical solver matches the clause registry on held-out type compositions and exact constraint satisfaction; stop the search-free claim if the compiled decoder loses material accuracy versus its solver counterpart or fails to reduce end-to-end inference cost under matched budgets; if any advantage appears only against expression-limited baselines, both claims terminate and collapse to a no-difference conclusion."},"surviving_claim":{"zh":"一个可证伪的归纳偏置/效率命题：在相同解码器下，符号子句比同等表达力的类型化 n 元因子具有更好的组合外推；和/或编译在保持求解器精度的同时严格降低推理成本。由于 n 元因子模型可以表达相同的高阶约束，本方案明确不作表征不可能性断言。","en":"A falsifiable inductive-bias/efficiency claim: symbolic clauses yield better compositional extrapolation than equally expressive typed n-ary factors under an identical decoder, and/or compilation preserves solver accuracy at strictly lower inference cost. No representational-impossibility claim is made, since the n-ary factor model can express the same higher-order constraints."},"collision_boundary":{"zh":"与 AGEL-Comp（从经验反馈诱导 Horn 子句用于新组合）及基于 ILP 的组合性符号任务规则学习相近，但本方案的差异在于测试记忆顺序约束的表征 × 解码器分解，并以共享求解器的 n 元因子为最强对照；置换/排序的因子化分布学习提供了非符号的强对照参照。依据所供最近工作上下文，不声称此类分解或对照在文献中不存在。","en":"Closest to AGEL-Comp (inducing Horn clauses from experiential feedback for novel compositions) and ILP-based compositional symbolic task-rule learning, but differs in testing a representation × decoder factorization for memory-order constraints with a solver-sharing n-ary factor as the strongest control; factorized permutation/ranking distribution learning provides a strong non-symbolic reference point. Per the supplied nearest-work context, no claim is made that such factorizations or controls are absent from the literature."},"r3_repair_summary":{"zh":"R3 指出页面将持久符号表征与免搜索行为混为一谈：精确求解仍在测试时重算，且缺少共享解码器的匹配类型化 n 元因子控制。修复采用预注册的 2×2 表征 × 解码器析因：符号子句 vs 匹配 n 元因子（同一精确求解器），加上离线编译并冻结的免搜索解码器单元，全部匹配端到端推理预算。这是对原始机制的最小物质修改，直接分离了表征与解码器两个因子。","en":"R3 found the page conflated a persistent symbolic representation with search-free behavior: exact solving was still recomputed at test time, with no matched typed n-ary factor control sharing the decoder. The repair adopts a preregistered 2×2 representation × decoder factorial: symbolic clauses vs a matched typed n-ary factor model with the identical exact solver, plus frozen compiled search-free decoder cells, all with matched end-to-end inference budgets. This is the smallest material change to the original mechanism and directly separates the representation and decoder factors."},"remaining_risk":{"zh":"对大规模类型化集合，编译可能不可行，从而将免搜索单元限制在有界集合规模；若如此，编译命题收窄至该规模区间，但不影响表征对比命题。此外，若 n 元因子容量匹配不当（过强或过弱），表征对比可能失真，需在预注册中固定容量匹配准则。","en":"Compilation may be infeasible for large typed sets, restricting the search-free cells to bounded set sizes; if so, the compilation claim narrows to that regime without affecting the representation contrast. Additionally, if n-ary factor capacity matching is miscalibrated (too strong or too weak), the representation contrast could be distorted, so capacity-matching criteria must be fixed in preregistration."}},{"idea_id":"certified-out-of-span-interaction-inverter-v53","revision":"R3.1","title":{"zh":"可认证张成空间外交互逆算子：混合参数化与全空间求解器对照","en":"Certified Out-of-Span Interaction Inverter: Mixed-Parameterization and Full-Space Solver Controls"},"purpose":{"zh":"解决组合性任务失败中，当存储增量张成空间内不存在可行修复时，如何生成有效的新知识方向的问题。Farkas不可行性证书仅证明张成空间内无可行修复，不证明纯正交修复存在或正确；本版本通过混合参数化与全空间求解器对照，检验正交退出是否为必要的修复几何。","en":"Address the problem of generating effective new-knowledge directions for compositional task failures when no feasible repair lies within the stored-delta span. The Farkas infeasibility certificate proves only that no feasible in-span repair exists, not that a pure orthogonal repair exists or is correct; this version tests whether orthogonal exit is the necessary repair geometry via mixed-parameterization and full-space solver controls."},"importance":{"zh":"模型编辑与持续学习需要在不破坏已有行为的前提下注入新知识。当组合失败无法通过已有增量张成空间修复时，确定正确的修复几何（张成内、正交补、或混合）对编辑方法的设计至关重要。若正交退出并非必要，则现有零空间约束编辑方法的核心机制主张需被重新限定。","en":"Model editing and continual learning require injecting new knowledge without disrupting existing behavior. When compositional failures cannot be repaired within the stored-delta span, identifying the correct repair geometry (in-span, orthogonal complement, or mixed) is critical for editing method design. If orthogonal exit is not necessary, the core mechanism claim of null-space-constrained editing methods must be re-scoped."},"core_idea":{"zh":"冻结表示与低秩线性决策适配器，对每个失败的组合求解同一预注册修复/保持可行性问题，仅保留携带LP对偶/Farkas不可行性证书的案例。对每个认证案例执行相同的单次、成对、完全回滚，并确定性计算交互残差R。在原有2×2（Target-ON/OFF × Projection-ON/OFF）基础上新增两个机制单元：(E) 混合张成+正交参数化生成器，输出 d = d_span + d_perp（d_perp = Q_perp(d_raw)），使用相同交互方向损失训练；(F) 等访问/等预算全空间约束低秩适配器求解器，在全参数空间（不限于张成或正交补）直接优化同一修复/保持可行性目标，秩、约束、计算量相同。证书仅作为案例选择装置，正交/新知识主张仅在Projection-ON单元在独立隐藏执行真值上优于混合与全空间对照时保留。","en":"Freeze the representation and low-rank linear decision adapter, solve the same preregistered repair/preservation feasibility problem for every failing composition, and retain only cases carrying an LP-dual/Farkas infeasibility certificate. For every certified case, execute identical single, pairwise, and full rollbacks and deterministically compute one interaction residual R. Beyond the original 2×2 (Target-ON/OFF × Projection-ON/OFF), add two mechanism cells: (E) a mixed span+orthogonal parameterization generator emitting d = d_span + d_perp with d_perp = Q_perp(d_raw), trained with the same interaction-direction loss; and (F) an equal-access/equal-budget full-space constrained low-rank adapter solver directly optimizing the same repair/preservation feasibility objective over the full parameter space (not restricted to span or orthogonal complement) with identical rank, constraints, and compute. The certificate serves only as a case-selection device; the projection/new-knowledge claim is retained only if Projection-ON cells outperform both mixed and full-space controls on independent hidden execution truth."},"core_intuition":{"zh":"Farkas证书证明的是\"张成空间内无解\"，而非\"正交补中有解\"或\"正交解最优\"。正确的修复方向可能同时需要张成内与正交分量，或任何满足约束的低秩方向即可。通过混合参数化与全空间求解器，可以在同等监督与预算下直接检验正交退出是否为必要机制，而非默认假设。","en":"The Farkas certificate proves \"no solution within the span,\" not \"a solution exists in the orthogonal complement\" or \"the orthogonal solution is optimal.\" The correct repair direction may require both span and orthogonal components, or any constrained low-rank direction may suffice. Mixed parameterization and full-space solvers directly test whether orthogonal exit is a necessary mechanism under equal supervision and budget, rather than assuming it by default."},"rationale":{"zh":"原版本隐含假设纯张成外退出是正确修复几何，但R3指出证书仅证明张成内不可行。最小材料修复是新增两个对照单元，直接检验混合与全空间几何是否在同等条件下匹配或超越纯正交单元，从而将正交主张限定为可证伪的几何/效率主张，而非存在性主张。","en":"The original version implicitly assumed pure out-of-span exit is the correct repair geometry, but R3 noted the certificate proves only in-span infeasibility. The smallest material repair adds two control cells that directly test whether mixed and full-space geometries match or exceed the pure-orthogonal cell under equal conditions, thereby scoping the orthogonal claim to a falsifiable geometry/efficiency claim rather than an existence claim."},"method_logic":{"zh":"1) 冻结表示与适配器，计算存储增量张成空间的P_span与Q_perp=I-P_span（评估开始后不再重算）。2) 对每个组合求解可行性LP，保留Farkas认证案例。3) 执行回滚并计算R。4) 训练六个容量匹配单元：原2×2加(E)混合参数化生成器与(F)全空间约束求解器。5) 所有单元共享相同认证案例、原子摘要、约束、回滚记录、R、适配器秩、参数量、调用、token、优化器、小批量、步数与墙钟等价更新预算；唯一差异为参数化/求解器几何。6) 在Farkas认证的留出组合上评估，报告2×2内Projection主效应、完整Projection-ON单元 vs 混合单元（检验纯正交必要性）、完整Projection-ON单元 vs 全空间求解器（检验正交退出是否优于无约束可行修复）。","en":"1) Freeze representation and adapter; compute P_span and Q_perp=I-P_span from the stored-delta span once (never recomputed after evaluation begins). 2) Solve the feasibility LP for each composition; retain Farkas-certified cases. 3) Execute rollbacks and compute R. 4) Train six capacity-matched cells: the original 2×2 plus (E) mixed-parameterization generator and (F) full-space constrained solver. 5) All cells share identical certified cases, atom summaries, constraints, rollback records, R, adapter rank, parameter count, calls, tokens, optimizer, minibatches, steps, and wall-clock-equivalent update budget; the only difference is parameterization/solver geometry. 6) Evaluate on Farkas-certified held-out compositions, reporting the Projection main effect within the 2×2, full Projection-ON vs mixed cell (tests pure-orthogonal necessity), and full Projection-ON vs full-space solver (tests whether orthogonal exit beats unconstrained feasible repair)."},"persistent_update_object":"frozen-representation low-rank linear decision adapter plus frozen generators/solvers for each cell; P_span and Q_perp computed once from the frozen stored-delta span and never recomputed after evaluation begins","learning_signal":{"zh":"所有六个单元共享完全相同的认证训练案例、原子摘要、约束、回滚执行、交互残差R、修复/保持约束与隐藏案例采样。唯一预注册的监督干预是交互方向损失是否激活（Target对比）以及参数化/求解器几何（Projection/混合/全空间对比）；禁用该损失不会移除R、回滚轨迹或任何可确定性计算的残差统计量，消除信息匮乏基线。","en":"All six cells share exactly the same certified training cases, atom summaries, constraints, rollback executions, interaction residual R, repair/preservation constraints, and hidden-case sampling. The only preregistered supervision interventions are whether the interaction-direction loss is activated (Target contrast) and the parameterization/solver geometry (Projection/mixed/full-space contrasts); disabling the loss does not remove R, rollback traces, or any deterministically computable residual statistic, eliminating information-deprived baselines."},"independent_ground_truth":{"zh":"证书仅来源于冻结适配器参数空间中的线性修复/保持不等式（LP对偶/Farkas不可行性）。最终正确性由隐藏执行测试判定，这些测试从未用于证书、残差目标或训练，包括目标行为恢复、受保护行为保持与真实组合任务成功。证书与真值因此独立。","en":"The certificate is derived only from linear repair/preservation inequalities in the frozen adapter parameter space (LP-dual/Farkas infeasibility). Final correctness is determined by hidden execution tests never used for the certificate, residual target, or training, including target-behavior recovery, preservation of protected behavior, and true compositional task success. Certificate and truth are therefore independent."},"strongest_baseline":{"zh":"最强简化为单元F：全空间约束低秩适配器求解器，具有相同可行性目标、秩、预算与监督，可自由寻找任何修复方向；以及单元E：混合张成+正交生成器，具有相同监督。两者均强于原无限制Target-ON/Projection-OFF单元（保留为第三对照）。","en":"The strongest simplifications are Cell F: the full-space constrained low-rank adapter solver with identical feasibility objective, rank, budget, and supervision, free to find any repair direction; and Cell E: the mixed span+orthogonal generator with identical supervision. Both are stronger than the original unrestricted Target-ON/Projection-OFF cell, which is retained as a third control."},"matched_resources":["identical certified training cases","identical atom summaries","identical repair/preservation constraints","identical single/pairwise/full rollback executions and records","identical interaction residual R and all deterministically computable residual statistics","identical adapter rank","identical generator/solver parameter count","identical number of calls","identical token budget","identical optimizer","identical minibatches","identical optimization steps","identical wall-clock-equivalent update budget","identical hidden-case sampling","identical frozen representation and adapter","identical P_span/Q_perp operators computed once from the frozen span"],"decisive_pilot":{"zh":"训练前冻结认证案例列表、扩展因子设计、隐藏执行集与因子对比。仅在Farkas认证的留出组合上评估所有单元，报告：(i) 2×2内Projection主效应；(ii) 完整Target-ON/Projection-ON单元 vs 混合单元E（检验纯正交必要性）；(iii) 完整Target-ON/Projection-ON单元 vs 全空间求解器F（检验正交退出是否优于等预算无约束可行修复）。所有对比在独立隐藏执行真值上以等预算进行。若仅投影对比在等残差监督下存活，主张限定为认证张成退出；若仅目标对比存活，限定为交互监督；若仅交互存活且单一因子均无法复现，则仅主张交互；若混合或全空间单元匹配纯正交单元，则停止正交/新知识主张。","en":"Before training, freeze the certified-case list, expanded factorial design, hidden execution set, and factorial contrasts. Evaluate all cells only on Farkas-certified held-out compositions, reporting: (i) the Projection main effect within the 2×2; (ii) full Target-ON/Projection-ON vs mixed cell E (tests pure-orthogonal necessity); (iii) full Target-ON/Projection-ON vs full-space solver F (tests whether orthogonal exit beats equal-budget unconstrained feasible repair). All contrasts are evaluated on independent hidden execution truth with equal budgets. If only the projection contrast survives under equal residual supervision, the claim is restricted to certified span exit; if only the target contrast survives, it is restricted to interaction supervision; if only the interaction survives and neither single factor reproduces it, only the interaction is claimed; if the mixed or full-space cell matches the pure-orthogonal cell, stop the orthogonal/new-knowledge claim."},"stop_condition":{"zh":"若混合张成+正交单元E或全空间约束求解器F在独立隐藏执行真值上匹配纯Target-ON/Projection-ON单元，停止张成外/新知识机制主张。若Target-OFF单元匹配完整方法，停止显式交互目标主张；若Target-ON/Projection-OFF复现完整方法，停止投影主张。若无任何几何隔离组件或交互在独立真值上相对最简等价方法产生稳定优势，终止该想法而非添加或重命名组件。","en":"Stop the out-of-span/new-knowledge mechanism claim if the mixed span+orthogonal cell E or the full-space constrained solver F matches the pure Target-ON/Projection-ON cell on independent hidden execution truth. Stop the explicit interaction-target claim if Target-OFF cells match the full method; stop the projection claim if Target-ON/Projection-OFF reproduces it. If no geometrically isolated component or interaction yields a stable advantage on independent truth over the simplest equivalent method, terminate the idea rather than adding or renaming components."},"surviving_claim":{"zh":"一个可证伪的几何/效率主张：对于Farkas认证的张成内不可行案例，在相同秩与预算下，纯正交补修复在隐藏执行成功率上优于同等监督的混合或全空间约束修复。不主张正交修复是唯一可能的修复。","en":"A falsifiable geometry/efficiency claim: for Farkas-certified in-span-infeasible cases, pure orthogonal-complement repair achieves better hidden execution success than equally supervised mixed or full-space constrained repairs of identical rank and budget. No claim that orthogonal repair is the only possible repair is made."},"collision_boundary":{"zh":"AlphaEdit使用零空间投影约束编辑，与本工作的张成退出组件重叠，但不包含证书加因子识别契约，也不包含混合参数化或全空间求解器对照。O-Edit使用正交编辑子空间，与投影原理重叠，但同样无证书驱动的案例选择与几何必要性检验。Quasi-Orthogonal Model Merging将新任务向量投影至先前任务向量张成的正交补，与任务向量几何重叠，但不涉及组合失败的LP可行性认证或受控几何对比。本工作的边界在于：仅当纯正交单元在独立执行真值上优于混合与全空间对照时，才主张正交退出的必要性。","en":"AlphaEdit constrains edits using null-space projection, overlapping the span-exit component but lacking the certificate-plus-factorial identification contract and the mixed-parameterization or full-space solver controls. O-Edit uses orthogonal editing subspaces, overlapping the projection principle, but likewise lacks certificate-driven case selection and geometry-necessity testing. Quasi-Orthogonal Model Merging projects new task vectors toward the orthogonal complement of previous task-vector spans, overlapping the task-vector geometry, but involves no LP feasibility certification of compositional failures or controlled geometry contrasts. The boundary of this work: the necessity of orthogonal exit is claimed only if the pure-orthogonal cell outperforms mixed and full-space controls on independent execution truth."},"r3_repair_summary":{"zh":"R3指出Farkas证书仅证明张成内不可行，而非纯正交修复存在或正确。修复方式：新增混合张成+正交参数化单元（E）与等访问/等预算全空间约束低秩适配器求解器（F），将证书降级为案例选择装置，并将正交/新知识主张限定为仅在Projection-ON单元于独立隐藏执行真值上优于混合与全空间对照时保留的可证伪几何/效率主张。","en":"R3 found the Farkas certificate proves only in-span infeasibility, not that a pure orthogonal repair exists or is correct. Repair: add a mixed span+orthogonal parameterization cell (E) and an equal-access/equal-budget full-space constrained low-rank adapter solver (F), demote the certificate to a case-selection device, and scope the orthogonal/new-knowledge claim to a falsifiable geometry/efficiency claim retained only if Projection-ON cells outperform mixed and full-space controls on independent hidden execution truth."},"remaining_risk":{"zh":"全空间求解器在大适配器秩下计算开销可能较高；预算匹配可能要求限制秩，从而将主张窄化至该秩区间。此外，若混合单元与纯正交单元在所有测试秩上均表现相当，则正交退出的必要性主张将被彻底放弃。","en":"The full-space solver may be computationally expensive for large adapter ranks; budget matching may require restricting rank, narrowing the claim to that rank regime. Additionally, if the mixed cell matches the pure-orthogonal cell across all tested ranks, the necessity claim for orthogonal exit will be fully abandoned."}},{"idea_id":"compiler-residual-contract-editor-v53","revision":"R3.1","title":{"en":"Compiler-Residual Contract Editor: Typed-Residual vs Generic Local-Delta Isolation","zh":"编译器残差式契约编辑器：类型化残差与通用局部增量编辑的隔离对比"},"purpose":{"en":"Determine whether a typed relational residual edit whitelist (dependency-edge, semantic-predicate, temporal-relation) applied on top of a deterministic schema compiler's output M0 provides measurable held-out contract-transfer value beyond an equally supervised, equally local generic delta editor and a monolithic rewriter, under strictly matched data, supervision, capacity, and compute.","zh":"在严格匹配的数据、监督、容量与算力条件下，判定作用于确定性模式编译器输出 M0 之上的类型化关系残差编辑白名单（依赖边、语义谓词、时序关系），是否相较于同等监督、同等局部性的通用增量编辑器以及整体重写器，在留出契约迁移上带来可测量的额外价值。"},"importance":{"en":"Schema-migrated memory-contract assets must preserve hidden relational, handoff, and temporal invariants under unseen models and harnesses. If a structured residual object after deterministic compilation yields transferable gains that generic local edits and full rewriting cannot match at equal budget, it identifies a concrete, reusable inductive bias for agent memory migration; if not, the simpler mechanisms suffice and the added structure is unjustified.","zh":"模式迁移后的记忆契约资产必须在未见模型与未见执行框架下保持隐藏的关系、交接与时序不变量。若确定性编译之后的结构化残差对象能带来通用局部编辑与整体重写在同等预算下无法匹敌的可迁移收益，则它为智能体记忆迁移提供了一个具体可复用的归纳偏置；若不能，则更简单的机制已足够，额外结构不具正当性。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Run the shared deterministic compiler C_schema for every source/target schema pair to obtain M0. Freeze one common training set of source-target asset pairs, storing for each pair the source asset, target asset, M0, target execution traces, checker outcomes, success/failure labels, and a canonical residual annotation delta_R produced from M0 and the target asset by a fixed differencer. Train three cells under identical conditions: (1) a typed residual editor that may emit only whitelisted dependency-edge, semantic-predicate, and temporal-relation edits and returns Apply(M0, delta_R_hat); (2) a generic local-delta editor that emits unrestricted local edits (preregistered canonical locality: any contiguous span or AST-subtree replacement) applied to the same M0 via the same Apply(M0,·) decomposition, without the typed whitelist; (3) a capacity-matched monolithic rewriter that emits a complete target asset and contains an equally sized auxiliary residual head so it consumes the same delta_R supervision, with the auxiliary head discarded at inference. All three share identical train/validation examples, delta_R annotations, traces, checker outcomes, labels, verifier V, repair/rejection attempts, calls, tokens (output-length differences equalized by a preregistered padded/masked decoding budget), parameter budget, batch schedule, optimization steps, and wall-clock.","zh":"对每个源/目标模式对运行共享的确定性编译器 C_schema 得到 M0。冻结一份公共的源-目标资产训练集，为每对资产存储源资产、目标资产、M0、目标执行轨迹、检查器结果、成功/失败标签，以及由固定差分器从 M0 与目标资产生成的规范残差标注 delta_R。在完全相同条件下训练三个对比单元：(1) 类型化残差编辑器，仅可发出白名单内的依赖边、语义谓词与时序关系编辑，返回 Apply(M0, delta_R_hat)；(2) 通用局部增量编辑器，对同一 M0 通过相同的 Apply(M0,·) 分解施加不受类型限制的局部编辑（预先注册的规范局部性定义：任意连续片段或 AST 子树替换），不使用类型化白名单；(3) 容量匹配的整体重写器，输出完整目标资产，并含等大的辅助残差头以消费相同的 delta_R 监督，推理时丢弃该辅助头。三者共享完全相同的训练/验证样本、delta_R 标注、轨迹、检查器结果、标签、验证器 V、修复/拒绝尝试、调用次数、token 数（输出长度差异通过预先注册的填充/掩码解码预算拉平）、参数预算、批调度、优化步数与墙钟时间。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"The deterministic compiler already absorbs the mechanical schema-mapping work; the open question is whether what remains is best learned as typed relational edits rather than generic local edits or full regeneration. The typed whitelist is an inductive-bias hypothesis: restricting edits to dependency/predicate/temporal relations should bias learning toward exactly the invariants that must survive model-and-harness swaps. This hypothesis is only falsifiable if a generic local-delta editor with identical compiled state, supervision, and budget is given the same chance—otherwise any gain could come from locality or the Apply(M0,·) decomposition alone, not from the typed structure.","zh":"确定性编译器已吸收了机械性的模式映射工作；悬而未决的问题是剩余部分是否最适合以类型化关系编辑来学习，而非通用局部编辑或整体重生成。类型化白名单是一个归纳偏置假设：将编辑限制在依赖/谓词/时序关系上，应使学习偏向那些必须在模型与执行框架替换后仍然成立的不变量。只有当拥有相同编译状态、监督与预算的通用局部增量编辑器获得同等机会时，该假设才可被证伪——否则任何收益都可能仅来自局部性或 Apply(M0,·) 分解本身，而非类型化结构。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3 found the residual-specific thesis was not isolated from a generic matched local-delta editor: the original design contrasted typed residual editing only with a monolithic rewriter, leaving locality and the Apply(M0,·) decomposition confounded with typed structure. The smallest material repair is to add one generic local-delta cell that shares everything—compiled state M0, delta_R supervision, traces, labels, verifier access, capacity, calls, tokens, steps, wall-clock, and the Apply(M0,·) decomposition—differing only in lacking the typed edit whitelist. The typed-residual claim then survives only if it beats this generic local-delta editor on held-out contract transfer; the monolithic rewriter remains as the no-decomposition control.","zh":"R3 发现残差专属论点未与通用的匹配局部增量编辑器隔离：原设计仅将类型化残差编辑与整体重写器对比，使局部性与 Apply(M0,·) 分解同类型化结构混淆。最小的实质性修复是增加一个通用局部增量单元，它共享一切——编译状态 M0、delta_R 监督、轨迹、标签、验证器访问、容量、调用、token、步数、墙钟时间以及 Apply(M0,·) 分解——唯一差别是不具备类型化编辑白名单。类型化残差论点只有在留出契约迁移上击败该通用局部增量编辑器时才成立；整体重写器保留为无分解对照。"},"method_logic":{"en":"Three-way factorial comparison under a frozen protocol. Factor A (decomposition): Apply(M0,·) residual application vs full generation. Factor B (edit typing): typed relational whitelist vs unrestricted local edits, within the decomposition arm. Cell (1) typed residual editor, cell (2) generic local-delta editor, cell (3) monolithic rewriter. The residual-required evaluation subset is preregistered using only the deterministic compiler and gold target assets: M0 must already pass the schema/type/reference checker, its canonical difference from the gold target must contain at least one whitelisted relational residual, and that residual must be necessary for a preregistered target-execution assertion; membership is determined entirely by compiler, gold asset, and the predefined assertion procedure, never by any learned model's output. Primary contrast: cell (1) vs cell (2) on identical held-out residual-required cases plus a joint unseen-model × unseen-harness swap. Secondary: cell (3) and the full held-out set to prevent subset-only overfitting.","zh":"在冻结协议下进行三因素析因对比。因素 A（分解方式）：Apply(M0,·) 残差应用 vs 完整生成。因素 B（编辑类型化）：在分解臂内，类型化关系白名单 vs 不受限局部编辑。单元 (1) 类型化残差编辑器，单元 (2) 通用局部增量编辑器，单元 (3) 整体重写器。残差必需评估子集仅使用确定性编译器与金标目标资产预先注册：M0 必须已通过模式/类型/引用检查器；其与金标目标的规范差异必须包含至少一个白名单关系残差；且该残差对一个预先注册的目标执行断言是必要的；子集归属完全由编译器、金标资产与预定义断言程序决定，绝不由任何学习模型的输出决定。主要对比：在完全相同的留出残差必需样本以及联合未见模型 × 未见执行框架替换上比较单元 (1) 与单元 (2)。次要对比：单元 (3) 与完整留出集，以防止仅在子集上过拟合。"},"persistent_update_object":"Frozen typed residual editor, frozen generic local-delta editor, and frozen monolithic rewriter, all trained once on the frozen training set and then fixed; the persistent migrated memory-contract asset is produced as Apply(M0, delta_R_hat) for the two editor cells and as a complete generated asset for the rewriter. No model is retrained, fine-tuned, or re-fitted after held-out evaluation or the model-and-harness swap begins; all three are reused as-is at evaluation.","learning_signal":{"en":"All three models share, example by example, identical source-target pairs, M0, canonical delta_R annotations, target execution traces, checker outcomes, success/failure labels, verifier V feedback, and repair/rejection attempts, with strictly matched calls, tokens (padded/masked equalization of output-length differences), batch schedule, optimization steps, parameter count, and wall-clock. Delta_R supervision is available to all cells: directly for both editors and via an equally sized auxiliary residual head for the monolithic rewriter.","zh":"三个模型逐样本共享完全相同的源-目标对、M0、规范 delta_R 标注、目标执行轨迹、检查器结果、成功/失败标签、验证器 V 反馈以及修复/拒绝尝试，并严格匹配调用次数、token 数（以填充/掩码方式拉平输出长度差异）、批调度、优化步数、参数量与墙钟时间。delta_R 监督对所有单元可用：两个编辑器直接使用，整体重写器通过等大的辅助残差头使用。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Final truth comes from hidden target executions, hidden relational assertions, handoff/temporal invariants, and true task completion under joint model-and-harness swaps that are unavailable during training and subset construction. Training target traces, delta_R annotations, and verifier V do not contain these hidden assertions, and no learned scorer or judge is used as ground truth.","zh":"最终真值来自隐藏的目标执行、隐藏的关系断言、交接/时序不变量，以及在联合模型与执行框架替换下的真实任务完成情况；这些在训练与子集构建期间均不可用。训练用目标轨迹、delta_R 标注与验证器 V 均不包含这些隐藏断言，且不以任何学习得到的评分器或评判器作为真值。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"The generic local-delta editor: identical compiled state M0, identical delta_R supervision, data, capacity, calls, tokens, optimization steps, wall-clock, verifier access, repair attempts, and the same Apply(M0,·) decomposition, differing only in that its local edits (contiguous span or AST-subtree replacements, one preregistered canonical locality definition) are not restricted to the typed dependency-edge/semantic-predicate/temporal-relation whitelist. The capacity-matched monolithic rewriter with the auxiliary residual head remains as the no-decomposition control.","zh":"通用局部增量编辑器：相同的编译状态 M0、相同的 delta_R 监督、数据、容量、调用、token、优化步数、墙钟时间、验证器访问、修复尝试以及相同的 Apply(M0,·) 分解，唯一差别在于其局部编辑（连续片段或 AST 子树替换，采用一个预先注册的规范局部性定义）不受类型化依赖边/语义谓词/时序关系白名单的限制。带辅助残差头的容量匹配整体重写器保留为无分解对照。"},"matched_resources":["same frozen train/validation source-target asset pairs","same deterministic compiler C_schema and identical M0 per example","same canonical delta_R annotations and differencer","same target execution traces and checker outcomes","same success/failure labels","same verifier V and checker-guided repair/rejection attempt budget","same number of model calls","same token budget with preregistered padded/masked decoding equalization of output-length differences","same parameter budget / model capacity","same batch schedule, optimizer, minibatches, and optimization steps","same wall-clock budget","same Apply(M0,·) decomposition for both editor cells","same auxiliary residual head size for the monolithic rewriter","same preregistered residual-required evaluation subset and joint unseen-model × unseen-harness swap protocol"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"A single preregistered crossed test. Before inspecting any model-comparison result, preregister the residual-required subset using only the deterministic compiler and gold target assets: M0 passes the schema/type/reference checker; its canonical difference from the gold target contains at least one whitelisted relational residual; that residual is necessary for a preregistered target-execution assertion. Subset membership is determined entirely by compiler, gold asset, and the predefined assertion procedure, never by any learned model's output. On identical held-out residual-required cases, cross the three cells (typed residual editor × generic local-delta editor × monolithic rewriter) with a joint unseen-model × unseen-harness swap. Primary contrast: typed residual editor vs generic local-delta editor. Primary outcomes: hidden execution success, relational correctness, and preservation failure; the monolithic rewriter and the complete held-out set are reported secondarily to prevent subset-only overfitting. The typed-structure claim is killed if the generic local-delta editor matches the typed editor on the primary outcomes.","zh":"一个预先注册的交叉测试。在查看任何模型对比结果之前，仅使用确定性编译器与金标目标资产预先注册残差必需子集：M0 通过模式/类型/引用检查器；其与金标目标的规范差异包含至少一个白名单关系残差；且该残差对一个预先注册的目标执行断言是必要的。子集归属完全由编译器、金标资产与预定义断言程序决定，绝不由任何学习模型的输出决定。在完全相同的留出残差必需样本上，将三个单元（类型化残差编辑器 × 通用局部增量编辑器 × 整体重写器）与联合未见模型 × 未见执行框架替换交叉。主要对比：类型化残差编辑器 vs 通用局部增量编辑器。主要结局指标：隐藏执行成功率、关系正确性与保持性失败；整体重写器与完整留出集作为次要报告，以防止仅在子集上过拟合。若通用局部增量编辑器在主要结局上追平类型化编辑器，则类型化结构论点被否决。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Stop the structured/typed-residual claim if the generic local-delta editor, with identical compiled state, delta_R supervision, data, capacity, calls, tokens, steps, wall-clock, and Apply(M0,·) decomposition, matches the typed residual editor on hidden execution success, relational correctness, and swap transfer within the preregistered residual-required subset. Stop the entire post-compiler residual claim if the monolithic rewriter matches both editor cells. Stop any claim if the advantage appears only on a subset selected after observing model results.","zh":"若通用局部增量编辑器在相同的编译状态、delta_R 监督、数据、容量、调用、token、步数、墙钟时间与 Apply(M0,·) 分解下，于预先注册的残差必需子集内在隐藏执行成功率、关系正确性与替换迁移上追平类型化残差编辑器，则终止结构化/类型化残差论点。若整体重写器同时追平两个编辑器单元，则终止整个编译后残差论点。若优势仅出现在观察到模型结果之后选取的子集上，则终止一切相关论点。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"A falsifiable inductive-bias/transfer claim only: under identical compiled state, supervision, locality, decomposition, and budget, restricting learned residual edits to a typed relational whitelist (dependency-edge, semantic-predicate, temporal-relation) yields better held-out contract transfer—hidden execution success, relational correctness, and robustness under joint model-and-harness swaps—than an equally supervised generic local-delta editor. No claim is made that generic local edits or full rewriting cannot represent the same transformations; the claim concerns an identifiable transfer/efficiency factor that the preregistered pilot can falsify.","zh":"仅保留一个可证伪的归纳偏置/迁移论点：在相同的编译状态、监督、局部性、分解方式与预算下，将学习到的残差编辑限制在类型化关系白名单（依赖边、语义谓词、时序关系）内，相较于同等监督的通用局部增量编辑器，能带来更好的留出契约迁移——隐藏执行成功率、关系正确性，以及在联合模型与执行框架替换下的稳健性。不主张通用局部编辑或整体重写无法表示相同的变换；该论点关乎一个可被预先注册试验证伪的、可识别的迁移/效率因素。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Nearest supplied work learns execution-guided edits to existing programs (Learning to Edit Visual Programs with Self-Supervision), directly studies learned structural editing against direct generation (Learning Structural Edits via Incremental Tree Transformations), and trains structured localized program edits with reinforcement learning (SCALPEL). The present claim is therefore not generic edit locality, sparsity, or edit-vs-generation novelty; it is narrowly that, after deterministic schema compilation of memory-contract assets, a typed relational edit whitelist outperforms an identically resourced generic local-delta editor on held-out contract transfer under model-and-harness swaps. No assertion is made that this factor is absent from the literature beyond the supplied nearest work.","zh":"所提供的最近邻工作包括：以执行引导方式学习对既有程序的编辑（Learning to Edit Visual Programs with Self-Supervision）、直接对比结构化编辑与从头生成（Learning Structural Edits via Incremental Tree Transformations）、以及用强化学习训练结构化局部程序编辑（SCALPEL）。因此，本论点不涉及通用的编辑局部性、稀疏性或“编辑 vs 生成”的新颖性；它仅窄化为：在对记忆契约资产进行确定性模式编译之后，类型化关系编辑白名单在留出契约迁移（模型与执行框架替换下）上优于资源完全相同的通用局部增量编辑器。除所提供的最近邻工作外，不断言该因素在文献中不存在。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"R3 required isolating the residual-specific thesis from a generic matched local-delta editor. The repair adds exactly one new cell: a generic local-delta editor with identical compiled state M0, delta_R supervision, traces, labels, verifier access, capacity, calls, tokens, steps, wall-clock, and the same Apply(M0,·) decomposition, differing only in lacking the typed edit whitelist. The primary contrast of the preregistered pilot is re-aimed at typed residual vs generic local-delta; the monolithic rewriter is demoted to a no-decomposition control; the stop condition now explicitly collapses the typed-structure claim when the generic local-delta editor reproduces it, and collapses the whole residual claim when the monolithic rewriter matches both.","zh":"R3 要求将残差专属论点与通用的匹配局部增量编辑器隔离。本次修复恰好新增一个单元：通用局部增量编辑器，具有相同的编译状态 M0、delta_R 监督、轨迹、标签、验证器访问、容量、调用、token、步数、墙钟时间以及相同的 Apply(M0,·) 分解，唯一差别是不具备类型化编辑白名单。预先注册试验的主要对比重新定位为类型化残差 vs 通用局部增量；整体重写器降为无分解对照；停止条件现在明确规定：当通用局部增量编辑器复现该效应时，类型化结构论点即告崩溃；当整体重写器同时追平两者时，整个残差论点即告崩溃。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"The granularity of 'local edit' for the generic cell (contiguous span vs AST-subtree replacement) can itself affect the comparison and could be tuned post hoc; this is mitigated by preregistering one canonical locality definition before any model results are inspected. A residual risk remains that the typed whitelist's benefit, if any, interacts with the specific canonical differencer or verifier V, which the current design does not vary.","zh":"通用单元中“局部编辑”的粒度（连续片段 vs AST 子树替换）本身可能影响对比结果，并存在被事后调优的风险；通过在查看任何模型结果之前预先注册一个规范局部性定义来缓解。剩余风险在于：类型化白名单若有效，其收益可能与特定的规范差分器或验证器 V 相互作用，而当前设计并未对这两者进行变化。"}},{"idea_id":"filtered-chronological-evaluator-state-v53","revision":"R3.1","title":{"en":"Filtered Longitudinal Evaluator-State Extrapolation: Retrained Recurrent Transition-Free Control","zh":"滤波式纵向评价器状态外推：重训练循环无转移对照"},"purpose":{"en":"Predict how an unseen future evaluator's actor-specific biases will behave by extrapolating a learned latent evaluator state over time, and test whether an explicit filtered state-space transition is genuinely necessary for that extrapolation rather than any recurrent sequence model trained on the same chronological record.","zh":"通过在时间上外推学习到的潜在评价器状态，预测未见未来评价器的行动者特定偏差行为，并检验显式的滤波状态空间转移结构对该外推是否真正必要，而非任何在相同编年记录上训练的循环序列模型即可达到。"},"importance":{"en":"LLM evaluators drift across versions, so static judge models misestimate actor quality on future evaluators. If a frozen latent-state transition extrapolates better than a matched recurrent predictor trained on identical data, that isolates a transferable inductive bias for temporal evaluator drift, informing how to maintain evaluation validity as benchmarks and judges age.","zh":"LLM 评价器随版本漂移，静态评判模型会在未来评价器上错误估计行动者质量。若冻结的潜在状态转移比在同数据上训练的匹配循环预测器外推更好，则分离出针对评价器时间漂移的可迁移归纳偏置，为基准与评判模型老化时维持评估有效性提供依据。"},"core_idea":{"en":"Keep the filtered state model z_t^- = T_theta(z_{t-1}, Δt_t), z_t = z_t^- + K_phi(z_t^-, o_t)(o_t − H_psi(z_t^-)), r_hat(a,t) = C_omega(d_a, z_t), trained only on historical evaluators and frozen. The R3.1 repair adds a retrained, capacity/data/budget-matched recurrent transition-free control (GRU-style sequence model) that consumes the identical chronological observations (ordered fingerprints and Δt intervals) and the same residual supervision, and directly predicts actor-specific residuals without an explicit transition/filter decomposition. Both models, plus the direct-history predictor D, undergo the same correspondence-destroying derangement (frozen seed π re-pairing fingerprints with intervals from other slots, no absolute timestamps or sortable version IDs) and the same inference-only transition-prior ablation (z_t^- := z_{t-1} for the state model).","zh":"保留滤波状态模型 z_t^- = T_theta(z_{t-1}, Δt_t)，z_t = z_t^- + K_phi(z_t^-, o_t)(o_t − H_psi(z_t^-))，r_hat(a,t) = C_omega(d_a, z_t)，仅在历史评价器上训练并冻结。R3.1 修复新增一个重训练的、容量/数据/预算匹配的循环无转移对照（GRU 式序列模型），它接收完全相同的编年观测（有序指纹与 Δt 间隔）和相同的残差监督，直接预测行动者特定残差而不含显式转移/滤波分解。两个模型以及直接历史预测器 D 都接受相同的对应关系破坏重排（冻结种子 π 将指纹与其他槽位的间隔重新配对，不暴露绝对时间戳或可排序版本号）以及相同的仅推理转移先验消融（对状态模型令 z_t^- := z_{t-1}）。"},"core_intuition":{"en":"A recurrent network can in principle represent the same input-output function as the filtered state model, so the claim is not about representational power. The claim is that the explicit transition-plus-observation-update factorization is a better inductive bias for frozen extrapolation to future evaluator versions: it should generalize better clean, and it should rely on true fingerprint-interval correspondence, so destroying that correspondence should hurt it more than the recurrent control.","zh":"循环网络原则上可以表示与滤波状态模型相同的输入输出函数，因此主张不在于表示能力。主张是：显式的转移加观测更新分解是面向未来评价器版本冻结外推的更好归纳偏置——它在干净输入上应泛化更好，且应依赖真实的指纹-间隔对应关系，因此破坏该对应关系对它的伤害应大于循环对照。"},"rationale":{"en":"R3 found that evaluator drift is real but the filtered-state mechanism was not separated from a retrained recurrent transition-free predictor seeing the same chronological observations and interventions. The smallest material repair is to add exactly that control as a trained model cell, retrained on identical windows with identical budget, and to make the decisive test a state × corruption interaction on independent endpoint truth, so the mechanism claim is falsifiable rather than assumed.","zh":"R3 发现评价器漂移真实存在，但滤波状态机制未与一个看到相同编年观测与干预的重训练循环无转移预测器分离。最小的实质修复正是把该对照作为训练模型单元加入，在相同窗口与相同预算下重训练，并将决定性检验设为基于独立终点真值的状态×腐败交互，使机制主张可证伪而非被假设。"},"method_logic":{"en":"Train three models on identical historical actor-by-evaluator residual supervision: (1) the filtered state model, (2) the retrained recurrent transition-free control, (3) the direct-history predictor D. Freeze all before rolling-origin evaluation. For each window, apply the frozen derangement π to construct the Correspondence-Destroyed input (fingerprint multiset and interval multiset preserved, true pairing destroyed, no absolute timestamps/version IDs), and apply the inference-only transition-prior ablation to the state model. Compare frozen future-version extrapolation against held-out actor-by-evaluator judgments and task outcomes. The mechanism claim requires a clean advantage over both controls plus a larger degradation under correspondence destruction than the recurrent control exhibits.","zh":"在完全相同的历史行动者×评价器残差监督上训练三个模型：(1) 滤波状态模型，(2) 重训练的循环无转移对照，(3) 直接历史预测器 D。滚动起点评估前全部冻结。每个窗口用冻结重排 π 构造对应关系破坏输入（指纹多重集与间隔多重集保持不变，真实配对被破坏，无绝对时间戳/版本号），并对状态模型施加仅推理转移先验消融。以留出的行动者×评价器评判与任务结果为真值比较冻结的未来版本外推。机制主张要求干净条件下优于两个对照，且在对应关系破坏下的退化幅度大于循环对照。"},"persistent_update_object":"Frozen filtered evaluator-state modules (transition T_theta, observation filter K_phi/H_psi, actor-specific correction head C_omega) and the frozen retrained recurrent transition-free control; both are fitted only on historical evaluators, frozen before any rolling-origin evaluation window, and reused without test-time relearning.","learning_signal":{"en":"All models receive exactly the same historical actor-by-evaluator residual supervision, ordered fingerprints, transition intervals Δt, actor descriptors, training windows, and intervention supervision; no future-evaluator labels are available to any model. The derangement corruption and the transition-prior ablation operate only on the evaluation path of frozen models.","zh":"所有模型接收完全相同的历史行动者×评价器残差监督、有序指纹、转移间隔 Δt、行动者描述符、训练窗口与干预监督；任何模型都得不到未来评价器标签。重排腐败与转移先验消融仅作用于冻结模型的评估路径。"},"independent_ground_truth":{"en":"Actor-specific bias truth for each future evaluator is computed programmatically from fully held-out actor-by-evaluator judgments and task outcomes revealed only for final scoring. These labels are never used by the fingerprints, T/K/H/C modules, the recurrent control, the direct predictor, the permutation seed, or the corruption construction, and no learned scorer or judge defines the endpoint.","zh":"每个未来评价器的行动者特定偏差真值由完全留出的行动者×评价器评判与任务结果以程序化方式计算，仅在最终评分时揭示。这些标签从不被指纹、T/K/H/C 模块、循环对照、直接预测器、置换种子或腐败构造使用，且终点不由任何学习型打分器或评判模型定义。"},"strongest_baseline":{"en":"The retrained recurrent transition-free control (GRU-style) with identical chronological observations, intervention supervision, capacity, data, and budget, receiving the identical derangement corruption. The capacity-matched direct-history predictor D remains as a non-recurrent control; current-fingerprint-only and last-version predictors remain weaker controls.","zh":"重训练的循环无转移对照（GRU 式），具有相同的编年观测、干预监督、容量、数据与预算，并接受相同的重排腐败。容量匹配的直接历史预测器 D 作为非循环对照保留；仅用当前指纹与仅用末版本的预测器作为更弱对照。"},"matched_resources":["identical ordered historical fingerprints and current fingerprint","identical transition intervals Δt","identical actor descriptors d_a","identical historical actor-by-evaluator residual labels and training windows","identical intervention supervision (derangement corruption applied to all models)","identical parameter count (preregistered capacity match between state model and recurrent control)","identical training calls, tokens, optimizer, minibatches, and optimization steps","identical inference tokens and wall-clock budget","identical frozen evaluation protocol with no test-time relearning for any model"],"decisive_pilot":{"en":"One preregistered rolling-origin factorial: {Clean, Correspondence-Destroyed} × {State model, Recurrent control, Direct predictor}, plus the inference-only Transition-Prior-Ablated arm for the state model. The latent-transition claim survives only if (i) the clean state model outperforms both the recurrent control and D on zero-anchor future evaluators on independent endpoint truth; (ii) the state model's advantage over the recurrent control contracts significantly more under correspondence destruction than the recurrent control's own degradation (state × corruption interaction); and (iii) inference-only T_theta ablation worsens the state model. Equal degradation of both models under identical corruption does not support the mechanism claim.","zh":"一项预注册的滚动起点析因实验：{干净， 对应关系破坏} × {状态模型， 循环对照， 直接预测器}，外加状态模型的仅推理转移先验消融臂。潜在转移主张仅在以下全部成立时存活：(i) 干净状态模型在独立终点真值上于零锚点未来评价器优于循环对照与 D；(ii) 在对应关系破坏下，状态模型相对循环对照的优势收缩显著大于循环对照自身的退化（状态×腐败交互）；(iii) 仅推理 T_theta 消融使状态模型变差。两个模型在相同腐败下同等退化不能支持机制主张。"},"stop_condition":{"en":"Stop or collapse the latent-transition claim if the retrained recurrent transition-free control matches the clean state model on frozen future-version extrapolation, if both models degrade equally under correspondence destruction (no state-specific interaction), if inference-only transition-prior ablation does not reduce state-model performance, if removing all recoverable time identifiers leaves the state model unchanged, or if the clean state model shows no stable advantage over the matched direct-history predictor.","zh":"若重训练的循环无转移对照在冻结未来版本外推上追平干净状态模型，若两个模型在对应关系破坏下同等退化（无状态特异性交互），若仅推理转移先验消融不降低状态模型性能，若移除全部可恢复时间标识后状态模型不变，或干净状态模型相对匹配的直接历史预测器无稳定优势，则终止或坍缩潜在转移主张。"},"surviving_claim":{"en":"A falsifiable inductive-bias and extrapolation claim: the explicit filtered state-space transition yields better frozen future-version extrapolation than an equally trained, equally capacitated recurrent sequence model on identical chronological observations, and its advantage is specifically attributable to the transition structure via the state × corruption interaction. No claim is made that a recurrent model cannot represent the same function.","zh":"一条可证伪的归纳偏置与外推主张：显式滤波状态空间转移在相同编年观测上比同等训练、同等容量的循环序列模型带来更好的冻结未来版本外推，且其优势通过状态×腐败交互可专门归因于转移结构。不主张循环模型无法表示相同函数。"},"collision_boundary":{"en":"Learning to Judge (ACL Anthology) studies learned LLM evaluation and explicitly leaves temporal evaluator drift/adaptation outside its static treatment; this work targets exactly that longitudinal gap but claims only an inductive-bias advantage established against a matched recurrent control, not a new judging rubric. The Silent Judge (arXiv) documents shortcut biases such as provenance/recency effects in LLM judges but does not learn a frozen transition state extrapolating actor-specific bias to future judge versions; this work's falsifier design is informed by such shortcut findings but the mechanism claim is restricted to the state × corruption interaction. When Benchmarks Age (ACL Anthology) studies temporal misalignment and benchmark aging rather than state-space forecasting of changing evaluator behavior; this work does not claim to be the first to note evaluator drift, only to separate a filtered-transition mechanism from matched recurrent alternatives.","zh":"Learning to Judge（ACL Anthology）研究学习型 LLM 评估，并明确将评价器的时间漂移/适应置于其静态处理之外；本工作正针对该纵向空白，但仅主张经匹配循环对照检验的归纳偏置优势，而非新的评判准则。The Silent Judge（arXiv）记录了 LLM 评判中的来源/近因等捷径偏差，但未学习可向未来评判版本外推行动者特定偏差的冻结转移状态；本工作的证伪设计受此类捷径发现启发，但机制主张仅限于状态×腐败交互。When Benchmarks Age（ACL Anthology）研究时间错配与基准老化，而非对评价器行为变化的状态空间预测；本工作不主张首个指出评价器漂移，仅主张将滤波转移机制与匹配的循环替代方案分离。"},"r3_repair_summary":{"en":"R3 found the filtered-state mechanism was not separated from a retrained recurrent transition-free predictor seeing the same chronological observations and interventions. The repair adds exactly that control as a trained, frozen model cell with identical data, supervision, capacity, and budget; applies the derangement corruption and transition-prior ablation identically; makes the decisive test a preregistered factorial requiring a state × corruption interaction on independent endpoint truth; and keeps the honest framing that the recurrent model can represent the same function, so the surviving claim concerns inductive bias and extrapolation only.","zh":"R3 发现滤波状态机制未与看到相同编年观测与干预的重训练循环无转移预测器分离。修复正是将该对照作为经训练并冻结的模型单元加入，数据、监督、容量与预算完全相同；重排腐败与转移先验消融同样施加；决定性检验设为预注册析因，要求在独立终点真值上出现状态×腐败交互；并保留诚实表述：循环模型可表示相同函数，因此存活主张仅涉及归纳偏置与外推。"},"remaining_risk":{"en":"Capacity matching between a structured state-space model and a GRU-style recurrent control is approximate; if exact functional-capacity matching is infeasible, preregister parameter-count and wall-clock matching and report sensitivity to capacity variation. A positive interaction could also reflect filter-specific overfitting to interval pairing rather than a generalizable transition prior, so the preregistered interaction threshold and replication across rolling windows are required before strengthening the claim.","zh":"结构化状态空间模型与 GRU 式循环对照之间的容量匹配是近似的；若无法做到精确的函数容量匹配，则预注册参数量与墙钟时间匹配并报告对容量变化的敏感性。正向交互也可能反映滤波器对间隔配对的特异性过拟合而非可泛化的转移先验，因此在强化主张之前需要预注册的交互阈值与跨滚动窗口的复现。"}}]};
